%0A%22%D6jevind%20L%E5ng%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20skrev%20i%20melding%0Anews:4dZRa.310$41nospam@nospam.net...%0ARings%22%2C%0Atastes%0Aboring.%0A%0A%0AIt%20appears%20to%20me%20that%20the%20original%20poster%20requests%20subjective%20opinions%2C%0Awhereas%20the%20groups%20answers%20more%20commonly%20deals%20with%20objective%20statements.%0ATo%20provide%20my%20subjective%20vote:%20Yes%2C%20%22the%20Silmarillion%22%20is%20worth%20reading%20-%0Afor%20completeness.%0AAlthough%20the%20stories%20of%20%22the%20Silmarillion%22%20are%20grand%20enough%20by%20any%20measure%2C%0Athe%20style%20of%20writing%20is%20a%20very%20different%20one%20from%20both%20%22the%20Hobbit%22%20and%20%22the%0ALord%20of%20the%20Rings%22.%20I%20find%20it%20much%20duller%20than%20the%20work%20Tolkien%20published%0Awhile%20he%20was%20alive.%0A%0APerhaps%20on%20purpose%20Tolkien%20wrote%20%22the%20Silmarillion%22%20in%20a%20more%20saga-like%0Astyle.%20The%20narrator%20is%20quite%20distal%20with%20respect%20to%20the%20events%20and%20seems%0Amore%20occupied%20with%20a%20correct%20record%20rather%20than%20bringing%20the%20characters%20to%0Alife%20in%20a%20way%20that%20captures%20the%20imagination%20of%20the%20reader.%0AReading%20the%20Silmarillion%20however%20improved%20my%20understanding%20of%20%22the%20Lord%20of%0Athe%20Rings%22%20specially%20and%20Middle%20Earth%20and%20the%20writtings%20of%20Tolkien%20in%0Ageneral.%20For%20me%2C%20definetly%20worth%20the%20effort.%0A%0AMy%20recommendation%20to%20Karl-Peder%20will%20be%20that%20after%20taking%20on%0A%22Silmarillion%22%20-%20proceed%20to%20%22the%20Unfinished%20Tales%22.%20In%20that%20book%20parts%20of%0Asome%20of%20the%20tales%20which%20are%20related%20in%20%22the%20Silmarillion%22%20is%20present%20in%20a%0Amore%20novel-like%20style%2C%20more%20similar%20to%20what%20you%20find%20in%20%22the%20Lord%20of%20the%0ARings%22.%20My%20favourite%20is%20the%20tragic%20story%20of%20the%20Mormegil%2C%20which%20I%20find%20to%20be%0Avery%20well%20written.%20Another%20good%20one%20is%20%22Of%20Turgon%20and%20his%20coming%20to%0AGondolin%22.%20These%20two%20unfinished%20tales%20to%20some%20extent%20need%20the%20background%0Ainformation%20from%20%22the%20Silmarillion%22%20in%20order%20to%20work%20in%20you%20mind.%20The%0Apleasure%20of%20reading%20these%20two%20Unfinished%20Tales%20is%20alone%20worth%20the%20struggle%0Aof%20reading%20the%20Silmarillion.%0A%0AThomas%20Sperre%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
