%0A%22coyotes%20rand%20mair%20fheal%20greykitten%20tomys%20des%20anges%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%0Awrote%20in%20message%20news:41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0ABetter%20than%20that.%20Look%20again%20at%20the%20scene%20in%20Moria.%20The%20%27balrog%27%20is%0Aadvancing%20towards%20the%20bridge%20and%20Boromir%20blows%20the%20horn.%20It%20stops%20for%20a%0Amoment.%20Even%20the%20balrog%20is%20intimidated%2C%20if%20only%20for%20a%20moment.%20This%20is%0Adirectly%20from%20Norse%20mythology.%20The%20beginning%20of%20Ragnarok%20is%20described%20in%0Aexactly%20this%20way.%20The%20god%20Heimdall%20is%20standing%20guard%20at%20the%20end%20of%20Bifrost%0A%28the%20bridge%20linking%20the%20world%20of%20the%20gods%20to%20Middle-earth%2C%20erm%2C%20Middgard%20:%29%0Aand%20he%20sees%20Surtr%20approaching%20to%20attack.%20Surtr%20%28as%20all%20%27fire%20giants%27%29%20is%0Adescribed%20_exactly_%20like%20the%20%27balrog%27%20--%20a%20huge%20figure%20of%20flame%20and%20shadow.%0AHeimdall%20blows%20his%20horn%20Gjaller%20%28yes%2C%20%22Yeller%22%29%20and%20rouses%20the%20gods%20to%20come%0Aout%20and%20fight.%20And%20even%20Surtr%20pauses%20for%20a%20moment%20at%20the%20noise%20of%20Gjaller.%0ARagnarok%20results%20in%20the%20death%20of%20all%20the%20gods%2C%20of%20course%2C%20but%20Tolkien%20in%20his%0Ausual%20habit%20of%20reversing%20and%20re-arranging%20things%20has%20made%20the%20confrontation%0Ainto%20the%20%27fire%20giant%27%20trying%20to%20get%20OUT%20of%20the%20underworld%20rather%20than%20up%20to%0Athe%20world%20of%20the%20gods.%20The%20basic%20event%20is%20still%20recognizable%2C%20though.%0A%0ASo%20no%2C%20not%20a%20mere%20%22hero%27s%22%20horn%2C%20but%20a%20god%27s%20horn%21%20No%20wonder%20it%20could%20be%0Aheard%20100+%20miles%20away%21%20:%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
