%22Graham%20Lockwood%22%20wrote:%0A%0AHopeless%2C%0Ahis%0Awalk%0A%0AThe%20burly%20innkeeper%20stared%20at%20Gerard.%20%22Why%2C%20I%20must%20be%20going%20blind%2C%20master%21%22%0Ahe%20said.%2C%20%22Indeed%2C%20you%20aren%27t%20Nob%2C%20that%20good-for-nothing%20slowcoach%21%20I%20humbly%0Aapologize.%20I%20suppose%20y%27all%20-%20I%20mean%2C%20all%20you%20people%20-%20will%20be%20wanting%0Asupper%2C%20I%20don%27t%20doubt.%20As%20soon%20as%20may%20be.%20This%20way%20now%21%22%0A%20%20He%20led%20Gerard%2C%20Mesmeralda%20Moomintook%20and%20Walker%2C%20the%20Taixus%20ranger%2C%20into%0Athe%20inn%2C%20down%20a%20passage%2C%20and%20opened%20a%20door.%20%22Here%20is%20a%20nice%20little%20parlour%21%22%0Ahe%20said.%20%22I%20hope%20it%20will%20suit.%20Excuse%20me%20now.%20I%27m%20that%20busy.%20No%20time%20for%0Atalking.%20I%20must%20be%20trotting.%20It%27s%20hard%20work%20for%20two%20legs.%20but%20I%20don%27t%20get%0Athinner.%20I%27ll%20look%20in%20again%20later.%20If%20you%20want%20anything%2C%20ring%20the%20hand-bell%2C%0Aand%20Nob%20will%20come.%20If%20he%20don%27t%2C%20ring%20and%20shout%21%22%0A%20%20Off%20he%20went%20at%20last%2C%20and%20left%20them%20feeling%20rather%20breathless.%20He%20seemed%0Acapable%20of%20an%20endless%20stream%20of%20talk%2C%20however%20busy%20he%20might%20be.%20They%20found%0Athemselves%20in%20a%20small%20and%20cosy%20room.%20There%20was%20a%20bit%20of%20bright%20fire%20burning%0Aon%20the%20hearth%2C%20and%20in%20front%20of%20it%20were%20some%20low%20and%20comfortable%20chairs.%0AThere%20was%20a%20round%20table%2C%20already%20spread%20with%20a%20white%20cloth%2C%20and%20on%20it%20was%20a%0Alarge%20hand-bell.%0A%20%20However%2C%20this%20cosy%20spectacle%20did%20not%20seem%20to%20appeal%20to%20Mesmeralda.%20%22I%20want%0Ato%20know%20where%20Breckenridge%20is%21%22%20she%20said.%20%22Them%20varmints%20in%20the%20Valley%20o%27%0AFear%20cain%27t%20do%20him%20no%20harm%20nohow%2C%20but%20that%20theer%20harlot%20Rose%20Cotton%2C%20the%20one%0Athey%20calls%20%27the%20Red%20Rose%20of%20Taixus%27%2C%20is%20gunning%20for%20him%2C%20so%20I%20want%20to%20keep%0Amy%20eyes%20clapped%20on%20him.%20Now%20will%20you%20gentlemen%20help%20me%20find%20him%20or%20not%3F%22%0A%20%20Meanwhile%2C%20at%20the%20hostelry%20in%20the%20alternative%20universe%2C%20the%20de-tailed%20Two%0AGun%20Moomin%20fainted%20from%20the%20loss%20of%20blood%20and%20fell%20to%20the%20floor%20with%20a%20heavy%0Athud.%20Simultaneously%2C%20a%20death%20rattle%20was%20heard%20from%20Mr%20Beauchamp%2C%20the%0Achronicler%20of%20heroes%20of%20the%20West.%20The%20undead%20Foreign%20Legion%20Sergeant%20laughed%0Aand%20look%20at%20Little%20Bill%20and%20English%20Bob%2C%20who%20both%20seemed%20at%20a%20loss%20about%0Awhat%20to%20do.%0A%0A%D6jevind%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%22Jamie%20Armstrong%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0A%0AI%27m%20not%20sure%20it%27s%20appropriate%20to%20talk%20of%20%27the%20Dwarves%27%20in%20general%20terms.%0AAfter%20the%20First%20Age%2C%20the%20only%20Dwarves%20that%20we%20hear%20about%20in%20any%20sort%0Aof%20detail%20are%20Durin%27s%20Folk%2C%20and%20it%20is%20clear%20that%20any%20sort%20of%20multilateral%0Aaction%20was%20rare%20from%20the%20avowedly%20exceptional%20events%20of%20the%20Moria%0Awars.%20It%20is%20strongly%20implied%20that%20they%20all%20went%20their%20separate%20ways%20--%0Ato%20such%20an%20extent%20that%20some%20few%20Dwarves%20even%20fought%20for%20Sauron%20in%0Athe%20war%20of%20the%20Last%20Alliance.%20I%20see%20no%20reason%20to%20read%20the%20text%20any%20way%0Aother%20than%20the%20way%20it%20asks%20to%20be%20read:%20that%20Durin%27s%20Folk%20were%20keen%20to%0Aassert%20that%20%2Athey%2A%20were%20NOT%20beholden%20to%20or%20tricked%20by%20Sauron.%20There%0Ais%20certainly%20nothing%20to%20suggest%20that%20the%20other%20Houses%20did%20not%20tell%0Asimilar%20stories%20of%20%2Atheir%2A%20rings%2C%20but%20I%20doubt%20very%20much%20that%20one%20House%0Awould%20especially%20care%20about%20how%20the%20other%20Houses%20obtained%20their%0Arings%3B%20and%20furthermore%2C%20Durin%27s%20Folk%20were%20seemingly%20the%20most%0Astraightforwardly%20%27good%27%20of%20the%20Dwarves%20%28ie%2C%20the%20most%20aligned%20with%0Athose%20opposed%20to%20Sauron%29.%20It%20is%20strongly%20implied%20by%20the%20presence%20of%0ADwarves%20in%20Sauron%27s%20army%20that%20some%20at%20least%20of%20the%20other%20Houses%0Awere%20much%20less%20choosy.%0A%0AIn%20story-external%20terms%2C%20it%20seems%20more%20like%20an%20attempt%20to%20explain%20just%0Ahow%20Durin%27s%20heirs%20managed%20to%20obtain%20one%20of%20the%20Seven%20after%20sealing%20their%0Adoors%20and%20retreating%20underground%20until%20the%20Balrog%20stirred%20%28and%2C%20as%0Alater%20emerged%2C%20when%20they%20had%20themselves%20fought%20%2Aagainst%2A%20Sauron%20in%20this%0Awar%29.%0A--%0AMatthew%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
