%22teepee%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3C3f0dd27b$0$45180$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0AHi%2C%0A%20%20I%20was%20just%20having%20a%20reread%20recently%20and%20recall%20thinking%20along%20those%0Alines.%20I%20was%20disappointed%20that%20he%20was%20not%20in%20the%20movie%20so%20the%20issue%20of%0Ahis%20origin%20and%20relevance%20is%20on%20my%20mind%20often.%20My%20theory%20is%20that%20the%0Aonly%20actor%20that%20could%20do%20the%20character%20justice%20is%20Tom%20Waits%20and%20it%0Awould%20have%20been%20too%20distracting.%20To%20me%20the%20two%20Toms%20are%20the%20same%20guy.%0A%0A%0A
%22the%20softrat%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20skrev%20i%20en%20meddelelse%0Anews:41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0A%0A%20%20%20No.pe.%20%20The%20Elven%20languages%20of%20Aman%20did%20adopt%20some%20Valarin%20words%20-%0Asuitably%20changed%20to%20accomodate%20the%20phonetics%20of%20Elven%20language%3B%20pure%20Valarin%0Asounded%20distasteful%20to%20the%20Elves.%20%20It%20is%20the%20Mannish%20languages%20which%20derive%0Afrom%20Khuzdul%20%28which%20was%20devised%20by%20Aul%EB%2C%20designer%20of%20the%20Dwarves%29%20and%20Elvish%0A%28which%20they%20devised%20themselves%29%2C%20to%20a%20great%20degree.%0A%0AKirina.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%22the%20softrat%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0Amind%0A%0AI%20have%20no%20doubt%20that%20played%20a%20role%20too%2C%20particularly%20in%20the%20description%20of%0Athe%20Dead%20Marshes.%0A%0A%D6jevind%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%28I%20know%20it%27s%20been%20done%20before%2C%20but%20I%20couldn%27t%20resist.%29%0A%0A%0AThe%20Gold%20Ring%0Aby%20Raymond%20Chandler%0A%0AThere%20was%20an%20east%20wind%20blowing%20that%20night.%20%20It%20was%20one%20of%20those%20bitterly%20cold%0AEasterners%20that%20come%20down%20out%20of%20the%20Mountains%20of%20Shadow%20and%20freeze%20your%20beard%0Aand%20make%20your%20bones%20ache.%20%20On%20nights%20like%20that%20wise%20men%20lose%20their%20sense%20of%0Apurpose%2C%20and%20brave%20men%20look%20at%20their%20swords%20and%20think%20about%20throwing%20themselves%0Aon%20them.%20%20Anything%20can%20happen.%0A%0AShe%20had%20hair%20as%20dark%20as%20a%20nazgul%27s%20heart%2C%20and%20gray%20eyes%20that%20could%20have%20given%0Athe%20sea%20lessons%20in%20being%20vast%20and%20unfathomable.%20%20She%20was%20wearing%20a%20simple%0Ahomespun%20cloak%20that%20looked%20as%20wrong%20on%20her%20as%20a%20two-handed%20broadsword%20looks%20on%0Aa%20halfling.%20%20Her%20lips%20parted%20and%20in%20a%20voice%20like%20a%20maia%20she%20said%2C%20%22Aragorn%0AElfstone%3F%22%0A%0A%22That%27s%20what%20they%20call%20me%2C%22%20I%20said.%20%20%22Come%20in%20and%20have%20a%20seat%2C%20Miss%20.%20.%20.%20%3F%22%0A%0A%22Evenstar%2C%22%20she%20said%20as%20she%20swung%20shut%20the%20door%20behind%20her%20with%20the%20words%0AELFSTONE%20INVESTIGATIONS%20etched%20across%20the%20glass%20in%20faded%20gilt.%20%20%22Arwen%0AEvenstar.%22%0A%0AAs%20she%20seated%20herself%2C%20I%20asked%2C%20%22What%20can%20I%20do%20for%20you%2C%20Miss%20Evenstar%3F%22%0A%0A%22I%27m%20looking%20for%20a%20man%20named%20Mithrandir%2C%22%20she%20said.%20%20%22Mithrandir%20Grayhame.%20%20I%0Ahave%20reason%20to%20believe%20he%20might%20be%20here%20in%20Minas%20Tirith.%22%0A%0A%22I%20see%2C%22%20I%20said.%20%20%22And%20what%20was%20it%20made%20you%20come%20all%20the%20way%20here%20from%20Imladris%0Ajust%20to%20find%20this%20Grayhame%20guy%3F%22%0A%0AHer%20full%20lips%20pressed%20together%20into%20a%20thin%2C%20angry%20line.%20%20%22What%20makes%20you%20think%0AI%27m%20from%20Imladris%3F%22%0A%0A%22You%20hide%20it%20well%2C%22%20I%20told%20her%2C%20%22but%20your%20Sindarin%20has%20got%20that%20sibilance%20you%0Aonly%20get%20in%20Imladris.%20%20So%2C%20do%20you%20want%20to%20tell%20me%20about%20it%3F%22%0A%0AHer%20eyes%20smoldering%2C%20she%20said%2C%20%22Mr.%20Grayhame%20knows%20the%20whereabouts%20of%20a%20certain%0Avery%20valuable%20object.%20%20I%27d%20like%20to%20question%20him%20regarding%20its%20location.%22%20%20Now%0Athat%20she%20wasn%27t%20trying%20to%20hide%20it%2C%20her%20Imladris%20accent%20gave%20her%20words%20a%20hissing%0Aquality%20that%20would%20have%20made%20her%20sound%20angry%20even%20if%20she%20hadn%27t%20been.%0A%0A%22What%20sort%20of%20object%20are%20we%20talking%20about%3F%22%20I%20asked.%0A%0A%22That%27s%20none%20of%20your%20concern%2C%22%20she%20said%20in%20a%20voice%20like%20a%20Rohirrim%20branding%0Airon%20laying%20claim%20to%20a%20young%20calf.%0A%0A%22Oh%2C%20but%20it%20is%2C%20Miss%20Evenstar%2C%22%20I%20responded.%20%20%22There%20are%20certain%20objects%20which%2C%0Ain%20addition%20to%20being%20very%20valuable%2C%20are%20also%20very%20dangerous.%20%20I%27d%20like%20to%0Areassure%20myself%20that%20Mr.%20Grayhame%20doesn%27t%20have%20access%20to%20any%20dangerous%20valuable%0Aobjects.%22%0A%0AEvenstar%20glared%20at%20me%20for%20a%20moment%20before%20she%20said%2C%20%22It%27s%20a%20palantir%2C%20the%0Apalantir%20of%20Annuminas.%22%0A%0A%22There%20now%2C%22%20I%20said%20soothingly%2C%20%22was%20that%20so%20hard%3F%20%20All%20right%2C%20then%2C%20I%27ll%20take%0Athe%20case.%20%20I%20charge%20twelve%20crowns%20a%20day%2C%20plus%20expenses%2C%20with%20a%20fifty%20crown%0Aretainer.%22%0A%0AI%20didn%27t%20expect%20her%20to%20haggle%2C%20and%20I%20was%20right.%20%20Despite%20the%20homespun%20cloak%2C%20I%0Astrongly%20suspected%20that%20Miss%20Evenstar%20moved%20in%20social%20circles%20where%20haggling%0Aover%20money%20was%20considered%20undignified.%20%20She%20reached%20into%20a%20belt%20pouch%20and%0Awithdrew%20the%20fifty%20crowns%2C%20all%20of%20it%20freshly%20minted%20in%20Imladris%20gold%20with%20Lord%0AElrond%27s%20profile%20standing%20sharply%20out.%20%20I%20didn%27t%20bother%20biting%20any%20of%20it%20-%0Awhere%20Miss%20Evenstar%20was%20from%2C%20it%20was%20also%20considered%20undignified%20to%0Ashort-change%20a%20tradesman.%0A%0AMiss%20Evenstar%20left%20me%20an%20address%20in%20the%20city%20where%20she%20could%20be%20reached%2C%20then%0Arose%20from%20her%20seat%20and%20left%20my%20office%20without%20another%20word.%20%20When%20she%20was%20gone%2C%0AI%20leaned%20back%20in%20my%20chair%20and%20studied%20the%20ceiling%20while%20I%20thought.%0A%0AAlthough%20the%20case%20had%20its%20share%20of%20question%20runes%2C%20one%20thing%20was%20certain:%20Miss%0AEvenstar%20was%20lying.%20%20Whatever%20it%20was%20that%20Mithrandir%20Grayhame%20had%20stashed%20away%2C%0Ait%20sure%20as%20Mandos%20wasn%27t%20the%20palantir%20of%20Annuminas.%0A--%0AJohnny%20Pez%0ANewport%2C%20Rhode%20Island%0AJuly%202003%0A%0A%0A
%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0A%3C%3F%3E%0A%0ASo%20far%20as%20I%20know%20the%20elven%20%27cycles%20of%20life%27%20were%20never%20spelled%20out%20in%0Adetail.%20%20The%20only%20reference%20I%20know%20of%20is%3B%0A%0A%22Elves%20did%20not%20have%20beards%20until%20they%20entered%20their%20third%20cycle%20of%0Alife.%20%20Nerdanel%27s%20father%20was%20exceptional%2C%20being%20only%20early%20in%20his%0Asecond.%22%0AVT%20%2341%0A%0ANow%2C%20from%20this%20we%20might%20guess%20that%20the%20%27cycles%27%20were%3B%0A%0A1st:%20Childhood.%20%20About%20100%20years.%0A2nd:%20Adulthood.%20%20Several%20thousand%20years.%0A3rd:%20Aging.%20%20Until%20the%20end%20of%20Arda%3F%0A%0AHowever%2C%20that%20is%20only%20speculation.%20%20Galadriel%20might%20be%20early%20in%20the%0Athird%20cycle%20or%20there%20might%20be%20some%20aging%20even%20in%20the%202nd.%0A%0AI%20think%20you%20are%20probably%20correct...%20for%20instance%20there%20is%20no%0Aindication%20that%20Galadriel%20looked%20more%20%27aged%27%20than%20Arwen%2C%20but%20the%0A%27cycles%27%20are%20just%20guesswork.%0A%0A%0A
%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0A%0AWhen%20Gerard%2C%20Walker%20the%20Taixus%20Ranger%20and%20Mesmeralda%20Moomintook%20landed%20with%0Aa%20thump%20in%20front%20of%20the%20hotel%20clerk%27s%20desk%20at%20The%20Limping%20Nazg%FBl%2C%20the%20Undead%0AForeign%20Legion%20Sergeant%20looked%20at%20them%20and%20laughed%20an%20eViol%20laughter.%20The%0ABalrog%20clerk%20hesitated%3B%20Little%20Bill%20and%20English%20Bob%20whistled%20and%20cleaned%0Atheir%20fingernails%2C%20feigning%20insouciance.%20From%20the%20unconscious%20body%20of%20Two%0AGun%20Moomin%20-%20hey%2C%20who%20let%20this%20stampede%20of%20M%FBmaks%20into%20my%20room%3F%20They%20are%0Atrampling%20down%20everything%21%20Haalp%21%20Haalp%21%20HAALP%21%20Ha%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0ARichard%0Athe%0Aaction%0A%0A%22Nob%21%20You%20woolly-footed%20addlepate%21%20I%20have%20warned%20you%20about%20slipping%20on%20the%0Ahorse%20apples%20in%20the%20courtyard.%20Suppose%20you%20had%20hurt%20yourself%20really%20badly%21%20I%0Aneed%20your%20help%2C%20and%20I%20need%20Bob%20too%21%20Where%27s%20Bob%3F%20You%20don%27t%20know%3F%20Well%2C%20find%0Ahim%21%20Double%20sharp%21%20I%20haven%27t%20got%20six%20legs%2C%20nor%20six%20eyes%20either%21%20Tell%20Bob%0Athere%27s%20five%20ponies%20that%20have%20to%20be%20stabled.%20He%20must%20find%20room%20somehow.%22%0A%20%20All%20that%20Gerard%2C%20in%20his%20confused%20state%2C%20could%20think%20of%20was%20that%20he%20had%0Abeen%20accused%20of%20having%20woolly%20feet.%20Automatically%2C%20he%20looked%20down%20and%0Adiscovered%20that%20his%20shoes%20had%20disappeared%20somehow%2C%20and%20that%20his%20feet%20were%0Aindeed%20covered%20by%20thick%2C%20curly%20hair.%0A%0A%D6jevind%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0A%0ARealize%20that%20I%20had%20done%20the%20Undead%20Foreign%20Legion%20Sergeant%20an%20injustice.%20At%0Athe%20sight%20of%20this%20touching%20reconciliation%2C%20he%20wiped%20away%20a%20not%20unmanly%20tear%0Aand%20said:%20%22I%27m%20a%20hard%2C%20embittered%20non-person%2C%20but%20even%20I%20cannot%20separate%0Athose%20who%20have%20shown%20that%20they%20are%20the%20right%20stuff%21%20Bless%20you%21%20God%20bless%20us%0Aall%21%20Two%20Gun%2C%20I%27ll%20just%20go%20back%20to%20the%20Foreign%20Legion%20crypt%20and%20report%20you%0Aas%20missing%20in%20action%2C%20presumed%20alive.%22%0A%0A%D6jevind%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%41nospam@nospam.net%3Ewrote:%0A%0A%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0Abehind%0A%0ABeauchamp%2C%20the%20scribbler%20in%20snuff-coloured%20garb%2C%20who%20fell%20to%20the%20floor%2C%0Aclutching%20his%20midriff%20and%20moaning:%20%22Aaarghhh...%22%0A%20%20Little%20Bill%20looked%20at%20Nosferatu%20with%20shock%20and%20outrage%20in%20his%20eyes.%0A%20%20%22You%2C%20sir%2C%20are%20a%20coward%21%22%20he%20thundered.%20%22You%20hurt%20an%20unarmed%20man.%22%0A%0A%D6jevind%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%5BI%27ve%20posted%20this%20in%20addition%20to%20emailing%20it.%20%20I%20figured%20it%20was%20worth%0Aexplaining%20myself%20just%20a%20bit%20more%20to%20the%20group%2C%20and%20also%20worth%0Amentioning%20a%20%22less%20bad%22%20possible%20explanation%20for%20the%20publicity%20campaign%0Athat%20I%20thought%20of.%5D%0A%0AIn%20rec.arts.books.tolkien%2C%20you%20expounded:%0A%0AI%27m%20glad%20of%20that%2C%20anyway.%20:%29%20%20%28I%20_do_%20mean%20the%20best%2C%20really%20I%20do.%29%0A%0A%0AThe%20thing%20is%2C%20I%27m%20pretty%20convinced%20that%20your%20arrival%20on%20Usenet%20for%0Athat%20purpose%20was%20part%20of%20a%20coordinated%20effort.%20%20If%20you%20_aren%27t_%20the%0Asame%20person%20as%20%22rwarrior2%22%2C%20%22kings%22%2C%20and%20%22Jason%20McGerty%22%2C%20then%20it%0Aseems%20clear%20that%20you%20are%20associated%20with%20them%20in%20some%20way.%20%20It%0Astretches%20the%20bounds%20of%20credibility%20that%20Robert%20Stanek%20%28the%20fantasy%0Aauthor%29%20would%20not%20be%20mentioned%20on%20Usenet%20for%20almost%20a%20year%20%28not%20since%0Athe%20last%20round%20of%20accusations%20that%20he%20promoted%20himself%20deceptively%2C%20in%0Afact%29%20and%20then%20randomly%20have%20four%20fans%20appear%20for%20the%20first%20time%20and%0Astart%20posting%20about%20him%20together%20on%20several%20different%20groups%20within%20a%0Afew%20days%20of%20each%20other.%0A%0AThus%2C%20I%20conclude%20that%20you%20are%20associated%20with%20those%20other%20identities%0Ain%20some%20way%2C%20and%20that%20the%20group%20of%20you%20came%20to%20Usenet%20specifically%20to%0Amake%20it%20look%20like%20Stanek%20had%20a%20larger%20fan%20base%20than%20he%20actually%20does.%0AIf%20you%20_are_%20all%20Robert%20Stanek%20or%20if%20he%20%28or%20his%20agents%29%20arranged%20for%0Aall%20of%20you%20to%20do%20this%2C%20then%20I%20think%20he%27s%20advertizing%20in%20an%20unethical%0Amanner%20%28and%2C%20in%20the%20latter%20case%2C%20that%20you%20and%20the%20others%20were%20probably%0Aacting%20inappropriately%20by%20taking%20part%20in%20his%20plan%29.%0A%0AIf%20you%27re%20just%20some%20Stanek%20fan%20club%20and%20decided%20on%20your%20own%20to%20help%0Aout%20your%20favorite%20author%2C%20I%20am%20more%20sympathetic%2C%20but%20I%20still%20think%0Ayour%20methods%20are%20inappropriate.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20I%20think%20that%20you%20owe%20an%0Aapology%20not%20just%20to%20the%20groups%20that%20you%20tried%20to%20deceive%20but%20also%20to%0AStanek%20himself%2C%20who%20has%20only%20been%20hurt%20by%20your%20actions.%20%20%28It%20might%0Aeven%20be%20nice%20if%20he%20or%20his%20representatives%20came%20to%20the%20groups%20where%0Ayou%27ve%20posted%20and%20apologized%20on%20your%20behalf%2C%20actually%2C%20though%20it%0Aclearly%20wouldn%27t%20be%20their%20responsibility.%29%20%20We%20all%20make%20mistakes%2C%0Athough%2C%20so%20I%27m%20happy%20to%20forgive%20and%20forget%20if%20this%20was%20the%20case.%20:%29%0A%28Was%20it%3F%29%0A%0A%0AMy%20apologies%20for%20my%20suspicions%2C%20then.%20%20I%20remain%20very%20curious%2C%20however%2C%0Aabout%20how%20exactly%20you%20handsell%20_The%20Shaping%20of%20Middle-earth_%2C%20and%20why%0Ayou%20have%20chosen%20that%20book%20over%20something%20like%20_Unfinished%20Tales_%20%28or%0Afor%20that%20matter%2C%20why%20you%20recommend%20it%20before%20_Morgoth%27s%20Ring_%20and%20_The%0AWar%20of%20the%20Jewels_%29.%20%20Could%20you%20share%20your%20thoughts%20on%20the%20matter%3F%0A%28And%20if%20you%20do%2C%20I%27m%20sure%20the%20whole%20newsgroup%20would%20be%20interested:%20it%27s%0Aalways%20neat%20to%20see%20which%20aspects%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20different%0Apeople%20enjoy%2C%20and%20why.%29%0A%0A%0AAnd%20I%20don%27t%20think%20that%20anyone%20expects%20you%20to%20be%20one.%20:%29%20As%20someone%20who%0A_is_%20something%20of%20a%20Tolkien%20scholar%2C%20though%2C%20I%20think%20the%20best%20advice%20I%0Acan%20give%20you%20is%20to%20avoid%20recommending%20specific%20books%20in%20the%20%22History%0Aof%20Middle-earth%22%20series%20altogether%20until%20you%20become%20a%20bit%20more%20of%0Aone.%20:%29%20%20Readers%20who%20have%20only%20read%20through%20_The%20Silmarillion_%0Aprobably%20need%20some%20substantial%20explanation%20of%20what%20the%20HoMe%20books%0A_are_%20if%20they%20don%27t%20want%20an%20unpleasant%20surprise%2C%20and%20it%20takes%20someone%0Awho%20knows%20those%20books%20reasonably%20well%20to%20get%20them%20started%20in%20the%20right%0Aplace.%20%20%28_Unfinished%20Tales_%20is%20a%20much%20more%20gentle%20introduction%20to%20the%0Astyle%20of%20HoMe%2C%20I%20think%2C%20which%20is%20one%20of%20many%20reasons%20to%20recommend%20it%0Abefore%20any%20of%20the%20HoMe%20books.%29%0A%0AAnd%2C%20as%20I%20said%20in%20an%20earlier%20message%2C%20once%20your%20readers%20finish%20_The%0ASilmarillion_%20and%20_Unfinished%20Tales_%2C%20you%20might%20honestly%20think%20about%0Apointing%20them%20to%20my%20Custom%20Tolkien%20Book%20List%20%28at%0Ahttp:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Fbooks.html%29%2C%20which%20has%20gotten%20a%20fair%20bit%20of%0Apositive%20feedback%20and%20very%20few%20complaints%20that%20I%20can%20recall.%20%20I%20think%0Ait%20does%20a%20decent%20job%20of%20telling%20people%20what%20they%20are%20likely%20to%20enjoy.%0A%0A%0AI%27m%20sorry%20to%20hear%20that%2C%20and%20I%20hope%20that%20there%27s%20been%20no%20permanant%0Adamage%20done.%20:%29%20%20%28I%27m%20not%20quite%20sure%20what%20%22such%20thinking%22%20you%27re%0Areferring%20to%2C%20though.%29%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
%5BThis%20will%20probably%20be%20my%20last%20post%20in%20this%20branch%20of%20this%20thread%2C%20but%0AI%20figured%20I%27d%20wrap%20up%20a%20final%20loose%20end%20before%20closing%20the%20topic.%20%20Why%0Aam%20I%20bothering%20at%20all%3F%20%20As%20I%27ve%20said%20elsewhere%2C%20I%27m%20not%20fond%20of%0Adeliberate%20attempts%20at%20deception%2C%20and%20smearing%20someone%20else%27s%0Areputation%20based%20on%20false%20evidence%20certainly%20counts.%20%20The%20possibility%0Athat%20the%20smearer%20might%20have%20a%20monetary%20interest%20in%20what%20they%27re%20doing%0Adoesn%27t%20help%20matters%2C%20either.%20%20My%20apologies%20if%20my%20little%20%22truth%20in%0Aadvertising%22%20campaign%20here%20has%20bothered%20anyone.%5D%0A%0AQuoth%20%22Jason%20McGerty%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CMtYOa.19762$ye4.17015@sccrnsc01%3E:%0A%0AThe%20nice%20thing%20about%20using%20Google%20information%20in%20debates%20is%20that%20it%27s%0Apublicly%20accessible%20and%20can%20therefore%20be%20checked.%20%20Whomever%20%22raycun%22%0Ais%2C%20he%27s%20posted%20to%20rec.arts.sf.written%20and%2For%20rec.arts.sf.fandom%0Aalmost%20every%20month%20since%20August%202001.%20%20The%20one%20exception%20is%20a%20seven%0Amonth%20gap%20at%20the%20beginning%20of%202002%2C%20and%20his%20first%20post%20after%20that%20gap%0Acomments%20on%20his%20absence%20and%20gripes%20that%20someone%20is%20still%20posting%20ideas%0Athat%20he%20%22demolished%20a%20year%20ago%22.%20%20Sounds%20like%20a%20typical%20Usenet%20hiatus%0Ato%20me.%20:%29%20%20I%20see%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20that%20the%20owner%20of%20the%20address%0Achanged%20in%20that%20time%2C%20and%20I%20had%20the%20impression%20that%20hotmail%20account%0Anames%20were%20%22reserved%22%20for%20more%20than%20seven%20months%20in%20any%20case.%0A%0A%0AI%20for%20one%20appreciated%20being%20made%20aware%20of%20what%20seems%20to%20have%20been%20an%0Aattempt%20at%20dishonest%20advertising.%20%20I%20don%27t%20know%20if%20I%20would%20have%20done%0Athe%20same%20thing%20in%20his%20place%2C%20but%20I%20know%20that%20I%20might%20have%20fallen%20for%0Athe%20deception%20if%20it%20hadn%27t%20been%20for%20his%20warning%2C%20so%20I%20certainly%20thank%0Ahim%20for%20his%20trouble.%20%20What%20aspect%20of%20%22what%20he%27s%20doing%22%20is%20it%20that%20you%0Abelieve%20%22stinks%22%2C%20anyway%3F%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
%D6jevind%20L%E5ng%20said:%0A%0AMaybe%20he%20had%20just%20seen%20Disney%27s%20%22Lady%20and%20the%20Tramp%22%20too%20many%20times%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
%D6jevind%20L%E5ng%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AIglishm%EAk%20was%20a%20type%20of%20sign-language%20used%20by%20the%20Dwarves.%20It%27s%20talked%20about%0Ain%20_The%20War%20of%20the%20Jewels_%20which%20I%20haven%27t%20read%20so%20I%20can%27t%20really%20tell%20you%0Aany%20more%20than%20that.%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28jim%20deutch%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news%3A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%22the%20hobbits%20sat%20in%20shadow%20by%20the%20wayside.%20before%20long%20the%20elves%20came%0Adown%20the%20lane%20towards%20the%20valley.%20they%20passed%20slowly%2C%20and%20the%20hobbits%0Acould%20see%20the%20starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%20and%20in%20their%20eyes.%0Athey%20bore%20no%20lights%2C%20yet%20as%20they%20walked%20a%20shimmer%2C%20like%20the%20light%20of%0Athe%20moon%20above%20the%20rim%20of%20the%20hills%20before%20it%20rises%2C%20seemed%20to%20fall%0Aabout%20their%20feet.%20they%20were%20now%20silent%2C%20and%20as%20the%20last%20elf%20passed%20he%0Aturned%20and%20looked%20towards%20the%20hobbits%20and%20laughed.%20%22%0A-%20the%20fellowship%20of%20the%20ring%2C%20chapter%20iii%0Aa%20%22starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%22%20and%20%22shimmer%20like%20the%20light%20of%0Athe%20moon%22%20surrounding%20the%20elves%20sounds%20a%20little%20like%20the%20sub-lime%0Alight%20representing%20the%20influence%20of%20the%20holy%20spirit%20on%20saints%20in%0Areligious%20icons.%20the%20sub-lime%20light%20is%20also%20represented%20as%20a%20halo%0Awhen%20there%20thought%20to%20be%20a%20need%20for%20a%20source%20for%20the%20light.%0Athe%20thought%20of%20the%20high%20elves%20%28and%20not%20other%20elves%29%20being%20blonde%20comes%0Afrom%20mis%20remembering%20the%20%22starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%22%20as%20a%0Agolden%20glimmering.%20in%20a%20movie%20how%20would%20you%20represent%20hair%20with%20a%0Agolden%20glimmering%3F%20possibly%20by%20presenting%20the%20elves%20of%20light%20as%0Aplatinum%20blondes%20and%20others%20as%20not%20so%20blonde%20...%20so%20i%20found%20myself%0Awondering%20how%20did%20legolas%20come%20by%20the%20same%20golden%20glimmering%20as%0Agaladriel.%0Awe%20have%20a%20reference%20from%20another%20thread%20to%20the%20influence%20of%20living%20in%0Athe%20west%2C%20or%20of%20being%20indirectly%20affected%20through%20an%20artifact%20from%20the%0Awest%3A%0A%22important%20note%3A%20but%20elwing%2C%20
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Jim%20Deutch%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%22The%20hobbits%20sat%20in%20shadow%20by%20the%20wayside.%20Before%20long%20the%20Elves%20came%0Adown%20the%20lane%20towards%20the%20valley.%20They%20passed%20slowly%2C%20and%20the%20hobbits%0Acould%20see%20the%20starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%20and%20in%20their%20eyes.%0AThey%20bore%20no%20lights%2C%20yet%20as%20they%20walked%20a%20shimmer%2C%20like%20the%20light%20of%0Athe%20moon%20above%20the%20rim%20of%20the%20hills%20before%20it%20rises%2C%20seemed%20to%20fall%0Aabout%20their%20feet.%20They%20were%20now%20silent%2C%20and%20as%20the%20last%20Elf%20passed%20he%0Aturned%20and%20looked%20towards%20the%20hobbits%20and%20laughed.%20%22%0A%0A-%20The%20Fellowship%20of%20the%20Ring%2C%20Chapter%20III%0A%0AA%20%22starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%22%20and%20%22shimmer%20like%20the%20light%20of%0Athe%20moon%22%20surrounding%20the%20Elves%20sounds%20a%20little%20like%20the%20sub-lime%0Alight%20representing%20the%20influence%20of%20the%20holy%20spirit%20on%20saints%20in%0Areligious%20icons.%20%20The%20sub-lime%20light%20is%20also%20represented%20as%20a%20halo%0Awhen%20there%20thought%20to%20be%20a%20need%20for%20a%20source%20for%20the%20light.%0A%0AThe%20thought%20of%20the%20high%20elves%20%28and%20not%20other%20elves%29%20being%20blonde%20comes%0Afrom%20mis%20remembering%20the%20%22starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%22%20as%20a%0Agolden%20glimmering.%20%20In%20a%20movie%20how%20would%20you%20represent%20hair%20with%20a%0Agolden%20glimmering%3F%20%20Possibly%20by%20presenting%20the%20elves%20of%20light%20as%0Aplatinum%20blondes%20and%20others%20as%20not%20so%20blonde%20...%20so%20I%20found%20myself%0Awondering%20how%20did%20Legolas%20come%20by%20the%20same%20golden%20glimmering%20as%0AGaladriel.%0A%0AWe%20have%20a%20reference%20from%20another%20thread%20to%20the%20influence%20of%20living%20in%0Athe%20West%2C%20or%20of%20being%20indirectly%20affected%20through%20an%20artifact%20from%20the%0AWest:%0A%0A%22Important%20note:%20But%20Elwing%2C%20Earendil%2C%20and%20both%20of%20their%20sons%20were%20all%0Aexposed%20to%20the%20LIGHT%20of%20the%20Two%20Trees%20captured%20in%20the%20Silmaril.%20So%0Athey%20were%20all%20%27Caliquendi%27%20%28At%20least%20Elros%20was%20until%20he%20chose%0Amortality%29.%20A%20fair%20number%20of%20mortal%20Men%20must%20have%20also%20been%20exposed%20to%0Ait%20at%20this%20time%2C%20and%20it%20must%20have%20left%20it%27s%20mark%20on%20the%20Numenoreans.%0AJust%20a%20thought%20on%20something%20that%20few%20people%20seem%20to%20notice...%22%0A%0AHow%20would%20you%20go%20about%20representing%20%22understanding%2C%20power%2C%20and%0Anobility%22%20%20in%20a%20visual%20medium%3F%20%20Well%2C%20we%20know%20that%20%22understanding%2C%0Apower%2C%20and%20nobility%22%20%20need%20have%20no%20visual%20representation%20%28%22mark%22%29%20but%0Asometimes%20artists%20try%20to%20express%20these%20qualities%20of%20their%20subjects%0Avisually.%20%20Some%20attempts%20in%20this%20direction%20are%20presenting%20the%20subject%0Ain%20sub-lime%20light%20%28halos%29%20or%20by%20making%20the%20subject%20beautiful.%20%20To%0Aportray%20the%20reverse%20of%20these%20qualities%20the%20subject%20is%20presented%20in%0Adarkness%20or%20as%20ugly.%0A%0ATolkien%20used%20such%20devices%20constantly%2C%20with%20the%20notable%20exception%20of%0AFrodo%27s%20backhanded%20evaluation%20of%20Strider%27s%20looks%20%28Strider%20did%20not%0A%22look%20the%20fairer%20and%20feel%20the%20fouler%22%29.%20%20Thus%20my%20thinking%20that%20the%0AElves%20who%20returned%20from%20Valinor%20must%20have%20had%20the%20%22mark%22%20%28represented%0Avisually%29%20of%20having%20lived%20in%20the%20undying%20lands%2C%20a%20mark%20not%20shared%20by%0ALegolas.%0A%0AAnyhow%2C%20once%20again%2C%20I%27m%20presenting%20a%20movie%20inspired%20question%20from%20a%0Acasual%20fan%2C%20so%20sorry%20for%20my%20lack%20of%20a%20scholarly%20approach%20to%20the%0Amatter.%20%20So%20many%20posters%20here%20enjoy%20explaining%20Tolkien%20to%20the%20very%0Aleast%20detail%20so%20I%20reasoned%20that%20no%20one%20would%20be%20really%20put%20out%20by%20a%0Aquestion%20from%20a%20casual%20fan.%20%20I%20don%27t%20think%20it%20is%20one%20of%20those%20dreaded%0Afrequently%20asked%20questions.%0A%0A--Terry%0A%0A%0A
=%3E%3E%20The%20runes%20were%20cast%2C%20the%20portents%20thundered%20and%20then%20Brenda%20Selwyn%0A%20%20warbled%20on%20about%20%22LOTR%20on%20Banned%20Texts%20List%20at%20Hogwarts%22%20in%20a.f.h-p%20%3C%3C=%0A%0A%0AIt%20got%20a%20mention%20at%20one%20point%20on%20the%20actors%20commentary%20track%20for%20the%20SE%0ADVD:%20basically%20the%20other%20three%20hobbits%20were%20bagging%20Elijah%20Wood%20for%20having%0Athe%20sweatiest%20feet%20and%20needing%20to%20get%20his%20feet%20reapplied%20by%20lunchtime.%0A%0ATig%21%0A%0A%0A--%0AI%27ve%20seen%20things%20you%20newbies%20wouldn%27t%20believe.%20Advert-spammers%20aflame%20off%0Athe%20shoulder%20of%20rec.arts.sf.written.%20I%20watched%20Cancel%20posts%20glitter%20in%20the%0Aether%20near%20the%20waikato.ac.nz%20gateway.%20%20All%20those%20moments%20will%20be%20lost%20in%0Atime%20--%20like%20beers%20in%20the%20rain.%20%20Time%20to%20unsubscribe.%0A%0A%0A
A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ATolkien%20did%20it%20too.%20LotR%20was%20a%20sequel%20to%20The%20Hobbit.%20%3B%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%20wrote:%0A%0AThe%20sons%20of%20Feanor%20had%20pretty%20thoroughly%20splintered%20elven%20unity%0Aby%20that%20time.%20%20I%27m%20not%20sure%20any%20of%20the%20Elves%20thought%20that%0Aappeasing%20them%20would%20restore%20that.%20%20The%20argument%20in%20favor%20of%0Agiven%20the%20Silmaril%20to%20them%20was%20rightful%20ownership%20by%20inheritance.%0A%0AI%27m%20also%20not%20sure%20that%20keeping%20the%20Silmaril%20hurt%20the%20effort%20against%0AMorgoth.%20%20If%20anything%2C%20the%20taking%20of%20the%20Silmaril%20by%20Beren%20and%0ALuthien%20was%20the%20first%20indication%20in%20a%20long%20time%20that%20Morgoth%0Ahad%20weaknesses.%20%20It%20made%20sense%20for%20the%20house%20that%20performed%20that%0Afeat%20to%20keep%20the%20token.%20%20Unless%2C%20of%20course%2C%20you%27re%20thinking%20about%0Athe%20destruction%20of%20Elven%20unity%20being%20the%20deciding%20factor%20in%20the%0Awar%20against%20Morgoth.%0A%0ASo%20I%27m%20not%20convinced%20that%20giving%20the%20Silmaril%20to%20the%20sons%20of%0AFeanor%20would%20help%20either%20Elven%20unity%20or%20the%20war%20against%20Morgoth.%0AI%27d%20enjoy%20hearing%20explanations%20of%20why%20it%20would.%0A%0A--%0AGlenn%20Holliday%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%20wrote:%0A%0AWhy%3F%20I%20know%20he%20makes%20a%20lot%20of%20mistakes%20and%20is%20a%20tad%20arrogant%2C%20but%20he%0A%2Ais%2A%20a%20tragic%20hero:%20he%20can%27t%20help%20it%21%20It%27s%20always%20fate%20seeming%20to%20work%0Aagainst%20him.%20I%20find%20him%20a%20rather%20sympathetic%20character%20-%20he%20always%0A%2Atries%2A%20to%20make%20the%20right%20choice%2C%20but%20because%20of%20something%20he%20can%27t%0Apossibly%20know%20about%20it%20ends%20up%20working%20against%20him.%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%20wrote:%0A%0AWrong.%20Two%20words:%20Westernesse%20swords.%0A%0A%0AWrong.%20%20Way%20waay%20wrong.%20That%20%22pond%22%20was%20actually%20a%20rather%20wide%20%22lake%22%20-%0Athe%20Middle%20earth%27s%20biggest%20river%2C%20making%20a%20lake%20around%20a%20mountain%20%28yep%2C%0Athat%20island%20no%20man%20had%20ever%20set%20foot%20WAS%20a%20small%20mountain%29%20and%20falling%0Aon%20Middle%20earth%27s%20biggest%20waterfall.%0A%0AL.L.%0A--%0A%22We%20must.%20We%20can.%20We%20will%22.%0A%28Christopher%20Reeve%29%0A%0A%0A
A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%20wrote:%0AThat%20does%20rather%20depend%20on%20whether%20or%20not%20you%20believe%20the%20official%20story:%0A%0A%22According%20to%20Einhard%2C%20a%20member%20of%20Charles%27s%20court%2C%20who%20wrote%20a%20%27Vita%0Akaroli%20Magni%27%20or%20%27Life%20of%20Charles%20the%20Great%27%20in%20the%20820s%2C%20the%20king%0Adeclared%20that%20if%20he%20had%20known%20what%20was%20going%20to%20happen%20he%20would%20never%0Ahave%20entered%20the%20church%20that%20day.%20This%20is%20probably%20no%20more%20than%20a%0Areflection%20of%20the%20tradition%2C%20current%20since%20Antiquity%2C%20of%20the%20refusal%20of%0Apower.%20Prospective%20emperors%20and%20also%20bishops%20had%2C%20either%20in%20literary%0Atradition%20or%20in%20polite%20political%20behavious%2C%20to%20resist%20attempted%20to%20raise%0Athem%20to%20their%20new%20status.%20There%20are%20indications%20that%20the%20idea%20of%20an%0Aimperial%20coronation%20had%20been%20discussed%20in%20Charles%27s%20preence%20at%20least%0Asince%20he%20arrived%20in%20Rome%20in%20November%20800.%22%20%28Roger%20Collins%2C%20Early%0AMedieval%20Europe%2C%20p.272%29%0A%0AI%20think%20Collins%20is%20rightly%20sceptical%20of%20the%20idea%20that%20Charlemagne%20could%0Apossibly%20allowed%20himself%20to%20be%20maneuvered%20into%20the%20situation%20by%20the%0APapacy:%20it%20would%20have%20suited%20his%20own%20ends%20better%20to%20been%20seen%20to%20have%0Ataken%20on%20the%20role%20unwillingly.%20Remember%20that%20Einhard%20was%20writing%20what%20he%0Awas%20instructed%20to%20write%20by%20the%20Carolingians:%20he%20wasn%27t%20trying%20to%20write%0Aan%20%27objective%27%20history%20%28whatever%20that%20is%29%20as%20we%20would%20understand%20it%0Atoday.%20You%20can%20still%20see%20a%20ritualised%20form%20of%20the%20%27reluctance%27%20to%20take%0Apower%20whenever%20a%20new%20speaker%20is%20chosen%20for%20the%20House%20of%20Commons:%20he%20or%0Ashe%20must%20feign%20reluctance%2C%20and%20has%20to%20be%20led%20to%20the%20speaker%27s%20chair%20by%0Abackbenchers.%0A%0AThat%27s%20not%20to%20deny%20that%20the%20Papacy%20had%20been%20wanting%20to%20crown%20%2Asomeone%2A%20-%0Aanyone%20-%20whom%20it%20thought%20it%20could%20control%20for%20centuries.%20I%20just%20think%0Athat%20Charlemagne%20let%20the%20Pope%20play%20into%20his%20own%20hands.%20After%20all%2C%20as%20the%0Amost%20powerful%20man%20in%20Western%20Christendom%20Charlemagne%20could%20do%20as%20he%0Apleased:%20if%20he%20really%20didn%27t%20want%20the%20crown%20he%20could%20have%20quite%20easily%0Arefused%20it.%20I%20find%20the%20idea%20that%20Leo%20III%20managed%20to%20sneak%20up%20to%0ACharlemagne%20with%20the%20crown%20hidden%20behind%20his%20back%2C%20and%20then%20suddenly%0Awhipped%20it%20out%20and%20stuck%20it%20on%20Charles%27s%20head%20crying%20%22surprise%21%22%20hard%20to%0Abelieve%20:%29%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0AThanks%20:%29%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
A%20musical%20retelling%20of%20the%20heart%20of%20the%20Silmarillion%20with%20only%20a%20very%0Avery%20few%20artistic%20liberties.%20What%20do%20you%20all%20think%3F%0A%0AWAR%20OF%20WRATH%0Anarrator%20%28Sauron%29:%0AThe%20field%20is%20lost%2C%0AEverything%20is%20lost%0AThe%20black%20one%20has%20fallen%20from%20the%20sky%20and%20the%20towers%20in%20ruins%20lie%0AThe%20enemy%20is%20within%2C%20everywhere%0AAnd%20with%20him%20the%20light%2C%20soon%20they%20will%20be%20here%0AGo%20now%2C%20my%20lord%2C%20while%20there%20is%20time%0AThere%20are%20places%20below%0A%0A%28Morgoth%29:%0AAnd%20you%20know%20them%20too%0AI%20release%20thee%2C%20go%0AMy%20servant%20you%27ll%20be%20for%20all%20time%0A%0A%28Sauron%29:%0AAs%20you%20command%0AMy%20king%0A%0A%28Morgoth%29:%0AI%20had%20a%20part%20in%20everything%0ATwice%20I%20destroyed%20the%20light%20and%20twice%20I%20failed%0AI%20left%20ruin%20behind%20me%20when%20I%20returned%0ABut%20I%20also%20carried%20ruin%20with%20me%0AShe%2C%20the%20mistress%20of%20her%20own%20lust%0A%0A%0A%0AINTO%20THE%20STORM%0AGive%20it%20to%20me%0AI%20must%20have%20it%0APrecious%20treasure%0AI%20deserve%20it%0A%0Abridge:%0AWhere%20can%20I%20run%0AHow%20can%20I%20hide%0AThe%20Silmarils%0AGems%20of%20treelight%0ATheir%20life%20belongs%20to%20me%0AOh%20it%27s%20sweet%20how%20the%0ADarkness%20is%20floating%20around%0A%0Achorus:%0AWe%20are%20following%0AThe%20will%20of%20the%20one%0AThrough%20the%20dark%20age%0AAnd%20into%20the%20storm%0AAnd%20we%20are%20following%0AThe%20will%20of%20the%20one%0AThrough%20the%20dark%20age%0AAnd%20into%20the%20storm%0A%0A%0ABlackheart%20show%20me%0AWhat%20you%20hold%20in%20hand%0AI%20still%20hunger%20for%20more%0ARelease%20me%0AFrom%20my%20pain%0AGive%20it%20to%20me%0AHow%20I%20need%20it%0AHow%20I%20need%20it%0AHow%20I%20need%20it%0A%0Abridge%0A%0Achorus%0A%0AI%20did%20my%20part%0ANow%20it%27s%20your%20turn%0AAnd%20remember%0AWhat%20you%27ve%20promised%0A%0Abridge%0A%0Achorus%0A%0A%0ALAMMOTH%0ARoooooooooooaar%21%0A%0A%0ANIGHTFALL%0ANo%20sign%20of%20life%20did%20flicker%0AIn%20floods%20of%20tears%20she%20cried%0A%22All%20hope%27s%20lost%20it%20can%27t%20be%20undone%0AThey%27re%20wasted%20and%20gone%22%0A%0A%22Save%20me%20your%20speeches%0AI%20know%20%28They%20blinded%20us%20all%29%0AWhat%20you%20want%0AYou%20will%20take%20it%20away%20from%20me%0ATake%20it%20and%20I%20know%20for%20sure%0AThe%20light%20she%20once%20brought%20in%0AIs%20gone%20forevermore%22%0A%0ALike%20sorrowful%20seaguls%20they%20sang%0A%22%28We%27re%29%20lost%20in%20the%20deep%20shades%0AThe%20misty%20cloud%20brought%0A%28A%20wailing%20when%20beauty%20was%20gone%0ACome%20take%20a%20look%20at%20the%20sky%29%0AMonstrous%20it%20covered%20the%20shore%0AFearful%20into%20the%20unknown%22%0AQuietly%20it%20crept%20in%20new%20horror%0AInsanity%20reigned%0AAnd%20spilled%20the%20first%20blood%0AWhen%20the%20old%20king%20was%20slain%0A%0Achorus:%0ANightfall%0AQuietly%20crept%20in%20and%20changed%20us%20all%0ANightfall%0AQuietly%20crept%20in%20and%20changed%20us%20all%0ANightfall%0AImmortal%20land%20lies%20down%20in%20agony%0A%0A%22How%20long%20shall%20we%0AMourn%20in%20the%20dark%0Athe%20bliss%20and%20the%20beauty%0AWill%20not%20return%0ASay%20farewell%20to%20sadness%20and%20grief%0AThough%20long%20and%20hard%20the%20road%20may%20be%22%0ABut%20even%20in%20silence%20I%20heard%20the%20words%0A%22An%20oath%20we%20shall%20swear%0ABy%20the%20name%20of%20the%20one%0AUntil%20the%20world%27s%20end%0AIt%20can%27t%20be%20broken%22%0A%0AJust%20wondering%20how%0AI%20can%20still%20hear%20these%20voices%20inside%0A%0AThe%20doom%20of%20the%20Noldor%20drew%20near%0A%0AThe%20words%20of%20a%20banished%20king%0A%22I%20swear%20revenge%21%22%0AFilled%20with%20anger%20aflamed%20our%20hearts%0AFull%20of%20hate%20full%20of%20pride%0AWe%20screamed%20for%20revenge%0A%0Achorus%0A%0A%22Vala%20he%20is%20that%27s%20what%20you%20said%0AThen%20your%20oath%27s%20been%20sworn%20in%20vain%0A%28But%29%20freely%20you%20came%20and%0AYou%20freely%20shall%20depart%0A%28So%29%20never%20trust%20the%20northern%20winds%0ANever%20turn%20your%20back%20on%20friends%22%0A%0A%22Oh%20I%27m%20heir%20of%20the%20high%20lord%21%22%0A%22You%20better%20don%27t%20trust%20him%22%0AThe%20enemy%20of%20mine%0AIsn%27t%20he%20of%20your%20kind%20and%0AFinally%20you%20may%20follow%20me%0AFarewell%0AHe%20said%0A%0Achorus%0A%0ABack%20to%20where%20it%20all%20began%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0ATHE%20MINSTREL%0ASo%20I%20stand%20still%0AIn%20front%20of%20the%20crowd%0AExcited%20faces%0AWhat%20will%20be%20next%3F%0AI%20still%20don%27t%20have%20a%20clue%0A%0A%0A%0A%0ATHE%20CURSE%20OF%20FEANOR%0ATaken%20the%20long%20way%0ADark%20realms%20I%20went%20through%0AI%20arrived%0AMy%20vision%27s%20so%20clear%0AIn%20anger%20and%20pain%0AI%20left%20deep%20wounds%20behind%0ABut%20I%20arrived%0ATruth%20might%20be%20changed%20by%20victory%0A%0ABeyond%20the%20void%20but%20deep%20within%20me%0AA%20swamp%20of%20filth%20exists%0AA%20lake%20it%20was%20of%20crystal%20beauty%0ABut%20Arda%27s%20spring%20went%20by%0AI%27ve%20heard%20the%20warning%0AWell%20curse%20my%20name%0AI%27ll%20keep%20on%20laughing%0ANo%20regret%0ANo%20regret%0A%0Achorus%20%281%29:%0ADon%27t%20fear%20the%20eyes%20of%20the%20dark%20lord%0AMorgoth%20I%20cried%0AAll%20hope%20is%20gone%20but%20I%20swear%20revenge%0AHear%20my%20oath%0AI%20will%20take%20part%20in%20your%20damned%20fate%0A%0AI%20will%20always%20remember%20their%20cries%0ALike%20a%20shadow%20which%20covers%20the%20light%0AI%20will%20always%20remember%20the%20time%0ABut%20it%27s%20past%0AI%20cannot%20turn%20back%20the%20time%0A%28I%29%20don%27t%20look%20back%0AThere%27s%20still%20smoke%20near%20the%20shore%0ABut%20I%20arrived%0ARevenge%20be%20mine%0A%0Achorus%20%282%29:%0AI%20will%20take%20part%20in%20your%20damned%20fate%0AMorgoth%20I%20cried%0AIt%27s%20my%20oath%0ASo%20don%27t%20fear%20the%20eyes%0AOf%20the%20dark%20lord%0A%0ASoon%20you%20will%20be%20free%0ASet%20your%20spirit%20free%0A%22Suddenly%20I%20realized%0AThe%20prophecies%0AI%27ve%20never%20believed%20in%0AMy%20deeds%20were%20wrong%0AI%27ve%20stained%20the%20land%0AAnd%20slain%20my%20kin%0A%28Burning%20Soul%29%0AThere%27s%20no%20release%20from%20my%20sins%0AIt%20hurts%0ATHE%20CURSE%20OF%20F%CBANOR%20RUNS%20LONG%0ATime%20and%20only%20time%20will%20tell%20us%0ATell:%20was%20I%20right%20or%20wrong%3F%0AWhen%20anger%20breaks%20through%0AI%27ll%20leave%20mercy%20behind%22%0A%0Achorus%20%282%29%0A%0AI%20will%20always%20remember%20their%20cries%0ALike%20a%20shadow%20they%27ll%20cover%20my%20life%0ABut%20I%27ll%20also%20remember%20mine%0A%28And%29%20after%20all%20I%27m%20still%20alive%0A%0A%0A%0A%0ACAPTURED%0Anarrator%20%28Morgoth%29:%0AYou%20are%20now%20my%20guest%2C%20forever%0A%0A%0A%0A%0ABLOOD%20TEARS%0AWelcome%20to%20my%20realm%0AWe%20are%20both%20condemned%20to%20live%0AIt%27s%20a%20dark%20fate%0A%28I%20can%20hear%20your%20calls%0AI%20can%20hear%20your%20calls%29%0AThe%20eternal%20life%0A%0AI%20see%20it%20still%20burns%0AEach%20night%20I%20cry%20in%20pain%0A%0AAlive%0AThough%20the%20end%20appears%20my%20friend%0A%0Achorus:%0AAnd%20blood%20tears%20I%20cry%0AYou%27ve%20searched%20and%20you%27ve%20found%0ACut%20off%20your%20old%20friends%20hand%0A%0AMy%20mind%27s%0AIn%20frozen%20dreams%0AThe%20rotten%20flesh%0AOf%20bitter%20lies%0AWelcome%20to%20where%20time%20stands%20still%0ANoone%20leaves%20and%20noone%20ever%20will%0A%0ACan%27t%20hold%20it%0AIt%20burns%0AEach%20night%20I%20cry%20in%20pain%0A%0Achorus:%0AAnd%20blood%20tears%20I%20cry%0AEndless%20grief%20remained%20inside%0AAnd%20blood%20tears%20I%20cry%0AEndless%20grief%20remained%20inside%0A%0AIt%20seems%20so%20clearly%0ABent%20the%20bow%0ACause%20life%20in%20me%20is%20gone%0AAnd%20a%20cruel%20wind%27s%20blowing%20cold%0AAnd%20a%20cruel%20wind%27s%20blowing%20cold%0AIn%20blame%0A%0AAnd%20life%20it%20shall%20wane%0AEach%20night%20I%20cry%20in%20pain%0A%0Achorus:%0AAnd%20blood%20tears%20I%20cry%0AEndless%20grief%20remained%20inside%0ACut%20off%20your%20old%20friends%20hand%0A%0A%0A%0AMIRROR%20MIRROR%0AFar%2C%20far%20beyond%20the%20island%0AWe%20dwelt%20in%20shades%20of%20twilight%0AThrough%20dread%20and%20weary%20days%0AThrough%20grief%20and%20endless%20pain%0A%0AIt%20lies%20unknown%0AThe%20land%20of%20mine%0AA%20hidden%20gate%0ATo%20save%20us%20from%20the%20shadow%20fall%0AThe%20lord%20of%20water%20spoke%0AIn%20the%20silence%0AWords%20of%20wisdom%0AI%27ve%20seen%20the%20end%20of%20all%0ABe%20aware%20the%20storm%20gets%20closer%0A%0Achorus%20%281%29:%0AMirror%20Mirror%20on%20the%20wall%0ATrue%20hope%20lies%20beyond%20the%20coast%0AYou%27re%20a%20damned%20kind%20can%27t%20you%20see%0AThat%20the%20winds%20will%20change%0AMirror%20Mirror%20on%20the%20wall%0ATrue%20hope%20lies%20beyo
AC%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AActually%20I%20find%20most%20of%20Book%20Four%20pretty%20trip-like%2C%20except%20for%20the%0AIthilien%20part%20maybe%20%28but%20that%20sounds%20like%20a%20pleasant%20sort%20of%20trip%0Asometimes%20%3B-%29.%20The%20Mordor%20chapters%20of%20Book%20Six%20sound%20much%20saner%20and%0Amore%20realistic%20%28however%20you%20define%20that%29%2C%20even%20though%20they%20take%20place%0Awithin%20Mordor%20itself.%0A%0A%0A
AC%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AErrrr....%20irk%3F%0A%0AOk%2C%20I%20%3Ethink%3C%20you%20are%20saying%20that%20Galadriel%20was%20born%20in%20the%20light%20of%0Athe%20two%20trees%20%28she%20was%29%2C%20though%20the%20structure%20makes%20it%20seem%20like%20this%0Astatement%20applies%20to%20Elrond%20%28who%20wasn%27t%29.%20%20However%2C%20as%20I%27m%20sure%20you%0Aactually%20know%2C%20Galadriel%20wasn%27t%20Elrond%27s%20mother...%20unless%20you%20count%0A%27mother%20in%20LAW%27%20since%20he%20married%20her%20daughter%20Celebrian.%20%20Elrond%27s%0Aactual%20mother%20was%20Elwing...%20who%20also%20was%20not%20born%20in%20the%20light%20of%20the%0ATwo%20Trees.%0A%0A%0A
AC%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0AYet%20the%20high%20elves%2C%20those%20who%20had%20lived%20in%20the%20undying%20lands%2C%20had%20a%0Asort%20of%20a%20halo:%0A%0A&%2312288%3B&%2312288%3B%22The%20hobbits%20sat%20in%20shadow%20by%20the%20wayside.%20Before%20long%0Athe%20Elves%20came%20down%20the%20lane%20towards%20the%20valley.%20They%20passed%20slowly%2C%0Aand%20the%20hobbits%20could%20see%20the%20starlight%20glimmering%20on%20their%20hair%20and%0Ain%20their%20eyes.%20They%20bore%20no%20lights%2C%20yet%20as%20they%20walked%20a%20shimmer%2C%20like%0Athe%20light%20of%20the%20moon%20above%20the%20rim%20of%20the%20hills%20before%20it%20rises%2C%0Aseemed%20to%20fall%20about%20their%20feet.%20They%20were%20now%20silent%2C%20and%20as%20the%20last%0AElf%20passed%20he%20turned%20and%20looked%20towards%20the%20hobbits%20and%20laughed.%20%22%0A%0A-%20J.R.R.%20Tolkien%2C%20The%20Fellowship%20of%20the%20Ring%2C%20Chapter%20III%0A%0AWhere%20did%20this%20shimmer%20come%20from%3F%20%20I%20thought%20it%20was%20an%20effect%20of%0Aliving%20in%20proximity%20of%20the%20two%20trees.%0A%0AWas%20it%20rather%20the%20result%20of%20eye%20makeup%20and%20hair%20products%3F%0A%0A--Terry%0A%0A%0A
AC%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%20On%202%20Jul%202003%2003:30:04%20-0700%2C%0A:%20Conrad%20Dunkerson%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%3E%20Johanna%20Katariina%20Rinne%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3Cbdttu0$rtr$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%3E%20In%20the%20Hobbit%20it%20is%20said%20that%20some%20dwarves%20had%20sometimes%20made%20alliances%20with%0A:%3E%3E%20orcs%20%28though%20never%20Thorin%27s%20people%29.%20So%20it%20is%20originally%20been%20J.R.R.%27s%20own%0A:%3E%3E%20idea.%20Don%27t%20know%20if%20he%20abandoned%20it%20himself%20at%20some%20point.%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%20The%20Dwarves%20started%20out%20as%20creatures%20of%20Morgoth%20like%20the%20Orcs%2C%20but%0A:%3E%20then%20slowly%20improved%20over%20time.%20%20They%20also%20got%20a%20considerable%20boost%20in%0A:%3E%20%27decency%27%20from%20%27The%20Hobbit%27...%20where%20the%20Dwarves%20were%20originally%20based%0A:%3E%20more%20on%20Grimm%27s%20fairy%20tales%20than%20Tolkien%27s%20own%20earlier%20Dwarves.%0A%0A:%20I%20don%27t%20recall%20Dwarves%20being%20Morgoth%27s%20creatures.%20%20In%20LT%2C%20they%20were%20an%0A:%20amoral%20bunch%20who%20traded%20with%20both%20sides.%20%20I%20believe%2C%20at%20that%20stage%2C%20Tolkien%0A:%20wrote%20nothing%20of%20their%20origins%2C%20but%20considering%20their%20behavior%2C%20I%20can%27t%0A:%20imagine%20that%20the%20notion%20that%20they%20were%20creations%20of%20Aule%20had%20arisen%20yet.%0A%0AMy%20first%20thought%20too%20was%20that%20they%20originally%20were%20creatures%20of%20Morgoth%2C%0Abut%20I%20cannot%20find%20such%20a%20reference.%20%20From%20%22The%20Nauglafring%22%20we%20have%0A%09%22The%20Nauglath%20are%20a%20strange%20race%20and%20one%20know%20surely%20whence%20they%0A%09%20be%3B%20and%20they%20serve%20not%20Meklo%20nor%20Manwe%20and%20reck%20not%20for%20Elf%20or%20Man%2C%0A%09%20and%20some%20say%20that%20they%20have%20not%20heard%20of%20Illuvatar%2C%20or%20hearing%0A%09%20disbelieve.%22%0AIn%20any%20case%2C%20the%20Dwarves%20did%20get%20better%20during%20the%20evolution%20of%0ATolkien%27s%20writings.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A
AC%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%20On%20Sat%2C%2012%20Jul%202003%2009:58:15%20-0700%2C%0A:%20coyotes%20morgan%20mair%20fheal%20greykitten%20tomys%20des%20anges%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%20its%20conceivable%20lorien%20and%20perhaps%20some%20companies%20from%20thranduil%20went%20there%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%20it%20could%20explain%20the%20elvenking%20suspicion%20when%20bilbo%20and%20company%0A:%3E%20assaulted%20them%0A%0A:%20I%20had%20always%20assumed%20that%20it%20was%20more%20of%20a%20show%20of%20power.%20%20Galadriel%2C%0A:%20Saruman%2C%20Gandalf%20and%20Elrond%20%28and%20whoever%20else%20was%20on%20the%20council%2C%20likely%0A:%20some%20Noldor%20likely%20Glorifindel%29%20were%20pretty%20powerful%20beings.%20%20However%2C%0A:%20Sauron%27s%20retreat%20was%20preplanned%20and%20feigned%2C%20so%20whatever%20means%20were%20used%20to%0A:%20evict%20him%2C%20it%20was%20too%20late%20for%20any%20meaningful%20injury%20to%20Sauron%20or%20his%20plans.%0A%0AYou%20also%20have%20to%20take%20into%20account%20what%20Gandalf%20says%20about%20the%20incident.%0A%20%22But%20Saruman%20has%20long%20studied%20the%20arts%20of%20the%20Enemy%20himself%2C%20and%0A%20%20thus%20we%20have%20often%20been%20able%20to%20forestall%20him.%20%20It%20was%20by%20the%0A%20%20devices%20of%20Saruman%20that%20we%20drove%20him%20from%20Dol%20Goldur.%22%0ADevices%20has%20many%20meanings%2C%20so%20this%20really%20does%20not%20tell%20us%20anything%0Aspecific%2C%20other%20than%20Saruman%20was%20behind%20their%20%22success%22%20at%20Dol%20Guldor.%0ASo%20even%20if%20the%20Elves%20supplied%20armies%2C%20that%20was%20not%20the%20reason%0Afor%20their%20victory.%0A%0ATolkien%20rarely%20describes%20battles%20between%20beings%20of%20power%20in%0Aany%20detail.%20%20The%20one%20example%20I%20can%20think%20of%20is%20Finrod%20and%20Sauron%2C%0Aand%20in%20that%20battle%20they%20sang%20songs.%20%20Maybe%20the%20devices%20of%20Saruman%20were%0Aa%20vocoder%20and%20a%20wawa%20pedal.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A
AC%20in%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20scripsit:%0A%0AAre%20you%20talking%20about%20the%20tale%20of%20the%20Faithful%20Stone%3F%0A%0AHere%27s%20the%20plot:%20Aghan%20and%20Barach%2C%20two%20Dr%FAedain%2C%20are%20great%0Afriends.%20Aghan%20protects%20Barach%27s%20family%20from%20Orc%20ambushes.%20One%20day%2C%20he%0Ahas%20to%20go%20to%20help%20his%20own%20kin.%20He%20leaves%20Barach%20a%20%27watch-stone%27%20%28a%0Astatue%20of%20himself%20intended%20to%20frighten%20Orcs%2C%20who%20believe%20them%20to%20have%0Amagical%20power%29.%20One%20night%2C%20Orcs%20attack%20Barach%27s%20house%2C%20but%20they%20are%0Adriven%20away%20by%20a%20mysterious%20Dr%FBg.%20When%20Aghan%20comes%20back%2C%20he%20finds%20that%0Athe%20watch-stone%20has%20killed%20Orcs%20and%20has%20been%20hurt.%20Aghan%20himself%20has%0Ahis%20legs%20bandaged%2C%20and%20he%20explains%20to%20Barach:%20%22Alas%21%20If%20some%20power%0Apasses%20from%20you%20to%20a%20thing%20that%20you%20have%20made%2C%20then%20you%20must%20take%20a%0Ashare%20in%20its%20hurts.%22%0A%0AThe%20tale%20is%20one%20told%20by%20the%20Haladin:%20%22though%20they%20held%20the%20Dr%FAedain%20in%0Alove%20and%20trust%2C%20many%20of%20the%20Folk%20of%20Haleth%20believed%20that%20they%0Apossessed%20uncanny%20and%20magical%20powers%3B%20and%20among%20their%20tales%20of%20marvels%0Athere%20were%20several%20that%20told%20of%20such%20things.%22%0A%0A--%0AMarie-Lan%20Nguyen%0A++%3F%3F%3F%3F%3F++%20Out%20of%20Cheese%20Error.%20Redo%20From%20Start.%0A%28Pratchett%2C%20_Interesting%20Times_%29%0A%3Chttp:%2F%2Fwww.pip-pip.org%2F%3E%0A%0A%0A
AC%20said:%0A%0AOily%20water%20is%20%2Ahealthy%2A%3F%21%3F%21%3F%21%0A%0ANot%20lethal%2C%20perhaps%2C%20but%20I%20don%27t%20know%20if%20I%20would%20call%20it%20healthy%20per%20se...%0A%3B%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
