Bill%20O%27Meally%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ANope.%20No%20improvement%20at%20all...%0A%0A%0AWell%2C%20%22Grimalkin%22%20could%20be%20pronounced%20%22Grimalkeen%22...%20I%20suppose...%0A%0ABut%20the%20thing%20is%20that%20it%20kinda-sorta%20rhymes.%20Tolkien%2FGimalkin.%20Grimm%2Fhim.%0ABut%20kinda-sorta%20rhymes%20are%20worse%20than%20no%20rhymes%20at%20all%20IMO.%0A%0ABlech.%20Good%20think%20he%20improved%20a%20bit%20in%20some%20of%20his%20other%20poetry...%0A%0ABilbo%20Baggins%0AHad%20a%20box%20with%20a%20mithril%20coat%20in%0AAnd%20also%20a%20sword%20named%20Sting%0AAnd%20lots%20of%20other%20things.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Bill%20O%27Meally%20wrote:%0A%0ADepends%20on%20how%20you%20read%20it%20%28oh%20look%2C%20%22Barrow%20blades%22%20are%20back%20on%20the%0Atopic%20again%21%29.%20I%20think%20assuming%20that%20the%20%22spells%22%20referred%20to%20are%20meant%0Ato%20be%20literally%20taken%20as%20anti-Nazgul%20magic%20is%20not%20what%20Tolkien%20intended.%0A%0APersonally%20I%20agree%20with%20the%20Tsar%27s%20take%20on%20men%20and%20magic%2C%20based%20on%20a%0Areference%20by%20Tolkien%20in%20Letters:%0A%0A%22Anyway%2C%20a%20difference%20in%20the%20use%20of%20%27magic%27%20in%20this%20story%20is%20that%20it%20it%0Anot%20to%20be%20come%20by%20by%20%27lore%27%20or%20spells%3B%20but%20is%20an%20inherent%20power%20not%0Apossessed%20or%20attainable%20by%20Men%20as%20such.%20Aragorn%27s%20%27healing%27%20might%20be%0Aregarded%20as%20%27magical%27%2C%20or%20at%20least%20a%20blend%20of%20magic%20with%20pharmacy%20and%0A%27hypnotic%27%20processes.%20But%20it%20is%20%28in%20theory%29%20reported%20by%20hobbits%20who%20have%0Avery%20little%20notions%20of%20philosophy%20science%3B%20%20while%20A.%20%5BAragorn%5D%20is%20not%20a%0Apure%20man%2C%20but%20at%20long%20remove%20one%20of%20the%20%27children%20of%20L%FAthien%27.%22%0A%28Letters%2C%20%23155%29%0A%0AIn%20the%20margin%20Tolkien%20had%20written:%0A%0A%22But%20the%20N%FAmen%F3reans%20used%20%27spells%27%20in%20making%20swords%3F%22%0A%0A%28Letters%2C%20%23155%29%0A%0ABut%20there%27s%20lots%20of%20dispute%20about%20the%20interpretation%20and%20validity%20of%20the%0Aparagraph%20and%20the%20footnote%20%28it%20was%20only%20part%20of%20a%20draft%2C%20and%20all%20of%20it%0Awas%20excluded%20from%20the%20finished%20article%29.%20For%20me%20it%20seems%20clear%20that%0ATolkien%20wasn%27t%20comfortable%20with%20the%20idea%20of%20men%20being%20able%20to%20do%20magic:%0Athe%20letter%20speaks%20of%20a%20confusion%20within%20himself%2C%20and%20an%20uncertainty%0Aabout%20what%20was%20correct%20and%20what%20was%20not.%20It%27s%20a%20shame%20he%20never%20fully%0Adeveloped%20that%20line%20of%20thought%20somewhere%20else%2C%20but%20at%20the%20same%20time%2C%20it%0Adoes%20leave%20the%20issue%20open%20for%20perfectly%20valid%20yet%20opposing%20interpretations.%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Bill%20O%27Meally%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20can%2C%20but%20not%20until%20later%20tonight.%20%20Don%27t%20have%20the%20book%20with%20me%20right%0Anow.%0A%0A--%0AMichael%20Martin%0A%22It%27s%20a%20fool%20who%20looks%20for%20logic%20in%20the%20chambers%20of%20the%20human%20heart.%22%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
