Conrad%20Dunkerson%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ACubic%20zirconium.%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AWell%2C%20to%20be%20fair%20to%20the%20movie%20makers%2C%20%22real%22%20hobbit%20feet%20are%20quite%20a%20bit%0Ahairier%20on%20top%20and%20tougher%20on%20bottom%20than%20normal%20human%20feet.%20So%20they%20really%0Adid%20need%20a%20full-foot%20prosthetic%20for%20the%20actors.%20The%20top%20was%20hairy%20and%20the%0Abottom%20thicker%20to%20protect%20their%20poor%20wittle%20feet%20as%20they%20ran%20around%20New%0AZealand.%20And%20the%20adding%20of%20the%20prosthetic%20neccesarily%20enlarged%20their%20feet.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%20quotes%7D%0A%0AIndeed.%20Why%20waste%20good%20meat%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%0A%0ALook%20at%20how%20much%20a%20lowly%20comma%20can%20do:%0A%0A%20%3E%3E%20...Elrond%2C%20son%20of%20Earendil%2C%20and%20Galadriel%2C%20who%20was%20born%0A%20%3E%3E%20in%20the%20light%20of%20the%20Two%20Trees%20of%20Aman.%0A%0ARegards%2C%0A%0A%0A--%0AGonzalo%20Diethelm%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%20%3E%20WHY%20did%20Faramir%20hear%20the%20horn%3F%20%20Was%20it%20just%20a%20%27daydream%27%20or%20his%0A%20%3E%20imagination%2C%20that%20just%20happened%20to%20coincide%20with%20the%20time%20the%20horn%0A%20%3E%20was%20being%20blown%3F%20%20If%20Faramir%20actually%20%27heard%27%20that%20horn%20because%0A%20%3E%20Boromir%20was%20blowing%20it%20then%20we%20are%20talking%20magic.%20%20If%20not%2C%20we%20are%0A%20%3E%20talking%20amazing%20coincidence...%20which%20in%20Middle-Earth%20often%20means%0A%20%3E%20%27divine%20intervention%27.%20%20:%29%0A%0AI%20certainly%20don%27t%20think%20he%20%2Aactually%2A%20heard%20Boromir%27s%20horn%20%28why%20only%0Ahim%2C%20and%20apparently%20no-one%20else%2C%20if%20it%27s%20just%20a%20straightforward%20case%20of%0Ahearing%3F%29.%20And%20in%20a%20previous%20post%20I%20did%20say%20that%20I%20thought%20%22that%20he%20had%0Aa%20presentiment%20of%20doom%20when%20he%20thought%20he%20%27heard%27%22.%20And%20that%27s%20all%20I%0Athink%20there%20is%20to%20it%2C%20in%20which%20case%20that%20fits%20the%20latter%20suggestion%20-%0A%27divine%20intervention%27.%20Magic%20just%20doesn%27t%20fit%20the%20evidence%2C%20as%20far%20as%0AI%27m%20concerned.%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20didn%27t%20say%20it%20did:%20I%20admitted%20that%20either%20interpretations%20are%20valid.%0ANor%20would%20I%20dismiss%20it%20%22out%20of%20hand%22%20-%20having%20gone%20over%20the%20evidence%20I%0Aprefer%20the%20view%20that%20men%20could%20not%20manipulate%20magic%20directly%2C%20but%20rather%0Athrough%20a%20medium%20%28a%20palantir%20etc%29.%20It%20just%20fits%20with%20the%20story%20more%0Acomfortably%20than%20the%20alternative%20for%20me.%0A%0AYes%2C%20I%27ve%20been%20a%20bit%20bothered%20about%20exactly%20%2Awhat%2A%20properties%20the%20horn%0Adid%20have%20-%20so%20far%20in%20this%20thread%20there%20has%20been%20a%20lot%20of%20assertions%20made%0Abut%20none%20of%20them%20have%20been%20backed%20up%20from%20the%20text.%20Unfortunately%0Asomeone%27s%20run%20off%20with%20my%20copy%20of%20Fellowship%2C%20so%20I%20can%27t%20do%20a%20full%0Aappraisal.%20But%20I%20think%20it%20would%20be%20helpful%20if%20someone%20actually%20posted%0Athe%20relevant%20quotes%2C%20rather%20than%20having%20everyone%20blunder%20about%20in%20the%0Adark%20%28so%20to%20speak%21%29.%20There%20seems%20to%20be%20heat%20and%20no%20light%20at%20all%20from%0Athis%20thread%20so%20far%21%0A%0A%20From%20memory%20I%20really%20can%27t%20see%20that%20there%20can%20be%20any%20issue%20about%0ABoromir%27s%20horn%20at%20all:%20it%27s%20quite%20clear%20to%20me%20from%20what%20Faramir%20says%0Athat%20it%20%2Awasn%27t%2A%20heard%20all%20the%20way%20to%20Minas%20Tirith%20-%20rather%20that%20he%20had%0Aa%20presentiment%20of%20doom%20when%20he%20thought%20he%20%27heard%27%20%28and%20one%20which%20later%0Acame%20to%20be%20fulfilled%29.%0A%0A%0ANope%2C%20sorry%20Conrad%2C%20that%27s%20not%20what%20it%20shows%20-%20all%20that%20can%20%2Adefinitely%2A%0Abe%20said%20is%20that%20Tolkien%20considered%20the%20possibility%20that%20they%20used%0Aspells:%20there%27s%20a%20question-mark%20at%20the%20end%20which%20makes%20his%20meaning%0Aunclear%20and%20open%20to%20reasonable%20doubt.%20More%20than%20that%20simply%20cannot%20be%20said.%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%0ASimplistic%20arguments%20of%20that%20kind%20on%20%2Aany%2A%20subject%20are%20annoying.%0AUnfortunately%2C%20many%20supporters%20of%20the%20film%20were%20usenet%20naifs%2C%20viewing%20%27cool%27%0Aas%20the%20winner%20of%20any%20argument%2C%20while%20many%20movie-snobs%20were%20of%20the%20opinion%0Athat%20%2Aany%2A%20departure%20from%20the%20text%20was%20necessarily%20bad.%20%20There%20were%20good%0Aarguments%20to%20be%20had%20on%20how%20PJ%27s%20interpretation%20of%20LotR%20contributes%20to%20one%27s%0Aunderstanding%20of%20it%2C%20but%20there%20weren%27t%20many%20people%20willing%20to%20join%20in%20that%0Adebate%2C%20unfortunately.%0A%0A%0A%0AOne%20could%20start%20by%20using%20Steuard%27s%20reviews%20as%20an%20example%20of%20neutrality%20and%0A%28some%29%20reviewed%20opinion.%20%20I%20discussed%20PJ%27s%20filling%20in%20of%20empty%20space%0A%28implied%20rather%20than%20stated%20features%20in%20the%20text%29%20in%20Tsar%27s%20thread%20of%20his%0Areview%20of%20FotR.%20%20And%20I%27m%20sure%20that%20such%20as%20yourself%20have%20contributed%20insight%0Ato%20the%20otherwise%20flame-filled%20fests%20generated%20by%20the%20discussion%20of%20the%0Afilms.%0A%0ACheers%2C%20ymt%20%28snip%20sig%20and%20continue%20after%20quotes%20to%20reply%29.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%0AThat%20was%20before%20he%20got%20his%20_third_%20yellow%20ticket%20from%20me.%0A%0AArchie%0A%0A--%0A%22I%20have%20told%20my%20sons%20that%20they%20are%20not%20under%20any%0Acircumstances%20to%20take%20part%20in%20massacres%2C%20and%20that%0Athe%20news%20of%20massacres%20of%20enemies%20is%20not%20to%20fill%20them%0Awith%20satisfaction%20or%20glee.%22%0A%0AKurt%20Vonnegut%2C%20_Slaughterhouse-Five_%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%20%3E%20Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0A%20%3E%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%20%3E%0A%20%3E%3E%20I%20didn%27t%20say%20it%20did:%0A%20%3E%0A%20%3E%20Ok%2C%20I%20thought%20that%20indirectly%20you%20had...%20Tsar%20said%20as%20much%20and%20you%0A%20%3E%20stated%20you%20agreed%20with%20his%20views.%20%20Presumably%20you%20agree%20with%20the%0A%20%3E%20interpretation%2C%20but%20not%20that%20it%20is%20incontrovertibly%20established.%0A%20%3E%0AYes:%20the%20Tsar%27s%20sentiments%20have%20my%20full%20support%2C%20but%20not%20the%20way%20he%0Aexpressed%20them%2C%20as%20they%20can%27t%20be%20conclusively%20proved%2C%20IMO.%0A%0A%20%3E%3E%20From%20memory%20I%20really%20can%27t%20see%20that%20there%20can%20be%20any%20issue%20about%0A%20%3E%3E%20Boromir%27s%20horn%20at%20all:%20it%27s%20quite%20clear%20to%20me%20from%20what%20Faramir%0A%20%3E%3E%20says%20that%20it%20%2Awasn%27t%2A%20heard%20all%20the%20way%20to%20Minas%20Tirith%20-%20rather%0A%20%3E%3E%20that%20he%20had%20a%20presentiment%20of%20doom%20when%20he%20thought%20he%20%27heard%27%20%28and%0A%20%3E%3E%20one%20which%20later%20came%20to%20be%20fulfilled%29.%0A%20%3E%0A%20%3E%20I%27d%20agree%20with%20that%20view%20of%20what%20the%20texts%20say%2C%20but%20would%20argue%20that%0A%20%3E%20it%20constitutes%20evidence%20of%20human%20magic%20in%20and%20of%20itself.%20%20Why%20did%0A%20%3E%20Faramir%20have%20this%20%27presentiment%20of%20doom%27%3F%20%20Why%20did%20the%20%27echo%20in%20his%0A%20%3E%20mind%27%20coincide%20with%20the%20time%20Boromir%20was%20blowing%20the%20horn%3F%20%20At%20that%2C%0A%20%3E%20how%20to%20explain%20%27foresight%27%20amongst%20Men%20in%20general%3F%20%20There%20are%0A%20%3E%20numerous%20examples%20of%20accurate%20predictions%20of%20the%20future...%20how%20can%0A%20%3E%20they%20do%20this%20if%20%27magic%27%20is%20completely%20alien%20to%20them%3F%20What%20was%20that%0Awhole%20scene%0A%20%3E%20with%20Gandalf%20and%20Denethor%20seeming%20to%20%27match%20wills%27%20REALLY%20about%20if%0A%20%3E%20Denethor%20had%20no%20means%20of%20externalizing%20his%20will%3F%20The%20%27healing%20hands%27%0A%20%3E%20of%20the%20Kings%3F%20The%20wonders%20created%20by%20the%20Numenoreans%3F%20%20References%20to%0A%20%3E%20human%20sorcerors%3F%0A%0AHave%20I%20missed%20those%3F%20Where%20are%20they%20referenced%3F%0A%0A%20%3E%20Et%20cetera...%20explanations%20can%20be%20constructed%20for%20each%2C%20but%20eventually%0A%20%3E%20it%20becomes%20rather%20alot%20of%20hoops%20to%20jump%20through.%0A%20%3E%0ASure%20they%20do%2C%20but%20at%20the%20same%20time%2C%20doesn%27t%20it%20bother%20you%20that%20you%20can%0Ajust%20point%20to%20all%20these%20events%20and%20lump%20them%20all%20in%20the%20big%20bin%20labelled%0A%27MAGIC%27%3F%20:%29%0A%0AWhere%27s%20the%20fun%20in%20an%20easy%20explanation%2C%20eh%3F%21%20And%20anyway%2C%20why%20assume%20that%0Aany%20of%20the%20above%20%2Aare%2A%20examples%20of%20%27magic%27%3F%20A%20few%20at%20least%20suggest%0Aspecial%20mental%20abilities%20rather%20than%20outright%20%27magic%27.%0A%0APerhaps%20the%20problem%20is%20what%20we%20are%20defining%20as%20%27magic%27.%20For%20me%2C%20I%20think%0Aof%20%27magic%27%20in%20quite%20specific%20terms%20-%20spells%20and%20incantations:%20Gandalf%20on%0ACarahdras%20for%20example.%20But%20I%27ve%20never%20assumed%20that%20anything%20else%20that%0Adoesn%27t%20have%20an%20obvious%20explanation%20%2Amust%2A%20be%20magic%20-%20the%20Moria%20doors%0Afor%20example.%20In%20the%20real%20world%20there%20are%20sometimes%20doors%20where%20you%20have%0Ato%20punch%20in%20a%20code%20to%20make%20it%20open:%20that%27s%20not%20magic%2C%20just%20technology.%0AOthers%20open%20when%20you%20approach%20them%2C%20but%20that%27s%20not%20magic%20either.%20It%0Amight%20%2Alook%2A%20magic%20of%20course%2C%20but%20that%27s%20hardly%20the%20same%20thing.%0ABasically%2C%20until%20there%20is%20outright%20evidence%20that%20magic%20%2Ais%2A%20involved%20in%0Aall%20of%20the%20above%20%28and%20other%20disputed%20things%29%2C%20I%20see%20no%20reason%20to%20accept%0Athe%20premise%20that%20it%27s%20%2Aalways%2A%20got%20to%20be%20magic.%0A%0A%20%3E%3E%20Nope%2C%20sorry%20Conrad%2C%20that%27s%20not%20what%20it%20shows%20-%20all%20that%20can%0A%20%3E%3E%20%2Adefinitely%2A%20be%20said%20is%20that%20Tolkien%20considered%20the%20possibility%0A%20%3E%3E%20that%20they%20used%20spells:%20there%27s%20a%20question-mark%20at%20the%20end%20which%0A%20%3E%3E%20makes%20his%20meaning%20unclear%20and%20open%20to%20reasonable%20doubt.%20More%20than%0A%20%3E%3E%20that%20simply%20cannot%20be%20said.%0A%20%3E%0A%20%3E%20%20Hrrrmmmm...%20if%20he%27d%20written%20that%20sentence%20in%20isolation%20I%27d%20agree.%0A%20%3E%20However%2C%20given%20that%20he%20had%20just%20stated%20that%20Men%20could%20not%20use%20magic%20I%0A%20%3E%20would%20think%20that%20the%20question%20mark%20indicated%20uncertainty%20of%20the%20%27NOT%0A%20%3E%20use%20magic%27%20statement%20rather%20than%20the%20%27but%20they%20DID%20use%20spells%27%0A%20%3E%20statement...%20he%27d%20made%20a%20claim%20and%20then%20noted%20that%20there%20was%0A%20%3E%20published%20material%20which%20seemed%20to%20contradict%20it.%20%20If%20he%20didn%27t%20think%0A%20%3E%20the%20published%20material%20was%20contradictory%20there%20would%20be%20no%20reason%20for%0A%20%3E%20the%20contrary%20sentence.%20%20Ergo%2C%20I%20have%20to%20believe%20that%20Tolkien%20saw%20a%0A%20%3E%20potential%20conflict%20there...%20meaning%20he%20could%20not%20have%20intended%20all%0A%20%3E%20along%20for%20the%20barrow%20blades%20to%20be%20completely%20non-magical%20or%20no%0A%20%3E%20conflict%20would%20have%20existed%20in%20his%20mind.%0A%0A%3Cshrug%3E%0A%0AI%20can%20see%20how%20that%20works%2C%20but%20I%20just%20don%27t%20think%20it%20can%20be%20fully%20relied%0Aon.%20Ultimately%2C%20I%20just%20prefer%20my%20interpretation%20:%29%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Conrad%20Dunkerson%20wrote:%0A%5B...%5D%0A%3Ca%20wicked%20smile%2F%3E%20Hasn%27t%20life%20shown%20you%20that%20there%20are%20no%20heroes%20at%20all%2C%0Ahowever%20tragic%20a%20fate%20may%20be%3F%20For%20me%2C%20it%27s%20just%20about%20doing%20what%20one%0Amust%2C%20though%20sometimes%20other%20rules%20pop%20up%20as%20well%20%28e.g.%20no%20naive%20faith%20in%0Athe%20enemy%20-%20cf.%20Turin%20and%20Glaurung%2C%20moral%20restraint%20etc.%29%20Turin%20the%20anti-%0Ahero%20has%20Free%20Will%20and%20is%20responsible%20for%20his%20actions%20whether%20good%20or%0Abad.%0A%0AFor%20instance%2C%20do%20you%20think%20Frodo%20is%20a%20%27tragic%20hero%27%20stereotype%3F%0A%0AWell%2C%20nobody%20is%20%28w.t.e.%20of%20Incarnate%20Evil%20%28TM%29%29.%20It%20was%20rather%20nice%20of%0ATolkien%20to%20drop%20the%20%27fiery%20bath%27%20part%20of%20redemption%20in%20later%20writings.%20I%0Aam%20happy%20that%20we%20would%20%28most%20probably%29%20have%20been%20given%20no%20details%20of%20the%0Amillennia%20of%20waiting%20in%20the%20Halls%20%28or%20a%20looong%20stay%20with%20Eru%2C%20in%20other%0Aversions%29.%0A%0AArchie%0A%0A--%0A%22I%20have%20told%20my%20sons%20that%20they%20are%20not%20under%20any%0Acircumstances%20to%20take%20part%20in%20massacres%2C%20and%20that%0Athe%20news%20of%20massacres%20of%20enemies%20is%20not%20to%20fill%20them%0Awith%20satisfaction%20or%20glee.%22%0A%0AKurt%20Vonnegut%2C%20_Slaughterhouse-Five_%0A%0A%0A
