Douglas%20Eckhart%20wrote:%0A%0AActually%20this%20is%20not%20that%20rare%2C%20especially%20in%20men%20of%20Northern%20origin%0A%28Southerners%20seem%20to%20get%20grey%20hair%20earlier%29.%20My%20father%20still%20has%0Acompletely%20black%20hair%2C%20and%20he%27s%2060%2C%20while%20I%20myself%20have%20some%20grey%0Astreaks%20at%2029.%20not%20fair....%20%3B-%29%0A%0A--%0A%0ALinards%20Ticmanis%0A%0A%20The%20Master%20said%2C%20%22The%20business%20of%20laying%20on%20the%20colors%20follows%20the%0Apreparation%20of%20the%20plain%20ground.%22%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Een%20wilde%20Ier%20said:%0A%0A%0ADo%20clean%20his%20mouth%20out%2C%20I%20assume...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Father%2C%20tell%20me%20about%20the%20mother%20I%20never%20knew%21%0A%0AReverie%2C%20I%20don%27t%20like%20to%20speak%20of%20her%3B%20sometimes%20I%27ve%20even%20forgotten%20her%20name.%0A%0AFather%2C%20it%20is%20beyond%20doubt%20that%20you%20came%20from%20over%20the%20wide%20wide%20sea%2C%20and%20that%0Ayou%20lost%20she%20who%20my%20own%20mother%20has%20replaced%20in%20that%20space%20where%20I%20have%20even%0Acried%2C%20between%20your%20arms.%0A%0AReverie%2C%20have%20you%20yet%20the%20years%20to%20have%20the%20thoughts%20of%20motherhood%3F%20%20I%20am%0Asurprised.%0A%0AFather%2C%20you%20are%20going%20blind%20in%20your%20old%20old%20age.%0A%0AI%20remember%20you%20crying%20near%20my%20own%20heart%2C%20dear%20child%20my%20youngest%2C%20dear%20Reverie.%0A%0AFather%2C%20I%20have%20met%20a%20man%2C%20I%20have%20met%20a%20man.%0A%0ADid%20he%20know%20ye%20already%3F%0A%0AFather%2C%20I%20know%20too%20little%20of%20those%20things%20that%20you%20speak%20with%20every%20move%2C%20that%0Aof%20your%20love%20for%20that%20woman%20who%20has%20become%20a%20witch%20in%20your%20own%20house.%20%20Do%20not%0Abe%20angry%20with%20me%21%0A%0AReverie%2C%20even%20though%20you%20carry%20none%20of%20her%20blood%2C%20it%20is%20most%20like%20she%20of%20my%0Achildren%20you%20are.%20%20Your%20own%20mother%20is%20not%20cursed.%0A%0AFather%2C%20I%20might%20grieve%20for%20my%20own%20mother%20if%20she%20were%20not%20as%20proud%20of%20you%20as%20she%0Ais%20giving%20of%20her%20that%20was%20lost%20long%20ago.%20%20She%20has%20become%20a%20witch%20among%20the%0Avillagers%2C%20a%20tale%2C%20a%20legend%20to%20scare%20every%20toothless%20infant.%20%20You%20at%20least%0Ashould%20tell%20me%20at%20least%2C%20all%20about%20that%20woman.%0A%0AReverie%2C%20her%20name%20is%20not%20forgotten%2C%20only%20I%20cannot%20speak%20it.%20%20How%20then%20shall%20I%0Acall%20her%3F%0A%0AShe%20is%20your%20own%20Reverie%2C%20then%2C%20fa.%0A%0AReverie%3B%20%20I%20suppose.%0A%0AFa%2C%20what%20was%20she%20like%3F%0A%0ABraver%20than%20you%21%20%20But%20maybe%20not.%20%20Prettier%20even%20than%20you%2C%20who%20are%20prettiest%0Aamong%20all%20the%20villages.%20%20I%20am%20not%20that%20blind.%0A%0AFa%2C%20you%20are%20still%20desirable%2C%20even%20among%20my%20%27cousins%27%2C%20the%20villagers.%20%20Maybe%20I%0Atake%20after%20you%3F%0A%0AWe%20were%20attractive%20people%2C%20the%20people%20of%20the%20raft%2C%20and%20your%20likeness%2C%20that%0AReverie%20of%20mine%2C%20was%20both%20brave%2C%20no%2C%20braver%20than%20she%20was%20beautiful%2C%20most%0Abeautiful%20and%20brave%20among%20the%20people%20on%20the%20raft.%20%20You%20have%20too%20much%20of%20your%0Amother%20in%20you%20to%20really%20remind%20me%20of%20her%2C%20my%20Reverie.%20%20And%20her%20hair%20was%20like%0Athe%20curls%20on%20the%20wavetops%2C%20sometimes%2C%20even%20darker%20than%20yours%2C%20daughter.%0A%0AOh%20fa%21%0A%0AYour%20behind%20is%20quite%20like%20hers%2C%20now%20that%20I%20remember%20it%2C%20saucy%20in%20my%20eyes%20and%0Awet%20from%20the%20fresh%20water%20she%20loved%20to%20dip%20herself%20into%20all%20of%20the%20time%2C%20and%0Aquivering%20with%20the%20youth%20that%20I%20have%20long%20since%20lost.%20%20Drip%20drop%2C%20drip%20drop%2C%0Ahmmmm.%0A%0AHee%21%20%20Now%20you%20are%20pulling%20my%20little%20toe%2C%20fa%21%0A%0AGet%20thee%20gone%20from%20here%2C%20Reverie%20my%20favorite%20and%20prettiest%20daughter%21%0A%0AOh%2C%20alright%2C%20bye%20bye%21%0A%0AHeh%21%0A%0A%0A
