In%20article%20%3C3f2ec6ce$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%0A%20Gonzalo%20Diethelm%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20Yep.%20%20%232%20and%20%233%20have%20the%20shorter%20theatrical%20cut%20of%20the%20movie%20%28about%0A3%20hours%29%20plus%20one%20disc%20of%20extras%2C%20the%20only%20difference%20between%20them%20being%0Athe%20aspect%20ratio%20--%20full%20screen%20fills%20your%20entire%20TV%20screen%2C%20and%0Awidescreen%20has%20the%20black%20bars%20at%20top%20and%20bottom.%20%20%28That%27s%20called%0A%22letterboxing%22%2C%20and%20reproduces%20the%20way%20it%20was%20shown%20in%20the%20theater.%29%0AThus%2C%20%232%20is%20as%20presented%20in%20the%20theater%3B%20%233%20has%20the%20sides%20chopped%20off%20to%0Afit%20your%20TV.%20%20Eliminate%20%233%20immediately.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%231%20and%20%234%20have%20the%20extended%20cut%20of%20the%20movie%20%28about%203%201%2F2%20hours%29%20on%0Atwo%20discs%20in%20widescreen.%20%20%231%20has%20two%20discs%20of%20fabulous%20extras%3B%20%234%20has%0Athose%20two%20plus%20a%20fifth%20disc%20containing%20a%20couple%20of%20National%20Geographic%0Aspecials%20%28available%20separately%29.%20%20%234%20also%20has%20a%20pair%20of%20bookends%20shaped%0Alike%20the%20Arionath.%20%20Both%20sets%20have%20four%20commentary%20tracks.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20I%20would%20recommend%20%231%20for%20you%20--%20the%20extra%20disc%20and%20the%20bookends%0Aaren%27t%20worth%20an%20extra%20$30%2C%20imho%2C%20and%20%232%20doesn%27t%20have%20any%20extra%20footage.%0ANote%2C%20however%2C%20that%20the%20extras%20disc%20that%20comes%20with%20%232%20doesn%27t%20overlap%0Aat%20all%20with%20the%20extras%20in%20%231%2C%20so%20if%20you%20want%20all%20the%20extra%20goodies%0Ayou%27ll%20need%20to%20get%20both.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20----j7y%0A%0A--%0A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%0Ajere7my%20tho%3Frpe%20%2F%20800-555-1212%20%20%20%20%20%20%22There%20is%20no%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20%20%22There%0A%20%20%20%20%3E%3E%3E%20%41nospam@nospam.net%20%20%3C%3C%3C%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20is%20no%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20%20%22There%20is%20no%0Ainvert%20liws%20to%20reply%20via%20email%20%20%20%20%20%20%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20--%20The%20Tick%20vs.%20Neo%0A%0A%0A
In%20article%20%3C3jAOa.7253$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%0Arec.arts.books.tolkien%2C%20Troels%20Forchhammer%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%0Awrote:%0A%0AYes%2C%20I%20agree.%20Tolkien%20talks%20about%20that%20in%20a%20Letter.%0A%0A%0AYes%2C%20I%20think%20so%20too.%20Close%2C%20but%20not%20quite%20there.%20As%20you%20say%2C%20the%0Alarger%20and%20landed%20clans%20did%20seem%20to%20have%20a%20certain%20amount%20of%0Aprestige:%20I%20think%20of%20them%20as%20landed%20gentry%20rather%20than%20nobility.%0A%0ABut%20two%20clans%20have%20clearly%20defined%20territories%2C%20and%20I%20think%20their%0Aheads%20_are_%20nobility%20because%20they%20have%20titles%20and%20even%20numerals%0Aafter%20their%20names:%20the%20Thain%20and%20the%20Master%20of%20Buckland.%28%2A%29%20Tolkien%0Aeven%20describes%20Buckland%20as%20%22virtually%20a%20small%20independent%20country%22%2C%0Awhich%20would%20put%20him%20in%20the%20position%20of%20the%20Marcher%20lords%20of%20England%0Aduring%20the%2012th%20and%2013th%20centuries.%0A%0A%28%2A%29%20Tolkien%20said%20that%20the%20Thains%20got%20numbers%20if%20required%2C%20but%20he%0Adidn%27t%20say%20that%20about%20the%20Masters.%20The%20genealogical%20table%20of%20the%0ABrandybucks%20in%20the%20back%20doesn%27t%20show%20any%20numbers%2C%20but%20it%20also%0Adoesn%27t%20show%20any%20repeated%20names%20that%20I%20notices%2C%20so%20that%20point%20could%0Ago%20either%20way.%20But%20Buckland%20is%20even%20more%20independent%20than%20the%0ATookland%2C%20since%20Buckland%20was%20not%20part%20of%20the%20Shire%20at%20the%20time%20of%0Athe%20War%20of%20the%20Ring.%0A%0A--%0AStan%20Brown%2C%20Oak%20Road%20Systems%2C%20Cortland%20County%2C%20New%20York%2C%20USA%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20http:%2F%2FOakRoadSystems.com%0ATolkien%20FAQs:%20http:%2F%2FTolkien.slimy.com%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%27s%20site%29%0ATolkien%20letters%20FAQ:%0A%20%20%20http:%2F%2Fusers.telerama.com%2F~taliesen%2Ftolkien%2Flettersfaq.html%0AFAQ%20of%20the%20Rings:%20http:%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Fgenl%2Fringfaq.htm%0AEncyclopedia%20of%20Arda:%20http:%2F%2Fwww.glyphweb.com%2Farda%2Fdefault.htm%0Amore%20FAQs:%20http:%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Ftech%2Ffaqget.htm%0A%0A%0A
