In%20article%20%3C5gKTa.118165$GL4.31476@rwcrnsc53%3E%2C%20%22Joe%20Seamour%22%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0Acaptured%20and%20tortured%20adn%20wounded%0A%28some%20have%20interpreted%20that%20as%20rape%29%0Aafter%20that%20celbrian%20grew%20weary%20of%20middleearth%20and%20left%20for%20eldamar%0Aleft%20her%20sons%20and%20daughter%20and%20elrond%0Aelrond%20joined%20her%20at%20the%20beginning%20f%20the%20fourth%20age%0A%0A%0A
In%20article%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%41nospam@nospam.net%20says...%0A%0AThe%20Silvan%20Elves%20seem%20to%20have%20been%20a%20mix%20of%20Eldar%20and%20Avari.%0A%0A%22But%20though%20Mithrellas%20%5Bhandmaiden%20to%20Nimrodel%5D%20was%20of%20the%20lesser%20Silvan%0Arace%20%28and%20not%20of%20the%20High%20Elves%20or%20the%20Grey%29%20it%20was%20ever%20held%20that%20the%0Ahouse%20and%20kin%20of%20the%20Lords%20of%20Dol%20Amroth%20was%20noble%20by%20blood%20as%20they%20were%0Afair%20in%20face%20and%20mind.%22%0AUnfinished%20Tales%0A%0AOf%20course%20we%20have:%0A%22The%20Silvan%20Elves%20%28Tawarwaith%29%20were%20in%20origin%20Teleri%2C%20and%20so%20remoter%20kin%0Aof%20the%20Sindar%2C%20though%20even%20longer%20separated%20from%20them%20than%20the%20Teleri%20of%0AValinor.%20%22%0Aop.%20cit.%0A%0AAnd:%0A%22The%20Silvan%20Elves%20hid%20themselves%20in%20woodland%20fastnesses%20beyond%20the%20Misty%0AMountains%2C%20and%20became%20small%20and%20scattered%20people%2C%20hardly%20to%20be%0Adistinguished%20from%20Avari%3B%0A%0Abut%20they%20still%20remembered%20that%20they%20were%20in%20origin%20Eldar%2C%20members%20of%20the%0AThird%20Clan%2C%20and%20they%20welcomed%20those%20of%20the%20Noldor%20and%20especially%20the%0ASindar%20who%20did%20not%20pass%20over%20the%20Sea%20but%20migrated%20eastward%20%5Bi.e.%20at%20the%0Abeginning%20of%20the%20Second%20Age%5D.%22%0Aop.%20cit.%0A%0AWe%20also%20have:%0A%22...the%20Lindarin%20elements%20in%20the%20western%20Avari%20were%20friendly%20to%20the%0AEldar%2C%20and%20willing%20to%20learn%20from%20them%3B%20and%20so%20close%20was%20the%20feeling%20of%0Akinship%20between%20the%20remnants%20of%20the%20Sindar%2C%20the%20Nandor%2C%20and%20the%20Lindarin%0AAvari%2C%20that%20later%20in%20Eriador%20and%20the%20Vale%20of%20Anduin%20they%20often%20became%0Amerged%20together.%22%0AQuendi%20&%20Eldar%2C%20WotJ%0A%0A%0AAnd:%0A%22This%20resentment%20on%20the%20part%20of%20the%20Avari%20is%20illustrated%20by%20the%20history%0Aof%20PQ%20%2Akwendi.%20This%20word%2C%20as%20has%20been%20shown%2C%20did%20not%20survive%20in%20the%0ATelerin%20languages%20of%20Middle-earth%2C%20and%20was%20almost%20forgotten%20even%20in%20the%0ATelerin%20of%20Aman.%20But%20the%20Loremasters%20of%20later%20days%2C%20when%20more%20friendly%0Arelations%20had%20been%20established%20with%20Avari%20of%20various%20kinds%20in%20Eriador%0Aand%20the%20Vale%20of%20Anduin%2C%20record%20that%20it%20was%20frequently%20to%20be%20found%20in%0AAvarin%20dialects.%20These%20were%20numerous%2C%20and%20often%20as%20widely%20sundered%20from%0Aone%20another%20as%20they%20were%20from%20the%20Eldarin%20forms%20of%20Elvish%20speech%3B%20but%0Awherever%20the%20descendants%20of%20%2Akwendi%20were%20found%2C%20they%20meant%20not%20%27Elves%20in%0Ageneral%27%2C%20but%20were%20the%20names%20that%20the%20Avari%20gave%20to%20themselves.%20They%20had%0Aevidently%20continued%20to%20call%20themselves%20%2Akwendi%2C%20%27the%20People%27%2C%20regarding%0Athose%20who%20went%20away%20as%20deserters%20...%20The%20Avarin%20forms%20cited%20by%20the%0ALoremasters%20were:%20kindi%2C%20cuind%2C%20hwenti%2C%20windan%2C%20kinn-lai%2C%20penni%20...%20The%0Aform%20penni%20is%20cited%20as%20coming%20from%20the%20%27Wood-elven%27%20speech%20of%20the%20Vale%0Aof%20Anduin%2C%20and%20these%20Elves%20were%20among%20the%20most%20friendly%20to%20the%20fugitives%0Afrom%20Beleriand%2C%20and%20held%20themselves%20akin%20to%20the%20remnants%20of%20the%20Sindar.%22%0Aop.%20cit.%0A%0AThen%20there%20is:%0A%22The%20Elves%20far%20back%20in%20the%20Elder%20Days%20became%20divided%20into%20two%20main%0Abranches:%20the%20West-elves%20%28the%20Eldar%29%20and%20the%20East-elves.%20Of%20the%20latter%0Akind%20were%20most%20of%20the%20elven-folk%20of%20Mirkwood%20and%20L%F3rien%3B%20but%20their%0Alanguages%20do%20not%20appear%20in%20this%20history%2C%20in%20which%20all%20the%20Elvish%20names%0Aand%20words%20are%20of%20Eldarin%20form.%22%0ALotR%2C%20App.%20F%0A%0A--%0ATar-Elenion%0A%0AExtremism%20in%20defence%20of%20liberty%20is%20no%20vice.%0AModeration%20in%20pursuit%20of%20justice%20is%20no%20virtue.%0A%0A%0A
In%20article%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20rec.arts.books.tolkien%2C%20Marie-%0ALan%20Nguyen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AIn%20fact%2C%20LotR%20strongly%20hints%20that%20Sam%20_did_%20eventually%20sail%20West%0Aover%20Sea%2C%20in%20the%20very%20passage%20you%20quote.%20%22Well%2C%20I%27m%20back%22%20closes%20the%0Abook%20but%20not%20Sam%27s%20life.%20Further%2C%20in%20a%20Letter%20Tolkien%20says%20that%20Sam%0A_did_%20go%20west.%0A%0AYou%20might%20like%20to%20read%20the%20FAQ%2C%20specifically%0A%09http:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Ffaq%2FHistory.html%23SamWest%0A%0A--%0AStan%20Brown%2C%20Oak%20Road%20Systems%2C%20Cortland%20County%2C%20New%20York%2C%20USA%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20http:%2F%2FOakRoadSystems.com%0ATolkien%20FAQs:%20http:%2F%2FTolkien.slimy.com%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%27s%20site%29%0ATolkien%20letters%20FAQ:%0A%20%20%20http:%2F%2Fusers.telerama.com%2F~taliesen%2Ftolkien%2Flettersfaq.html%0AFAQ%20of%20the%20Rings:%20http:%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Fgenl%2Fringfaq.htm%0AEncyclopedia%20of%20Arda:%20http:%2F%2Fwww.glyphweb.com%2Farda%2Fdefault.htm%0Amore%20FAQs:%20http:%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Ftech%2Ffaqget.htm%0A%0A%0A
