In%20article%20%3Cbfmflt$futn2$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%20%22Morgil%22%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0Ahunted%20down%20by%20the%20queens%20navy%20led%20by%20some%20pale%20faced%20git%0Awearing%20a%20silly%20eagle%20brooch%0A%0A%0Ahe%20was%20a%20hard%20-%20headed%20man%0Ahe%20was%20brutally%20handsome%20and%20she%20was%20terminally%20pretty%0Ashe%20held%20him%20up%20and%20he%20held%20her%20for%20ransom%20in%20the%20heart%0Aof%20the%20stone%20stone%20city%0Ahe%20had%20a%20nasty%20reputation%20as%20a%20wandering%20ranger%0Athey%20said%20he%20was%20ruthless%20they%20said%20he%20was%20crude%0Athey%20had%20one%20thing%20in%20common%20they%20were%0Ahalf%20elven%20offspring%0Ashed%20say%20faster%20faster%20the%20third%20age%20is%20fading%0Alife%20on%20the%20bounty%20main%0Asurely%20make%20you%20lose%20your%20mind%20mm%0Aare%20you%20with%20me%20so%20far%0A%0A%0A
In%20article%20%3Cbg5ggt$t7s$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%0A%20%22Luminaria%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20Most%20of%20Jackson%27s%20character%20changes%20can%20be%20followed%20back%20to%20one%0Aroot:%20%20he%20wanted%20to%20flaw%20up%20his%20heroes%2C%20probably%20because%20%22modern%22%20heroes%0Aovercome%20flaws%20and%20%22classical%22%20heroes%20are%20unflinchingly%20heroic%0Athroughout.%20%20This%20is%20why%20Aragorn%20hesitates%20about%20claiming%20the%20kingship%2C%0Awhy%20Theoden%20doesn%27t%20want%20to%20move%20his%20people%20to%20safety%2C%20why%20Faramir%20was%0Anot%20the%20kindly%20tea-sipper%20he%20was%20in%20the%20book%2C%20why%20Elrond%20was%20kind%20of%20a%0Adick%2C%20etc.%2C%20etc.%20%20This%20seems%20to%20be%20a%20deliberate%20move%20on%20Jackson%27s%20part%2C%0Aand%20I%20can%20understand%20why%20he%20did%20it%2C%20even%20if%20I%20don%27t%20always%20agree%20--%0Amodern%20film%20audiences%20don%27t%20react%20well%20to%20sterling%20saints.%20%20They%20want%0Acharacter%20development%2C%20not%20stasis.%20%20Certainly%20Faramir%2C%20as%20filmed%2C%20will%0Aneed%20to%20undergo%20some%20development%20before%20he%20can%20do%20what%20he%20does%20in%20RotK%2C%0Aor%20audiences%20won%27t%20accept%20him.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20A%20second%20%28and%20related%29%20root%2C%20I%20think%2C%20was%20a%20desire%20to%20consolidate%0Aheroism%2C%20specifically%20by%20giving%20the%20eight%20surviving%20members%20of%20the%0AFellowship%20%28plus%20Eowyn%29%20more%20to%20do.%20%20A%20natural%20corollary%20of%20this%20is%20that%0Athe%20secondary%20characters%20are%20less%20heroic.%20%20Merry%20and%20Pippin%20trick%0ATreebeard%20because%20they%27re%20main%20characters%3B%20in%20the%20scene%20as%20written%2C%20the%0Ahobbits%20are%20bystanders%20and%20Treebeard%20is%20the%20hero%2C%20whereas%20the%20filmed%0Ascene%20gives%20us%20the%20first%20glimmerings%20of%20a%20hobbit%20that%27ll%20stand%20up%20to%20the%0AWitch-King.%20%20Books%20can%20juggle%20and%20develop%20dozens%20of%20secondary%0Acharacters%2C%20because%20readers%20can%20flip%20back%20and%20forth%20and%20reread%2C%20and%0Abooks%20can%20take%20as%20many%20pages%20as%20they%20like%20to%20do%20it%3B%20movies%20really%0Astruggle%20when%20they%20have%20more%20than%20half%20a%20dozen%20character%20arcs.%20%20Hence%2C%0AEowyn%20absorbs%20Glorfindel%27s%20role%2C%20Eomer%20absorbs%20Erkenbrand%2C%20the%20hobbits%0Atake%20center%20stage%20away%20from%20Treebeard%2C%20Aragorn%20is%20right%20when%20Theoden%20is%0Awrong.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20Additionally:%20%20I%20suspect%20that%20Faramir%20was%20made%20harsher%20because%0AShelob%20was%20moved%20to%20RotK.%20%20Jackson%20didn%27t%20want%20a%20pleasant%20tea-break%20to%0Abe%20the%20climax%20of%20his%20second%20movie.%20%20If%20Helm%27s%20Deep%20is%20happening%20to%20one%0Aset%20of%20characters%20and%20another%20is%20tearing%20down%20Isengard%2C%20having%20the%20third%0Aengaged%20in%20pleasant%20conversation%20interrupts%20the%20rhythm%2C%20possibly%0Afatally.%20%20Thus%20there%27s%20some%20interpersonal%20tension%20and%20suspicion%20before%0Amovie-Faramir%20reaches%20the%20conclusion%20he%20reaches%20at%20once%20in%20the%20book.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20So%20there%20are%20certainly%20plausible%20reasons%20behind%20the%20changes%20other%0Athan%20%22Peter%20Jackson%20is%20a%20jerk%21%22%20%20I%20think%20it%27s%20more%20interesting%20to%20look%0Aat%20the%20changes%20and%20figure%20out%20why%20he%20made%20them%20than%20to%20assume%20he%20doesn%27t%0Aunderstand%20Tolkien%3B%20Jackson%20probably%20agonized%20over%20some%20of%20the%20changes%0Ahe%20had%20to%20make%2C%20since%20he%20obviously%20loves%20the%20books.%20%20But%2C%20as%20I%20say%2C%20I%0Ahope%20the%20extended%20edition%20and%2For%20Jackson%27s%20commentary%20will%20make%20some%20of%0Athis%20explicit%3B%20I%27m%20only%20guessing%20here.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20----j7y%0A%0A--%0A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%0Ajere7my%20tho%3Frpe%20%2F%20800-555-1212%20%20%20%20%20%20%22There%20is%20no%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20%20%22There%0A%20%20%20%20%3E%3E%3E%20%41nospam@nospam.net%20%20%3C%3C%3C%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20is%20no%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20%20%22There%20is%20no%0Ainvert%20liws%20to%20reply%20via%20email%20%20%20%20%20%20%20spoon.%22%20%20%22SPOON%21%22%20--%20The%20Tick%20vs.%20Neo%0A%0A%0A
