In%20the%20Year%20of%20the%20Goat%2C%20the%20Great%20and%20Powerful%20Louis%20Epstein%0Adeclared...%0AI%27m%20sure%20New%20Line%20is%20quite%20distraught%20at%20FotR%20going%20down%20a%20notch%0Aon%20the%20all-time%20list.%20I%20guess%20they%27ll%20just%20have%20to%20console%0Athemselves%20with%20the%20fact%20that%20each%20film%20has%20turned%20in%20a%20better%0Athan%20300%25%20profit.%0A%0A%0A--%0ASean%20O%27Hara%0A%22Harry%20goes%20through%20absolute%20hell%20every%20time%20he%20returns%20to%20school.%0ASo%20I%20think%20that%20a%20bit%20of%20snogging%20would%20alleviate%20matters.%22%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20--J.K.%20Rowling%0A%0A%0A
Its%20available%20via%20all%20the%20P2P%20programs%20now%20but%20I%20wouldnt%20try%20to%20get%20it%20from%0AKazaa%20as%20the%20fakes%20are%20a%20plenty%0A%0ASearch%20for%20file%20rotk.rar%20or%20rotk_768.mov%0A%0Aon%20Emule%20or%20Edonkey%0A%22Furio97%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:41nospam@nospam.net...%0Auntil%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0ABut%20that%20gives%20problems%20with%20respect%20to%20the%20Mouth%20of%20Sauron%2C%0Awho%20%22learned%20great%20sorcery%2C%22%20but%20was%20also%20definitely%20a%20man.%0A%0AThen%20there%27s%20the%20Dr%FAedain%20who%20are%20also%20definitely%20men%2C%20but%0Awho%20used%20some%20special%20kinds%20of%20magic%20%28%22The%20Faithful%20Stone%22%29.%0A%0AAnd%20IIRC%20in%20PoMe%2C%20though%20not%20necessarily%20canon%2C%20we%20hear%20about%0Athe%20people%20who%20took%20over%20the%20lands%20of%20one%20of%20the%20Northern%0AKingdoms%20that%20they%20were%20sorcerers%20or%20used%20sorcery%20...%0A%0AI%20think%20that%20there%20are%20problems%20no%20matter%20what%20explanation%0Aone%20favours%20%3B-%29%0A%0APersonally%20I%20think%20that%20Men%20could%20wield%20magic%2C%20but%20only%20in%0Aspecial%20circumstances%2C%20and%20never%20as%20something%20commonplace%0Athe%20way%20the%20Elves%20used%20it.%0A%0AWhat%20%27special%20circumstances%27%20that%20might%20apply%20is%20not%20very%0Aclear%2C%20but%20supernatural%20tutors%20appear%20to%20be%20one%20possibility%0A%28the%20Mouth%20of%20Sauron%20-%20people%20learning%20from%20the%20Witch-king%29.%0A%0A%0ASebastian%20has%20already%20posted%20the%20relevant%20passage%20about%0ABoromir%27s%20horn%20%28which%20is%20from%20Two%20Towers%2C%20BTW%29.%0A%0AThere%20was%20also%20the%20horn%20that%20%C9owyn%20gave%20to%20Merry.%20That%20too%20was%0Asaid%20to%20have%20properties%20that%20were%20definitely%20magical%20%28%22He%20that%0Ablows%20it%20at%20need%20shall%20set%20fear%20in%20the%20hearts%20of%20his%20enemies%20and%0Ajoy%20in%20the%20hearts%20of%20his%20friends%2C%20and%20they%20shall%20hear%20him%20and%0Acome%20to%20him.%22%29%2C%20but%20that%20one%20was%20made%20by%20the%20Dwarves.%20Is%20there%0Aanything%20that%20says%20that%20Boromir%27s%20horn%20was%20made%20by%20Men%3F%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0ATaken%20out%20of%20context%20I%20would%20probably%20agree%2C%20but%20when%20seen%20in%0Acontext%20with%20what%20was%20written%20about%20this%20in%20LotR%20%28%22wound%20about%0Awith%20spells%20for%20the%20bane%20of%20Mordor%22%20and%20%22No%20other%20blade%2C%20not%0Athough%20mightier%20hands%20had%20wielded%20it%22%29%20I%20am%20sure%20that%20Conrad%20is%0Aright%20-%20Tolkien%20did%20realise%20that%20he%20had%20written%20that%20they%20had%0Aindeed%20used%20spells.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A
Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0AI%20don%27t%20intend%20to%20reawaken%20that%20discussion%20at%20this%20time%20and%0Aplace%20and%20I%20dont%20think%20it%27s%20necessary%20either%20%3B-%29%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0A%22The%20rider%20was%20robed%20all%20in%20black%2C%20and%20black%20was%20his%20lofty%20helm%3B%0Ayet%20this%20was%20no%20Ringwraith%20but%20a%20living%20man.%22%0A%0AI%20think%20that%20this%20makes%20very%20clear%20that%20we%20are%20dealing%20with%20%22a%0Aliving%20man%22%20who%20has%20%22learned%20great%20sorcery%22.%20It%20might%20be%20that%0Athat%20is%20difficult%20within%20a%20normal%20life-span%20%28I%20don%27t%20think%20I%27d%0Aaccept%20%27impossible%27%29%20-%20or%20possibly%20that%20it%20took%20so%20much%20time%20to%0Alearn%20any%20kind%20of%20sorcery%20that%20it%20was%20impractical%20for%20normal%20Men%0A%28not%20many%20societies%20in%20Middle-earth%20had%20the%20surplus%20to%20allow%0Asome%20of%20their%20members%20to%20be%20inproductive%20for%2040+%20years%20after%0Acoming%20of%20age%29.%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0AWell%20-%20there%27s%20some%20fair%20indications%20that%20on%20at%20least%20some%20issues%0Ahe%20meant%20something%20different%20at%20different%20times%2C%20so%20that%20might%20not%0Asolve%20all%20questions.%20There%27s%20a%20few%20that%20it%20might%20be%20nice%20to%20get%0Asolved%20for%20good%2C%20but%20I%20think%20we%27re%20having%20too%20much%20fun%20with%20the%20rest%0Aof%20them%20to%20really%2C%20seriously%20want%20to%20have%20them%20solved%20%3B-%29%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0AIt%20is%2C%20IMO%2C%20a%20matter%20of%20the%20guarantee.%20If%20what%20%C9owyn%20says%20is%20correct%0A%28and%20I%20believe%20it%20is%20-%20remember%20the%20reaction%20of%20Sam%27s%20pony%20at%20Bywater%29%2C%0Athen%20the%20horn%20is%20magical%20because%20using%20it%20guarantees%20that%20these%20things%0Awill%20happen.%0A%0AA%20normal%20horn%20only%20makes%20this%20a%20little%20more%20probable%20than%20shouting%0A%28and%20only%20if%20the%20friends%20are%20able%20to%20recognise%20the%20tune%20or%20the%20voice%0Aof%20the%20horn%29.%0A%0AAnyway%2C%20Merry%27s%20horn%20was%20made%20by%20the%20Dwarves%20and%20has%20probably%20nothing%0Ato%20do%20with%20the%20issue%20of%20Men%20and%20magic.%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A
Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0ASure%2C%20but%20it%20DOESN%27T%20allow%20any%20possibility%20of%20%27human%20magic%27%20to%20be%0Adismissed%20out%20of%20hand.%20%20The%20horn%20was%20said%20to%20have%20magical%20properties.%0AThe%20horn%20was%20SHOWN%20to%20have%20properties%20which%20cannot%20be%20explained%20by%0Anormal%20physics.%0A%0AI%20take%20that%20as%20%27independant%20evidence%27...%20the%20letter%20draft%20shows%20both%0Asides%20of%20a%20disputed%20idea%2C%20but%20I%27d%20argue%20that%20there%20are%20several%0Aexternal%20pieces%20of%20evidence%20that%20argue%20only%20for%20one%20side%20%28that%20men%0ACOULD%20work%20%27magic%27%29%20and%20little%20outside%20that%20letter%20to%20support%20the%0Aother%20view.%20%20Still%2C%20nothing%20in%20the%20text%20ABSOLUTELY%20proves%20the%20point...%0Athere%20is%20always%20a%20way%20to%20come%20up%20with%20an%20alternate%20explanation.%0AHowever%2C%20the%20letter%20itself%20shows%20that%20%3ETolkien%3C%20believed%20they%20HAD%20used%0Aspells%20and%20this%20conflicted%20with%20his%20later%20idea%20that%20they%20shouldn%27t%20be%0Aable%20to.%0A%0A%0A
Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AOk%2C%20I%20thought%20that%20indirectly%20you%20had...%20Tsar%20said%20as%20much%20and%20you%0Astated%20you%20agreed%20with%20his%20views.%20%20Presumably%20you%20agree%20with%20the%0Ainterpretation%2C%20but%20not%20that%20it%20is%20incontrovertibly%20established.%0A%0A%0AI%27d%20agree%20with%20that%20view%20of%20what%20the%20texts%20say%2C%20but%20would%20argue%20that%0Ait%20constitutes%20evidence%20of%20human%20magic%20in%20and%20of%20itself.%20%20Why%20did%0AFaramir%20have%20this%20%27presentiment%20of%20doom%27%3F%20%20Why%20did%20the%20%27echo%20in%20his%0Amind%27%20coincide%20with%20the%20time%20Boromir%20was%20blowing%20the%20horn%3F%20%20At%20that%2C%0Ahow%20to%20explain%20%27foresight%27%20amongst%20Men%20in%20general%3F%20%20There%20are%20numerous%0Aexamples%20of%20accurate%20predictions%20of%20the%20future...%20how%20can%20they%20do%20this%0Aif%20%27magic%27%20is%20completely%20alien%20to%20them%3F%20%20What%20was%20that%20whole%20scene%0Awith%20Gandalf%20and%20Denethor%20seeming%20to%20%27match%20wills%27%20REALLY%20about%20if%0ADenethor%20had%20no%20means%20of%20externalizing%20his%20will%3F%20%20The%20%27healing%20hands%27%0Aof%20the%20Kings%3F%20%20The%20wonders%20created%20by%20the%20Numenoreans%3F%20%20References%20to%0Ahuman%20sorcerors%3F%20%20Et%20cetera...%20explanations%20can%20be%20constructed%20for%0Aeach%2C%20but%20eventually%20it%20becomes%20rather%20alot%20of%20hoops%20to%20jump%20through.%0A%0A%0AHrrrmmmm...%20if%20he%27d%20written%20that%20sentence%20in%20isolation%20I%27d%20agree.%0AHowever%2C%20given%20that%20he%20had%20just%20stated%20that%20Men%20could%20not%20use%20magic%20I%0Awould%20think%20that%20the%20question%20mark%20indicated%20uncertainty%20of%20the%20%27NOT%0Ause%20magic%27%20statement%20rather%20than%20the%20%27but%20they%20DID%20use%20spells%27%0Astatement...%20he%27d%20made%20a%20claim%20and%20then%20noted%20that%20there%20was%20published%0Amaterial%20which%20seemed%20to%20contradict%20it.%20%20If%20he%20didn%27t%20think%20the%0Apublished%20material%20was%20contradictory%20there%20would%20be%20no%20reason%20for%20the%0Acontrary%20sentence.%20%20Ergo%2C%20I%20have%20to%20believe%20that%20Tolkien%20saw%20a%0Apotential%20conflict%20there...%20meaning%20he%20could%20not%20have%20intended%20all%0Aalong%20for%20the%20barrow%20blades%20to%20be%20completely%20non-magical%20or%20no%0Aconflict%20would%20have%20existed%20in%20his%20mind.%0A%0A%0A
Jamie%20Armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0ABut...%20how%20does%20that%20square%20with%3B%0A%0Anorthward%20it%0Aboding%20of%0ABoromir%27s%0A%0AWHY%20did%20Faramir%20hear%20the%20horn%3F%20%20Was%20it%20just%20a%20%27daydream%27%20or%20his%0Aimagination%2C%20that%20just%20happened%20to%20coincide%20with%20the%20time%20the%20horn%20was%0Abeing%20blown%3F%20%20If%20Faramir%20actually%20%27heard%27%20that%20horn%20because%20Boromir%0Awas%20blowing%20it%20then%20we%20are%20talking%20magic.%20%20If%20not%2C%20we%20are%20talking%0Aamazing%20coincidence...%20which%20in%20Middle-Earth%20often%20means%20%27divine%0Aintervention%27.%20%20:%29%0A%0A%0A
Jason%20wrote%20...%0A%0AInteresting%20question.%20I%27ve%20always%20enjoyed%20speculating%2C%20especially%0Awithout%20any%20textual%20evidence%20to%20get%20in%20the%20way.%20Most%20such%20speculative%0Aquestions%20on%20this%20group%20tend%20to%20be%20pessimistic%20so%20it%27s%20a%20change%20to%20think%0Aof%20how%20things%20could%20have%20gone%20better.%0A%0AIf%20all%20five%20Istari%20had%20succeeded%20then%20the%20end%20of%20the%20Third%20Age%20could%0Ahave%20been%20much%20better%20indeed.%0A%0ASaruman%20seemed%20interested%20in%20political%20power%20and%20wheeling%20and%20dealing%0Aamong%20Men%20especially.%20With%20his%20base%20in%20Isengard%20it%27s%20not%20unlikely%20that%20a%0Afaithful%20Saruman%20could%20have%20brokered%20a%20just%20and%20lasting%20peace%20between%0Athe%20Rohirrim%20and%20Dunlendings.%20The%20Dunlendings%20could%20then%20have%20been%0Apersuaded%20into%20joining%20the%20coalition%20of%20Western%20forces%20against%20Sauron.%0A%0ARadagast%20could%20conceivably%20have%20struggled%20with%20the%20monstrous%20takeover%20of%0AMirkwood%2C%20mobilizing%20Ents%20and%20other%20good%20creatures%20to%20resist%20Dol%20Gulder%0Aand%20keeping%20Greenwood%20green.%20Of%20course%20he%20may%20have%20been%20trying%20that%0Aanyway%20and%20failed.%0AIf%20Greenwood%20remained%20a%20hospitable%20place%20it%20would%20have%20strengthened%0AThranduil%20and%20more%20importantly%20allowed%20the%20Northmen%20to%20prosper%20in%20the%0AVale%20of%20Anduin%20and%20the%20southern%20eaves%20of%20Greenwood.%20Some%20significant%0Anations%20could%20have%20arisen%20there%20to%20add%20their%20strength%20to%20the%20fight%0Aagainst%20Sauron.%0A%0AIn%20the%20East%20and%20South%2C%20Alatar%20and%20Pallando%20could%20have%20created%20enough%0Aresistance%20that%20Sauron%20loyalists%20were%20tied%20down%20defending%20their%20own%0Arealms%20and%20couldn%27t%20send%20much%20strength%20to%20Mordor.%20That%20would%20have%20left%0ASauron%20relying%20almost%20exclusively%20on%20his%20orcs%20to%20provide%20soldiers%20for%0Ahis%20war.%20It%20would%20also%20have%20taken%20a%20lot%20of%20pressure%20off%20Gondor%20during%0Athe%20late%20Third%20Age%2C%20allowing%20for%20a%20much%20stronger%20Gondor%20at%20the%20time%20of%0Athe%20War%20of%20the%20Ring.%0A%0AIf%20we%20get%20really%20optimistic%20we%20could%20also%20say%20that%20Gandalf%2C%20freed%20from%0Atrying%20to%20do%20everyone%27s%20job%2C%20could%20focus%20more%20on%20rallying%20all%20races%20to%0Aoppose%20Sauron%20together.%20It%27s%20not%20impossible%20that%20he%20could%20have%20been%0Aavailable%20to%20support%20Balin%27s%20retaking%20of%20Moria%2C%20now%20with%20help%20from%0ALorien%20and%20a%20friendly%20Dunland.%20With%20Elves%20of%20Lorien%20and%20Rivendell%2C%20Men%0Afrom%20Dunland%20and%20a%20secure%2C%20vitalized%20Vale%20of%20Anduin%20and%20Dwarves%20in%20Moria%0Aall%20acting%20together%2C%20the%20orcs%20of%20the%20Misty%20Mountains%20could%20be%20kept%20in%0Acheck%2C%20posing%20little%20or%20no%20threat%20to%20the%20West.%0A%0AAll%20this%20being%20the%20case%2C%20the%20tables%20are%20now%20turned%20on%20Sauron%20in%20a%20big%0Away.%20A%20broken%20and%20divided%20East%20and%20South%20would%20be%20facing%20a%20secure%20and%0Aunited%20West%20and%20North.%20Gondor%20and%20its%20allies%20could%20then%20have%20considered%0Aa%20march%20on%20Mordor%20in%20earnest%2C%20not%20just%20as%20a%20ploy%20to%20distract%20Sauron.%0AAfter%20the%20fall%20of%20Mordor%2C%20Alatar%20and%20Pallando%27s%20pro-Valar%20factions%20could%0Ahave%20asserted%20themselves%20and%20created%20just%20societies%20free%20of%20Gondor%27s%0Ayoke.%20Dunland%20would%20similarly%20be%20a%20free%20nation%2C%20as%20would%20the%20populous%0Aand%20prosperous%20nations%20of%20Anduin%20Vale%20and%20Greenwood.%20The%20Fourth%20Age%0Awould%20start%20in%20peace%20rather%20than%20in%20bloodshed%20as%20Gondor%20and%20Arnor%20tried%0Ato%20re-establish%20an%20empire.%0A%0AOf%20course%20the%20Ring%20could%20have%20totally%20unpredictable%20consequences%20that%0Amake%20a%20mockery%20of%20all%20this%20optimism.%20Still%2C%20that%27s%20my%20%20best%20case%0Ascenario%20FWIW.%0A%0ATrade.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Jeff%20Blanks%20wrote:%0A%0AAt%20the%20risk%20of%20sounding%20dense%2C%20is%20there%20an%20LotR%20link%3F%0A%0AAndrew%0A--%0AAndrew%20Wells%0AReplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
