Just%20wondering...%0ASomeone%20asked%20me%20once%20whether%20the%20Istari%20were%20always%20old%20men%20or%20if%20they%20were%0Ayoung%20when%20they%20arrived.%20From%20reading%20the%20appendix%20of%20tlotr%20as%20well%20as%20the%0ASil%20it%20seems%20that%20they%20were%20always%20%27old%20in%20body%20although%20vigorous%27.%0AHowever%2C%20in%20UT%20%28essay%20on%20Istari%29%20it%20refers%20to%20Saruman%20having%20%27Raven%20hair%27.%0AIn%20modern%20terminology%20this%20refers%20to%20black%20hair.%20Did%20Sauman%20originally%20have%0Ablack%20hair%3F%20or%20is%20Tolkien%20using%20an%20older%20meaning%20of%20%27raven%27%3F%0AIt%20seems%20that%20the%20Istari%20were%20%27always%20old%27%20and%20they%20only%20aged%20in%20terms%20of%0Athe%20burdens%20and%20weariness%20they%20carried%20over%20the%20long%20years%2C%20in%20much%20the%20same%0Away%20that%20Bilbo%20noticed%20the%20change%20in%20Gandalf%2C%20since%20the%20last%20time%20he%20seen%0Ahim%20%28in%20tlotr%29.%20However%2C%20Saruman%27s%20hair%20changing%20colour%20seems%20a%20change%20too%0Afar%2C%20so%20I%20imagine%20that%20the%20UT%20description%20of%20Raven%20hair%20is%20indeed%20an%20older%0Aterm%20used%20to%20describe%20white%20hair.%0A%0AAny%20thought%3F%0A%0ARegards%2C%0ADouglas%0A%0A%0A--%0A-----------------------------------------------%0A%27Drive%20away%20and%20try%20to%20keep%20smiling.%20Get%20a%20little%20rock%20and%20roll%20on%20the%20radio%0Aand%20go%20toward%20all%20the%20life%20there%20is%20with%20all%20the%20courage%20you%20can%20find%20and%0Aall%20the%20belief%20you%20can%20muster.%20Be%20true%2C%20be%20brave%2C%20stand.%20All%20the%20rest%20is%0Adarkness.%27%0AStephen%20King%27s%20IT%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Karl-%20Peder%20Sj%F8m%E6ling%20wrote:%0A%20%3E%20Is%20the%20Silmarillion%20really%20worth%20reading%3F%0A%20%3E%0AOf%20course:%20but%20it%20isn%27t%20an%20%2Aeasy%2A%20read%2C%20IMO.%20Don%27t%20expect%20it%20to%20be%20like%0ALotR:%20it%27s%20very%20different.%20But%2C%20if%20you%20have%20a%20real%20interest%20in%0AMiddle-earth%2C%20and%20want%20to%20understand%20the%20references%20to%20the%20Eldar%20days%0A%28Melkor%2C%20Sauron%20before%20he%20was%20the%20Dark%20Lord%2C%20Beren%20and%20Luthien%2C%20what%0Areally%20is%20in%20the%20West%20and%20other%20stuff%29%20then%20by%20all%20means%20read%20it%2C%20as%20all%0Athe%20questions%20will%20be%20answered%20%28and%20many%20more%20will%20replace%20them%21%29.%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Kevin%20Elliott%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ALOL%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20Sorry%2C%20I%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%0A%7C%2F%20have%20nothing%20%20%20%7C%0A%7C%20more%20to%20say...%20%2F%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A
Linards%20Ticmanis%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3Cbfnd63$1ic60$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0A%0AThis%20is%20the%20first%20I%20have%20heard%20of%20it%20and%20I%20don%27t%20own%20a%20copy%20so%20I%0Acouldn%27t%20say%20for%20certain.%20%20However%2C%20I%20skimmed%20the%20reviews%20at%20Amazon%0Aand%20they%20all%20seemed%20to%20be%20positive%20except%20one%2C%20and%20even%20that%20didn%27t%0Amention%20anything%20about%20missing%20text%3B%0A%0A%22I%20found%20Mr.%20Inglis%27%20voice%20characterizations%20to%20be%20poorly%20conceived%0Aand%20executed%2C%20and%20consequently%20this%20audiobook%20pales%20when%20compared%20to%0Athe%20two%20fully%20dramatized%20versions%20of%20The%20Hobbit%20by%20Minds%20Eye%20and%20the%0ABBC%2C%20both%20beautifully%20realized.%20I%20grant%20that%20this%20is%20an%20unabridged%0Areading%2C%20not%20a%20dramatization%2C%20but%20for%20an%20example%20of%20how%20the%0Acharacterizations%20could%20have%20been%20accomplished%2C%20and%20for%20sheer%0Alistening%20pleasure%20you%20must%20compare%20this%20to%20the%20Harry%20Potter%20audio%0Abooks%20read%20by%20Jim%20Dale.%20Jim%20Dale%20brings%20the%20characters%20to%20life%20in%20his%0Areading%20with%20amazingly%20diverse%20voice%20characterizations%2C%20speech%0Aaffectations%2C%20differing%20accents%20and%20pacing%2C%20such%20that%20the%20voices%0Areally%20suit%20the%20characters.%20In%20comparison%2C%20Mr.%20Inglis%20has%20a%20very%0Anarrow%20range%20of%20voice%20characterizations%2C%20and%20to%20my%20taste%20his%0Acharacterizations%20were%20distinctly%20amateurish%2C%20flat%20and%20one-dimensional%0Areally%2C%20which%20was%20surprising%20in%20light%20of%20his%20Shakespearian%20credentials%0Aand%20disappointing%20after%20my%20experience%20with%20the%20triumph%20that%20Jim%20Dale%0Abrought%20us%20in%20the%20Potter%20series.%20In%20addition%20there%20are%20some%20rather%0Ahorrible%20errors%20which%20should%20have%20been%20caught%2C%20and%20these%20now%20seem%0Atelling%20in%20the%20overall%20sparkless%2C%20indifferent%20and%20uninspired%0Aperformance%20of%20this%20classic.%20An%20example%20of%20one%20such%20error:%0A%22Confusticate%20and%20bebother%20those%20dwarves%21%22%2C%20which%20was%20flubbed%20by%0AInglis%2C%20saying%20%22Confiscate%22%20instead%20of%20%22Confusticate%22.%20It%20is%20possible%0Athat%20Mr.%20Inglis%20thought%20to%20correct%20the%20text%2C%20as%20there%20is%20really%20no%0Asuch%20word%20as%20Confusticate%2C%20nor%20%22Eleventy-One%22%20for%20that%20matter%2C%20but%0Athis%20may%20also%20underscore%20Mr.%20Inglis%27%20ill-suited%20understanding%20of%20The%0AHobbit.%22%0A%0A%0AGiven%20the%20lack%20of%20other%20comment%20about%20text%20missing%20I%27d%20suspect%20that%0Ayour%20CD%20is%20just%20%27skipping%27%20or%20otherwise%20defective%20in%20some%20way.%0A%0A%0A
Linards%20Ticmanis%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3Cbfnsl9$1ht7q$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AYup%2C%20the%20actual%20text%20is%3B%0A%0A%22In%202509%20Celebrian%20wife%20of%20Elrond%20was%20journeying%20to%20Lorien%20when%20she%0Awas%20waylaid%20in%20the%20Redhorn%20Pass%2C%20and%20her%20escort%20being%20scattered%20by%20the%0Asudden%20assault%20of%20the%20Orcs%2C%20she%20was%20seized%20and%20carried%20off.%20She%20was%0Apursued%20and%20rescued%20by%20Elladan%20and%20Elrohir%2C%20but%20not%20before%20she%20had%0Asuffered%20torment%20and%20had%20received%20a%20poisoned%20wound.%20She%20was%20brought%0Aback%20to%20Imladris%2C%20and%20though%20healed%20in%20body%20by%20Elrond%2C%20lost%20all%0Adelight%20in%20Middle-earth%2C%20and%20the%20next%20year%20went%20to%20the%20Havens%20and%0Apassed%20over%20Sea.%22%0ARotK%2C%20Appendix%20A%0A%0A%0A
Louis%20Epstein%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0AI%20note%20with%20great%20delight%20that%20in%20the%20WORLDWIDE%20all-time%20gross%20charts%2C%0AThe%20Fellowship%20of%20the%20Ring%20is%20still%20sitting%20at%20%237%20and%20The%20Two%20Towers%0Ais%20%235.%20Nemo%20is%20currently%20at%20%2374%2C%20but%20will%20no%20doubt%20rise%20higher%20as%20it%0Ais%20released%20in%20other%20countries.%20And%20good%20on%20it%2C%20I%20hear%20it%27s%20a%20great%0Amovie.%0A%0A%0AToo%20late%20for%20that%3B%20there%20are%20thousands...maybe%20even%20millions...of%0Apeople%20out%20there%20who%20will%20see%20the%20movies%20and%20never%20read%20the%20books.%0AWhatever%20will%20we%20do%3F%20Maybe......get%20over%20it%3F%3F%20:-%29%0A%0ACheers%2C%0A%0ASimon%0A%0A%0A
Luminaria%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A:%20%22SiFi%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0A:%20news:41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%20I%20don%27t%20think%20Harrowdale%20is%20mentioned%20in%20the%20movie%20is%20it%3F%20Gandalf%0A:%3E%20advises%20riding%20out%20to%20meet%20Saruman%27s%20army%20while%20Theoden%20decides%20to%20go%0A:%3E%20to%20Helms%20Deep%20and%20make%20a%20stand%20there.%0A%0A:%20In%20the%20film%2C%20Theoden%20wants%20to%20take%20the%20people%20%22into%20the%20hills%22%20and%20mentions%0A:%20that%20his%20people%20have%20hidden%20there%20before%2C%20in%20the%20distant%20past.%20Where%20else%0A:%20could%20he%20mean%2C%20but%20Harrowdale%3F%20When%20Gandalf%20and%20Aragorn%20disucss%20%22riding%0A:%20out%22%20-%20it%20never%20even%20occured%20to%20me%20that%20they%20mean%20in%20open%20battle%2C%20but%20to%20go%0A:%20to%20Helms%20Deep.%20This%20seems%20to%20have%20been%20Gandalf%27s%20concept%20from%20the%20start.%0A%0ANo.%20%20You%20misunderstood%20the%20scenes%20in%20the%20movie%20entirely.%0AAragorn%20and%20Gandalf%20wanted%20Theoden%20to%20ride%20out%20and%20battle%20Saruman%27s%0Atroops.%20%20I%20just%20happened%20to%20find%20the%20script%20online%0A%0AGandalf:%20This%20is%20but%20a%20taste%20of%20the%20terror%20that%20Saruman%20will%20unleash.%20All%0Athe%20more%20potent%20for%20he%20is%20driven%20mad%20by%20the%20fear%20of%20Sauron.%20Ride%20out%20and%0Ameet%20him%20head%20on.%20Draw%20him%20away%20from%20the%20women%20and%20children.%20You%20must%20fight.%0AAragorn:%20You%20have%202000%20good%20men%20riding%20north%20as%20we%20speak.%20Eomer%20is%20loyal%0Ato%20you.%20His%20men%20will%20return%20and%20fight%20for%20their%20king.%0ATheoden:%20They%20will%20be%20300%20leagues%20from%20here%20by%20now.%20Eomer%20cannot%20help%20us.%0AI%20know%20what%20is%20that%20you%20want%20of%20me.%20But%20I%20would%20not%20bring%20further%20death%0Ato%20my%20people.%20I%20will%20not%20risk%20open%20war.%0AAragorn:%20Open%20war%20is%20upon%20you%2C%20whether%20would%20risk%20it%20or%20not.%0ATheoden:%20When%20last%20I%20looked%2C%20Theoden%2C%20not%20Aragorn%2C%20was%20king%20of%20Rohan.%0AGandalf:%20Then%20what%20is%20the%20king%27s%20decision%3F%0A%5BOutside%20the%20Golden%20Hall%5D%0AHama:%20By%20order%20of%20the%20king%2C%20The%20city%20must%20empty.%20We%20make%20for%20the%20refuge%0Aof%20Helm%27s%20Deep.%20Do%20not%20burden%20yourself%20with%20treasures.%20Take%20only%20what%0Aprovisions%20you%20need.%0AGimli:%20Helm%27s%20Deep%21%20They%20flee%20to%20the%20mountains%20when%20they%20should%20stand%0Aand%20fight.%20Who%20will%20defend%20them%20if%20not%20their%20king%3F%0AAragorn:%20He%20is%20only%20doing%20what%20he%20thinks%20is%20best%20for%20his%20people.%20Helm%27s%20Deep%0Ahas%20saved%20them%20in%20the%20past.%0AGandalf:%20There%20is%20no%20way%20out%20of%20that%20ravine.%20Theoden%20is%20walking%20into%20a%0Atrap.%20He%20thinks%20he%20is%20leading%20them%20to%20safety%20but%20what%20he%27ll%20get%20is%20a%20massacre.%0ATheoden%20has%20a%20strong%20hold%20but%20I%20fear%20for%20him.%20I%20fear%20for%20the%20survival%20of%0ARohan.%20He%20will%20need%20you%20before%20the%20end%20there%20Aragorn.%20The%20people%20of%20Rohan%0Awill%20need%20you.%20The%20defenses%20have%20to%20hold.%0A%0AHelm%27s%20Deep%20is%20explictly%20stated%20as%20the%20King%27s%20desired%20destination%2C%0Aand%20Gandalf%20explicity%20disagrees%20with%20this%20decision.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Maeglin%20L%F3mion%20said:%0A%0AYou%20casting%20yourself%20into%20a%20great%20chasm%20in%20the%20earth%20after%20reading%20about%0AMaedhros%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Maeglin%20L%F3mion%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ATuor%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Marc%20A.%20Moniz%20said:%0A%0AElladan%20and%20Elrohir%2C%20the%20sons%20of%20Elrond%20and%20Celebrian%2C%20were%20also%20twins.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Marie-Lan%20Nguyen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%20Johanna%20Katariina%20Rinne%20%20in%20%3Cbegqbo$m6o$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20scripsit:%0A:%3E%0A:%3E%20I%20think%20I%20remember%20in%20some%20place%20it%20is%20said%20that%20Barad-Dur%20blows%20out%0A:%3E%20poisonous%20fumes%2C%20which%20refers%20to%20the%20clouds%20coming%20out%20of%20the%0A:%3E%20volcano.%0A%0A:%20I%20cannot%20find%20any%20occurrence%20of%20%27poisonous%20fume%27%20in%20LotR.%20But%20there%0A:%20are%20%27foul%20fumes%27%20leaking%20from%20the%20mounds%20of%20slag%20%28which%20are%20later%0A:%20describes%20as%20%27poisonous%27%29%20in%20Mordor%2C%20and%20when%20Frodo%20and%20Sam%20climb%0A:%20Orodruin%2C%20%22the%20air%20was%20full%20of%20fumes%3B%20breathing%20was%20painful%20and%0A:%20difficult%2C%20and%20a%20dizziness%20came%20on%20them%2C%20so%20that%20they%20staggered%20and%0A:%20often%20fell%22.%0A%0ASo%20we%20agree%20that%20the%20air%20in%20general%20in%20Mordor%20was%20breathable%20but%20there%0Awere%20places%20with%20fumes.%20If%20the%20word%20poisonous%20doesn%27t%20fit%20in%20a%20direct%0Aquote%2C%20it%20can%20be%20replaced%20with%20a%20near%20synonyme.%20After%20all%2C%20I%20am%20at%20work%0Awriting%20out%20of%20memory%20and%20have%20to%20put%20in%20%27close%20enough%27%20words%20instead%0Aof%20the%20exact%20ones.%0A%0AJust%20trying%20to%20say%20that%20this%20could%20be%20the%20very%20place%20I%20am%20recalling.%0A%0A--%0A%0A%20Johanna%20Rinne%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20I%20breathe%20fire%2C%20therefore%20I%20am%20a%20dragon.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2A%20%20%20%20%20%2A%2A%2A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%20%20%20%20%20%2A%20%20%20%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2A%20%20%206%20%7C%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%2A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2A_%20%2F%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Michael%20Martin%20wrote:%0A%3Csnips%3E%0A%0AThat%20was%20my%20first-ever%20posting%20to%20the%20Tolkien%20newsgroups%2C%20IIRC.%20%20As%20far%20as%20I%0Acan%20work%20out%2C%20she%20was%20just%20a%20correspondent%20who%20had%20a%20name%20in%20common%20with%0AJRRT%2C%20although%20they%20obviously%20did%20end%20up%20on%20affectionate%20terms.%0A%0AAndrew%0A--%0AAndrew%20Wells%0AReplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Mike%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0AI%27d%20perhaps%20put%20it%20a%20bit%20differently%2C%20but%20essentially%20agree.%0ATolkien%20himself%20had%20a%20problem%20with%20industralisation%20and%0Aespecially%20the%20%27machines%27%2C%20and%20that%20attitude%20did%2C%20IMO%2C%0Ainfluence%20LotR.%0A%0AThe%20more%20primitive%20rural%20and%20sylvan%20ways%20of%20life%20are%0Apresented%20as%20the%20more%20happy%20%28Elves%20and%20Hobbits%20in%20particular%29%0Awhile%20even%20the%20D%FAnedain%20of%20Gondor%27s%20cities%20while%20obviously%0Anobler%20than%20the%20Hobbits%20are%20also%20presented%20as%20less%20happy%2C%0AIMO%20%28more%20carefree%29.%0A%0AAt%20the%20same%20time%20the%20attitudes%20of%20Sauron%20and%20Saruman%20towards%0Athe%20nature%20that%20surrounds%20them%20is%20presented%20in%20terms%20that%0Aare%20reminiscent%20of%20the%20least%20responsible%20among%20the%20great%0Aindustrialists%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20age.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A
Mike%20wrote:%0A%0AHere%20is%20a%20snippet%20from%20a%20letter%20of%20his.%0A%0A%22...Beethoven...cheated%20his%20publishers%2C%20and%20abominably%20ill-treated%20his%0Anephew%3B%20but%20I%20do%20not%20believe%20that%20has%20anything%20to%20do%20with%20his%20music.%0A%0AThen%20there%20are%20some%20more%20significant%20facts%2C%20which%20%2Ahave%2A%20some%20relation%0Ato%20an%20authors%20work%3B%20....%0A%0A....And%20there%20are%20a%20few%20basic%20facts%2C%20which%20however%20drily%20expressed%2C%20are%0Areally%20significant.%20%20For%20instance%20I%20was%20born%20in%201892%20and%20lived%20my%20early%0Ayears%20in%20%22the%20Shire%22%20in%20a%20premechanical%20age.%20%20Or%20more%20important%2C%20I%20am%20a%0AChristian%20%28which%20can%20be%20deduced%20from%20my%20stories%2C%29%20and%20in%20fact%20a%20Roman%0ACatholic.%22%0A%0AThe%20preindustrial%20start%20to%20Tolkiens%20life%20has%20some%20bearing%20on%20his%0Astories.%20%20It%27s%20no%20allegory%2C%20it%20is%20sublegory%20%28what%20lies%20written%20beneath%29%0A%20%20or%20the%20subtext%20of%20his%20work.%20%20Just%20as%20the%20good%20vs%20evil%20theme%20of%20the%0Abook%2C%20absolute%20evil%20in%20Sauron%2C%20is%20a%20common%20christian%20idea%2C%20and%20is%0Asignificant%20to%20what%20he%20wrote.%0A%0AHasan%0A%0A%0A%0A
Morgil%20said:%0A%0AAh%2C%20but%20part%20of%20being%20%22intriguing%22%20is%20the%20mystery%20involved.%20For%20me%2C%20the%20most%0Aintriguing%20character%20has%20always%20been%20Eol.%20Where%20did%20he%20come%20from%3F%20How%2C%20when%2C%0Aand%20why%20did%20he%20come%20to%20Beleriand%3F%20What%2C%20if%20any%2C%20was%20his%20relationship%20to%0AThingol%3F%20And%20true%2C%20he%20wasn%27t%20always%20a%20very%20nice%20guy%2C%20but%20I%20think%20he%20was%0Alargely%20misunderstood...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Morgil%20wrote:%0A%0AEye%20strain%3F%0A%0AAndrew%0A--%0AAndrew%20Wells%0AReplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Terry%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AGroup%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20Hair%20Color%0ANoldor%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20Black%20%2F%20Dark%20brown%0AVanyar%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20Golden%0ATeler%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20Brown%20to%20Black%0ATeleri%20Royal%20House%20%20%20%20%20%20Silver%0A%0AThese%20are%20%27general%20rules%27.%20%20The%20exceptions%20indicated%20in%20the%20texts%20are%3B%0A%0ALuthien:%20A%20Telerin%20royal%20with%20black%20hair%20-%20presumably%20from%20her%20mother%0AMelian%20the%20Maia.%0A%0AMahtan%2C%20Nerdanel%2C%20Amrod%2C%20Amras%20and%20Maedhros:%20Noldor%20with%20red%20hair%0A%28though%20Amrod%27s%20darkened%20with%20age%29.%20%20Mahtan%20was%20the%20original%20anomally%0Aand%20the%20others%20all%20inherited%20it%20from%20him.%0A%0AThranduil%20&%20Legolas%20%28debated%29:%20Teleri%20with%20blond%20hair...%20though%20the%0Areferences%20to%20Legolas%27s%20hair%20color%20are%20unclear.%20%20It%20could%20be%20anything%0Afrom%20blond%20to%20black%20depending%20on%20interpretation.%0A%0AMiriel:%20Noldo%3F%20with%20silver%20hair.%20%20It%20is%20possible%20that%20Miriel%20was%20not%0Aalways%20accounted%20a%20Noldo.%0A%0AIdril%2C%20Glorfindel%2C%20Celegorm%2C%20Finarfin%2C%20Galadriel%2C%20Finrod%2C%20Finduilas%2C%0AAegnor:%20Noldor%20with%20golden%20hair.%20%20Idril%20and%20Finarfin%20each%20inherited%0Athis%20trait%20from%20a%20Vanyar%20mother.%20%20Celegorm%20is%20only%20said%20to%20have%20golden%0Ahair%20in%20some%20passages%20and%20there%20is%20no%20apparent%20source%20for%20it.%20%20We%0Adon%27t%20know%20anything%20about%20Glorfindel%27s%20parentage%20with%20which%20to%0Adetermine%20where%20he%20got%20it.%20%20The%20others%20all%20inherited%20the%20trait%20from%0AFinarfin.%0A%0A%0A
Not%20too%20long%20ago%2C%20several%20people%20suggested%20that%20I%20add%20an%20entry%20to%20the%0AFAQ%20dealing%20with%20%22The%20Ruin%20of%20Doriath%22%20in%20the%20published%0A_Silmarillion_.%20%20I%27ve%20finally%20finished%20it%2C%20but%20as%20you%20can%20see%20below%2C%0Athe%20entry%20deals%20with%20changes%20to%20Silm.%20more%20generally%2C%20and%20only%0Amentions%20the%20Doriath%20material%20as%20a%20special%20case.%20%20Let%20me%20know%20what%20you%0Athink.%20%20%28In%20particular%2C%20this%20may%20well%20be%20the%20longest%20entry%20in%20the%0AFAQ.%20%20If%20there%20are%20elements%20that%20you%20think%20don%27t%20deserve%20to%20be%20here%2C%0AI%27m%20eager%20to%20hear%20it.%29%20%20I%27m%20including%20that%20specific%20entry%20below%20so%20you%0Adon%27t%20have%20to%20go%20hunting%20for%20it%20in%20the%20full%20FAQ%3B%20it%20can%20also%20be%20found%0Afrom%20the%20%22Writing%20of%20the%20Books%22%20section%20of%20the%20Tolkien%20Meta-FAQ%2C%20on%0Athe%20web%20at%20http:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2F.%0A%0A-------%0AIII.A.3.%20How%20does%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20as%20published%20differ%20from%20what%0A%20%20%20%20Tolkien%20intended%3F%0A%0A%20%20%20This%20is%20a%20complicated%20question%20that%20is%20essentially%20unanswerable:%0Adespite%20his%20lifelong%20effort%2C%20Tolkien%20never%20came%20close%20to%20completing%0A_The%20Silmarillion_.%20%20At%20Tolkien%27s%20request%2C%20after%20his%20death%20his%20son%0AChristopher%20%28with%20some%20help%20from%20Guy%20Kay%29%20worked%20to%20%22bring%20the%20work%0Ainto%20publishable%20form%22%3B%20Christopher%20discusses%20the%20difficulties%20involved%0Ain%20the%20book%27s%20Foreword.%20%20To%20understand%20why%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20took%20the%0Aform%20that%20it%20did%20%28any%20why%20it%20is%20rarely%20considered%20%22canonical%22%2C%20as%0Amentioned%20in%20question%20III.A.2%29%2C%20it%20is%20worth%20exploring%20those%20editorial%0Achanges.%20%20%5BThe%20full%20story%20can%20be%20found%20in%20the%20%22History%20of%20Middle-earth%22%0Abooks%2C%20particularly%20_Morgoth%27s%20Ring_%20and%20_The%20War%20of%20the%20Jewels_%0A%28volumes%20X-XI%29.%5D%0A%0A%20%20%20The%20most%20basic%20editorial%20decision%20was%20which%20writings%20to%20include%20in%0Athe%20book%20at%20all.%20%20The%20%22Quenta%20Silmarillion%22%20is%20of%20course%20the%20central%0Atext%2C%20but%20Tolkien%20also%20wrote%20numerous%20associated%20stories%20and%20essays.%0ACharles%20Noad%20explored%20this%20question%20as%20part%20of%20his%20essay%20%22On%20the%0AConstruction%20of%20%27The%20Silmarillion%27%22%20%28published%20in%20_Tolkien%27s%0ALegendarium_%3B%20see%20question%20III.A.5%29%2C%20where%20he%20suggests%20an%20%22outline%20for%0A%27The%20Silmarillion%27%20as%20Tolkien%20may%20have%20intended%20it%22.%20In%20addition%20to%20the%0Atexts%20in%20the%20published%20book%2C%20Noad%20includes%20expanded%20versions%20of%20four%0Astories:%20%22The%20Lay%20of%20Leithian%22%20%28possibly%20in%20poetic%20form%29%2C%20%22Narn%20i%20Chin%0AHurin%22%2C%20%22The%20Fall%20of%20Gondolin%22%2C%20and%20%22Earendil%20the%20Wanderer%22%20%28which%0ATolkien%20never%20even%20fully%20sketched%29.%20%20He%20also%20includes%20five%0A%22Appendices%22:%20writings%20about%20Middle-earth%20and%20its%20inhabitants%20such%20as%0A%22Laws%20and%20Customs%20among%20the%20Eldar%22%20and%20the%20%22Athrabeth%20Finrod%20ah%0AAndreth%22%20%28most%20of%20these%20were%20published%20in%20HoMe%20X-XI%29.%20%20Sadly%2C%20a%20book%20on%0Athis%20plan%20could%20never%20be%20made%20satisfying%20with%20just%20the%20texts%20tht%0ATolkien%20left%20us.%0A%0A%20%20%20Moving%20on%20to%20the%20texts%20that%20were%20actually%20included%20in%20_The%0ASilmarillion_%20as%20published%2C%20there%20were%20three%20types%20of%20problems%20to%0Aovercome.%20%20In%20the%20worst%20cases%2C%20there%20were%20crucial%20gaps%20in%20the%20narrative%0Awhere%20Tolkien%20had%20never%20written%20more%20than%20an%20outline%20of%20the%20story%20%28or%0Awhere%20the%20most%20recent%20version%20was%20hopelessly%20outdated%29.%20Much%20more%0Afrequently%2C%20Tolkien%27s%20years%20of%20revisions%20led%20to%20factual%20inconsistencies%0Abetween%20stories%20written%20at%20various%20times%20%28especially%20between%20writings%0Abefore%20and%20after%20_The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings_%29.%20And%20finally%2C%20Tolkien%27s%0Awritings%20differed%20markedly%20in%20tone%2C%20ranging%20from%20vivid%20narratives%20to%0Aterse%20annals%20to%20philosophical%20essays.%20%20To%20assemble%20a%20single%20text%2C%0Aconsistent%20in%20style%20and%20detail%2C%20from%20such%20a%20range%20of%20source%20material%0Aclearly%20required%20substantial%20editing.%0A%0A%20%20%20Despite%20that%20pessimistic%20assessment%2C%20the%20vast%20majority%20of%20the%0Apublished%20_Silmarillion_%20is%20taken%20directly%20from%20Tolkien%27s%20work%20and%0Aseems%20to%20come%20quite%20close%20to%20what%20he%20intended%2C%20as%20far%20as%20it%20goes.%20%28None%0Aof%20the%20%22expanded%22%20tales%20were%20ever%20completed%2C%20but%20what%20exists%20of%20them%0Acan%20be%20found%20for%20the%20most%20part%20in%20_Unfinished%20Tales_%2C%20_The%20Lays%20of%0ABeleriand_%2C%20and%20the%20other%20%22History%20of%20Middle-earth%22%20books%20mentioned%0Aabove.%29%20%20Still%2C%20mild%20editing%20is%20not%20uncommon%2C%20and%20can%20be%20difficult%20to%0Aidentify%20even%20by%20comparison%20to%20the%20source%20texts%20as%20published%20in%20HoMe.%0AThus%2C%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20is%20often%20not%20treated%20as%20a%20final%20authority%20in%0Ascholarly%20discussions%20of%20Middle-earth.%20%20%28A%20classic%20example%20is%20the%0Amistaken%20ancestry%20of%20Gil-galad%2C%20as%20discussed%20in%20question%20III.B.8.%29%0A%0A%20%20%20The%20greatest%20concern%2C%20of%20course%2C%20comes%20from%20those%20few%20cases%20where%0Alarge%20gaps%20had%20to%20be%20filled%20by%20the%20editors.%20%20This%20happened%20to%20some%0Aextent%20for%20%22Of%20Tuor%20and%20the%20Fall%20of%20Gondolin%22%20and%20%22Of%20the%20Voyage%20of%0AEarendil%20and%20the%20War%20of%20Wrath%22%2C%20but%20the%20most%20substantial%20editorial%0A%22invention%22%20came%20in%20the%20chapter%20%22Of%20the%20Ruin%20of%20Doriath%22.%20%20The%20episode%0Awas%20of%20crucial%20importance%20and%20thus%20could%20not%20be%20left%20out%20or%20glossed%0Aover%2C%20but%20Tolkien%20had%20written%20almost%20no%20description%20of%20the%20event%20since%0A1930%20%28long%20before%20even%20_The%20Hobbit_%20was%20published%29%20and%20the%20mythology%0Ahad%20changed%20drastically%20since%20then.%20%20Moreover%2C%20Tolkien%20was%20never%20happy%0Awith%20some%20aspects%20of%20the%20story%2C%20in%20particular%20with%20the%20question%20of%20how%0Athe%20Dwarves%20could%20invade%20Doriath%20despite%20the%20Girdle%20of%20Melian.%20%20The%0Apublished%20version%20was%20directly%20inspired%20by%20some%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20drafts%20of%0Athe%20tale%20%28those%20which%20seemed%20easiest%20to%20reconcile%20with%20the%20rest%20of%20the%0Astory%29%2C%20but%20was%20essentially%20rewritten%20to%20be%20consistent%20with%20the%20rest%20of%0Athe%20book%20and%20to%20include%20a%20few%20ideas%20from%20Tolkien%27s%20later%20writings.%0AThat%20meant%20some%20major%20changes:%20for%20example%2C%20in%20Tolkien%27s%20own%20drafts%2C%0Athe%20Nauglamir%20did%20not%20exist%20before%20it%20was%20made%20to%20hold%20the%20Silmaril%0A%28out%20of%20raw%20gold%20from%20Nargothrond%29%2C%20and%20Thingol%20was%20not%20slain%20until%20the%0Afull%20Dwarvish%20army%20attacked.%0A%0A%20%20%20In%20his%20comments%20on%20%22Of%20the%20Ruin%20of%20Doriath%22%20%28an%20appendix%20to%20%22The%0ATale%20of%20Years%22%20in%20_The%20War%20of%20the%20Jewels_%29%2C%20Christopher%20Tolkien%0Aconcludes%20with%20the%20regret%20that%20%22the%20undoubted%20difficulties%20could%20have%0Abeen%2C%20and%20should%20have%20been%2C%20surmounted%20without%20so%20far%20overstepping%20the%0Abounds%20of%20the%20editorial%20function.%22%20%20Elsewhere%20in%20that%20book%2C%20at%20the%20end%0Aof%20the%20section%20%22The%20Wanderings%20of%20Hurin%22%2C%20he%20speaks%20of%20other%20omissions%0Aand%20alterations%2C%20and%20says%2C%0A%0A%20%20%20it%20seems%20to%20me%20now%2C%20many%20years%20later%2C%20to%20have%20been%20an%20excessive%0A%20%20%20tampering%20with%20my%20father%27s%20actual%20thought%20and%20intention:%20thus%0A%20%20%20raising%20the%20question%2C%20whether%20the%20attempt%20to%20make%20a%20%27uni
O%20wrote:%0A%0AAnd%20we%20speak%20lllike%20this%20all%20the%20way...%0A%0AArchie%0A%0A--%0A%22I%20have%20told%20my%20sons%20that%20they%20are%20not%20under%20any%0Acircumstances%20to%20take%20part%20in%20massacres%2C%20and%20that%0Athe%20news%20of%20massacres%20of%20enemies%20is%20not%20to%20fill%20them%0Awith%20satisfaction%20or%20glee.%22%0A%0AKurt%20Vonnegut%2C%20_Slaughterhouse-Five_%0A%0A%0A
