On%20Fri%2C%2011%20Jul%202003%2010:17:18%20-0400%2C%0Apawn%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20think%20at%20least%20part%20of%20Sauron%27s%20foresight%20wasn%27t%20foresight%20at%20all.%20%20It%20was%0Asimply%20intelligence.%20%20Gollum%20had%20gone%20as%20far%20as%20Esgaroth%20%28as%20I%20recall%29%2C%20and%0Aall%20of%20this%20would%20have%20been%20learned%20by%20Sauron.%20%20Bilbo%27s%20name%20wasn%27t%20unknown%2C%0Aand%20it%20would%20stand%20to%20reason%20that%20the%20circumstances%20of%20a%20Halfling%20with%20a%0Agroup%20of%20Dwarves%2C%20and%20a%20Halfling%20who%20had%20Gollum%27s%20Ring%2C%20would%20obviously%20mean%0Athat%20an%20attempted%20bribing%20of%20the%20Dwarves%20might%20be%20worthwhile.%0A%0A%0AI%20think%20part%20of%20it%20was%20very%20likely%20that%20the%20Dwarves%20were%20an%20exceedingly%0Asecretive%20people.%20%20The%20only%20people%20they%20generally%20seemed%20historically%20to%0Ahave%20had%20any%20desire%20to%20be%20around%20were%20the%20Noldor%2C%20who%20shared%20many%20interests%0Awith%20them.%20%20Saruman%2C%20in%20his%20pride%2C%20would%20likely%20have%20had%20little%20interest%20in%0Acracking%20any%20secrets%20the%20Dwarves%20might%20hold%2C%20as%20it%20would%20be%20within%20his%0Acharacter%20to%20view%20them%20as%20being%20of%20only%20secondary%20importance.%0A%0AAs%20to%20Sauron%2C%20he%20had%20likely%20known%20of%20Dwarves%20since%20the%20First%20Age%2C%20but%20again%2C%0Ahis%20attempt%20to%20dominate%20the%20Dwarves%20with%20the%20Seven%20had%20generally%20been%20a%0Afailure.%0A%0AAnother%20thought%20comes%20to%20me%20as%20I%27m%20writing%20this%2C%20and%20it%27s%20just%20my%20own%20guess%2C%0Aand%20nothing%20more.%20%20Perhaps%20Saruman%2C%20who%20rather%20fancied%20himself%20the%20expert%20on%0ARings%20of%20Power%20and%20the%20arts%20of%20the%20Enemy%2C%20may%20have%20only%20been%20looking%20where%0Ahe%20perceived%20Sauron%20was%20looking.%20%20Dwarves%20and%20Hobbits%20were%20of%20little%20use%20to%0ASauron%2C%20so%20why%20should%20they%20be%20of%20any%20importance%20to%20Saruman.%20%20Both%20Sauron%20and%0ASaruman%20suffered%20the%20sin%20and%20folly%20of%20pride.%0A%0APerhaps%20Saruman%20could%20have%20profited%20from%20a%20relationship%20with%20fellow%20Auleans%0A%28so%20to%20speak%29%2C%20but%20it%20likely%20never%20seemed%20of%20any%20great%20importance%20to%20do%20so.%0AThey%20weren%27t%20all%20that%20important%20to%20Sauron%2C%20save%20perhaps%20the%20recovery%20of%20what%0Aremained%20of%20the%20Seven%2C%20and%20once%20those%20were%20recovered%2C%20the%20Dwarves%2C%20for%20the%0Amost%20part%2C%20ceased%20to%20play%20a%20great%20role.%20%20They%20might%20have%20a%20few%20wars%20with%0AOrcs%2C%20but%20Sauron%20seems%20to%20have%20had%20no%20lack%20of%20Orcs.%20%20So%2C%20if%20Sauron%20cared%0Alittle%20for%20Dwarves%2C%20why%20should%20Saruman%20the%20Wise%3F%20%20By%20the%20time%20Sauron%20showed%0Aany%20interest%2C%20it%20was%20only%20to%20try%20to%20bribe%20%28and%20threaten%29%20some%20information%0Aout%20of%20them.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
