On%20Mon%2C%2028%20Jul%202003%2003:36:32%20GMT%2C%0ASLJ%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AThe%20Elves%20are%20immortal.%20%20They%20go%20to%20Mandos%2C%20and%20after%20a%20time%20are%20permitted%0Ato%20return%20re-embodied.%20%20The%20conception%20changed%20somewhat%20over%20the%20years.%20%20I%0Abelieve%20it%20started%20with%20them%20being%20reborn%20as%20children%20and%20then%2C%20as%20they%20got%0Aolder%2C%20they%20would%20come%20to%20resemble%20their%20old%20selves%20and%20remember%20who%20they%0Awere.%20%20The%20later%20conception%20was%20that%20the%20Valar%20aided%20them%20in%20being%0Are-embodied.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20if%20you%20desire%20references...%0A%0A%22For%20Elves%20die%20not%20till%20the%20world%20dies%2C%20unless%20they%20are%20slain%20or%20waste%20in%0Agrief%20%28and%20to%20both%20these%20seeming%20deaths%20they%20are%20subject%29%3B%20neither%20does%20age%0Asubdue%20their%20strength%2C%20unless%20one%20grow%20weary%20of%20ten%20thousand%20centuries%3B%20and%0Adying%20they%20are%20gathered%20to%20the%20halls%20of%20Mandos%20in%20Valinor%2C%20%2Awhence%20they%20may%0Ain%20time%20return%2A.%22%0AThe%20Silmarillion%20-%20Of%20the%20Beginning%20of%20Days%0A%0A%22When%20%27killed%27%2C%20by%20the%20injury%20or%20destruction%20of%20their%20incarnate%20form%2C%20they%0A%5BElves%5D%20do%20not%20escape%20from%20time%2C%20but%20remain%20in%20the%20world%2C%20either%0Adisincarnate%2C%20or%20being%20re-born.%22%0ALetter%20%23181%0A%0AThis%20is%20a%20fundemental%20conception%20of%20the%20mythology%3B%20that%20the%20First%20Born%20are%0Alinked%20to%20Arda%2C%20and%20exist%20as%20long%20as%20it%20exists.%20%20Tolkien%20himself%20used%20the%0Aterm%20%22serial%20immortality%22%2C%20meaning%20of%20course%2C%20that%20upon%20death%2C%20and%20after%0Asufficient%20time%20in%20Mandos%2C%20they%20can%20again%20be%20incarnated.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
On%20Mon%2C%2028%20Jul%202003%2013:08:17%20-0400%2C%0AGonzalo%20Diethelm%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AYou%20will%20have%20to%20wait%20until%20I%20get%20home.%20%20I%27m%20pretty%20sure%20it%27s%20in%20the%0Apublished%20Silmarillion%2C%20but%20it%20could%20be%20in%20HoME.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
On%20Mon%2C%204%20Aug%202003%2017:43:20%20+0000%20%28UTC%29%2C%0APaul%20Ciszek%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20think%20he%27s%20taking%20this%20from%20the%20statement%20that%20of%20all%20the%20creatures%20of%0AMiddle%20Earth%2C%20only%20the%20Elves%20were%20united%20against%20Sauron.%20%20This%20seems%20to%0Aindicate%2C%20if%20you%20want%20to%20take%20that%20extra%20leap%2C%20that%20there%20were%20Dwarves%20who%0Afought%20for%20Sauron.%0A%0AI%27m%20not%20saying%20it%20isn%27t%20true%2C%20though%20there%20is%20no%20direct%20citation%20that%20I%20am%0Aaware%20of%20that%20states%20some%20Dwarves%20fought%20on%20Sauron%27s%20side.%20%20My%20only%20problem%0Awith%20taking%20what%20I%20figure%20to%20be%20a%20more%20symbolic%20statement%20is%20that%20it%20leads%0Ato%20an%20obvious%20question.%20%20Were%20there%20Ents%20who%20fought%20on%20the%20side%20of%20Sauron%3F%0AFor%20myself%20at%20least%2C%20I%20doubt%20it%20very%20highly.%20%20So%20it%20seems%20clear%20that%20this%0Astatement%20was%20not%20precisely%20literal%2C%20which%20could%20leave%20the%20door%20open%20for%20no%0ADwarves%20to%20have%20served%20Sauron.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20there%20is%20the%20fact%20that%20six%20of%20the%20Seven%20did%20make%20it%20to%20Dwarf%20kings%0Avia%20Sauron.%20%20Whether%20they%20were%20unaware%20that%20the%20Noldor%20had%20discovered%20the%0Aidentity%20of%20Annatar%20is%20an%20open%20question.%20%20It%20isn%27t%20necessary%20that%20the%0ADwarves%20to%20have%20actually%20fought%20for%20Sauron%20to%20gain%20the%20Rings.%20%20My%20hunch%20is%0Athat%20doling%20out%20the%20Nine%20and%20the%20Seven%20was%20a%20sort%20of%20hastily%20thought%20up%20Plan%0AB.%20%20If%20he%20couldn%27t%20dominate%20the%20Noldor%2C%20then%20he%27d%20try%20Men%20and%20Dwarves.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20the%20question%20of%20Durin%27s%20ring%20is%20more%20complicated.%20%20Khazad-dum%20and%0AEregion%20were%20in%20close%20proximity%2C%20and%20there%20was%20a%20league%20of%20friendship%0Abetween%20the%20two.%20%20I%20cannot%20see%20Celebrimbor%20not%20warning%20Durin%27s%20people%20that%0Athe%20Lord%20of%20Gifts%20was%20in%20fact%20Gorthaur%20the%20Terrible%2C%20chief%20servant%20of%0AMorgoth.%20%20So%20Durin%20could%20not%20have%20received%20a%20Ring%20of%20Power%20from%20Sauron.%0AThat%20leaves%20only%20Celebrimbor%20giving%20the%20ring%20to%20Durin%20at%20some%20earlier%20point.%0AMaybe%20it%20was%20a%20gift%2C%20maybe%20it%20was%20for%20safe-keeping.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
On%20Mon%2C%207%20Jul%202003%2021:39:03%20+0100%2C%0AAndrew%20Wells%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AThese%20positions%20held%20a%20little%20weight%2C%20I%20suppose%2C%20but%20mainly%2C%20it%20appears%2C%0Aduring%20times%20of%20emergency.%20%20The%20rest%20of%20the%20time%2C%20outside%20of%20the%20Took%20and%0ABrandybuck%20clans%2C%20these%20positions%20had%20little%20weight%20in%20the%20rest%20of%20the%0AShire.%0A%0A%0A%0ABilbo%20owned%20some%20nice%20real-estate%2C%20but%20nowhere%20do%20I%20see%20any%20reference%20to%0Ahim%2C%20or%20to%20Frodo%20after%20him%2C%20owning%20large%20tracts%20of%20land.%20%20There%20is%20no%0Amention%20of%20indentured%20servants%2C%20or%20anything%20resembling%20them.%20%20It%27s%20difficult%0Ato%20say%20how%20exactly%20the%20Shire%27s%20economic%20system%20worked%2C%20but%20if%20Farmer%20Maggot%0Ais%20any%20indication%2C%20the%20farmers%20appear%20to%20have%20owned%20their%20own%20land.%20%20While%0Acertainly%20there%20were%20richer%20and%20poorer%20families%2C%20I%20see%20no%20evidence%20of%20a%0Awealthy%20land-owning%20class%2C%20a%20gentry%20if%20you%20will.%20%20If%20there%20was%20a%20class%0Asystem%2C%20it%20was%20pretty%20loose%20and%20didn%27t%20seem%20to%20infer%20any%20special%20rights%20of%0Aany%20kind.%20%20Certainly%20the%20position%20of%20Thain%20became%20very%20important%20in%20moments%0Aof%20crisis%2C%20but%20that%20didn%27t%20seem%20to%20translate%20into%20anything%20other%20than%20mild%0Adeference%20in%20times%20of%20peace.%0A%0AIn%20fact%2C%20it%27s%20darn%20hard%20to%20see%20how%20there%20was%20any%20meaningful%20centralized%0Agovernment%20at%20all.%20%20It%20seems%20likely%20that%20other%20clans%3B%20like%20the%20Tooks%20and%0ABrandybucks%2C%20may%20have%20had%20a%20chieftain%20of%20sorts%2C%20but%20his%20or%20her%20authority%0Acertainly%20didn%27t%20extend%20to%20unrelated%20families.%20%20Obviously%20there%20were%20a%20few%0Athings%2C%20like%20border%20defense%20and%20the%20post%2C%20that%20required%20some%20form%20of%0Aauthority%2C%20but%20beyond%20that%20we%20see%20none%20of%20the%20usual%20things%20applied%20to%20landed%0Agentry%20and%20agricultural%20aristocracy.%20%20If%20I%20recall%2C%20the%20folks%20of%20the%20Marish%0Aheld%20the%20Brandybucks%20in%20some%20esteem%2C%20but%20I%20don%27t%20really%20see%20that%20that%20meant%0Athey%20took%20their%20marching%20orders%20from%20them.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
On%20Sat%2C%2002%20Aug%202003%2016:18:47%20-0400%2C%0ABob%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AFirst%20of%20all%2C%20the%20Rings%20of%20Power%20really%20weren%27t%20meant%20for%20Dwarves%20or%20Men.%0AIt%20was%20Sauron%20who%20doled%20them%20out%20after%20he%20had%20captured%20the%20Nine%20and%20the%0ASeven.%0A%0ASecond%20of%20all%2C%20no%20one%20knew%20that%20Annatar%20was%20actually%20Sauron.%20%20Some%2C%20like%0AGil-galad%2C%20had%20misgivings%2C%20but%20Sauron%20could%20still%20appear%20in%20a%20fair%20form.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
On%20Sat%2C%2005%20Jul%202003%2004:35:25%20-0700%2C%0Acoyotes%20rand%20mair%20fheal%20greykitten%20tomys%20des%20anges%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0AThere%20were%20plenty%20of%20prideful%20people%20in%20the%20Silmarillion.%20%20I%20can%27t%20recall%0Aanyone%20else%20other%20than%20the%20Children%20of%20Hurin%20who%20Morgoth%20actively%20tried%20to%0Amake%20their%20lives%20a%20living%20hell.%20%20He%20had%20his%20faults%2C%20but%20then%20again%20things%0Afrequently%20went%20awry%20for%20him.%20%20We%27d%20all%20be%20miserable%20bastards%20if%20we%20were%20in%0Ahis%20shoes.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
