On%20Wed%2C%2009%20Jul%202003%2005:21:33%20GMT%2C%0ARobert%20J.%20Kolker%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%22They%20had%20trudged%20for%20more%20than%20an%20hour%20when%20they%20heard%20a%20sound%20that%20brought%0Athem%20to%20a%20halt.%20%20Unbelievable%2C%20but%20unmistakable.%20%20Water%20trickling.%20%20Out%20of%20a%0Agully%20on%20the%20left%2C%20so%20sharp%20and%20narrow%20that%20it%20looked%20as%20if%20the%20black%20cliff%0Ahad%20been%20cloven%20by%20some%20huge%20axe%2C%20water%20came%20dripping%20down:%20the%20last%0Aremains%2C%20maybe%2C%20of%20some%20sweet%20rain%20gathered%20from%20sunlit%20seas%2C%20but%20ill-fated%0Ato%20fall%20at%20last%20upon%20the%20walls%20of%20the%20Black%20Land%20and%20wander%20fruitless%20down%0Ainto%20the%20dust.%20%20Here%20it%20came%20out%20of%20the%20rock%20in%20a%20little%20falling%20streamlet%2C%0Aand%20flowed%20across%20the%20path%2C%20and%20turning%20south%20ran%20away%20swiftly%20to%20be%20lost%0Aamong%20the%20dead%20stones.%22%0A%0A%22Sam%20Sprang%20towards%20it.%20%20%27If%20ever%20I%20see%20the%20Lady%20again%2C%20I%20will%20tell%20her%21%27%20he%0Acried.%20%20%27Light%20and%20now%20water%21%27%20%20Then%20he%20stopped.%20%20%27Let%20me%20drink%20first%2C%20Mr.%0AFrodo.%27%20he%20said.%22%0A%0A%22%27All%20right%2C%20but%20there%27s%20room%20enough%20for%20two.%27%22%0A%0A%22%27I%20didn%27t%20mean%20that%2C%27%20said%20Sam%2C%20%27I%20mean:%20if%20it%27s%20poisonous%2C%20or%20something%0Athat%20will%20show%20its%20badness%20quick%2C%20well%2C%20better%20me%20than%20you%2C%20master%2C%20if%20you%0Aunderstand%20me.%27%22%0A%0A%22%27I%20do.%20%20But%20I%20think%20we%27ll%20trust%20our%20luck%20together%2C%20Sam%3B%20or%20our%20blessing.%0AStill%2C%20be%20careful%20now%2C%20if%20it%27s%20very%20cold%21%27%22%0A%0A%22The%20water%20was%20cool%20but%20not%20icy%2C%20and%20it%20had%20an%20unpleasant%20taste%2C%20at%20once%0Abitter%20and%20oily%2C%20or%20so%20they%20would%20have%20said%20at%20home...%22%0A%0ARotK%2C%20%22The%20Land%20of%20Shadow%22%0A%0A----%0A%0AYou%20seem%20to%20be%20confusing%20Mordor%20with%20the%20Morgul%20Vale.%20%20Faramir%20tells%20Frodo%0Ain%20%22Journey%20to%20the%20Crossroads%22%20%28in%20TTT%29:%0A%0A%22You%20will%20have%20no%20lack%20of%20water%20as%20you%20walk%20in%20Ithilien%2C%20but%20do%20not%20drink%20of%0Aany%20stream%20that%20flows%20from%20Imlad%20Morgul%2C%20the%20Valley%20of%20Living%20Death.%22%0A%0A----%0A%0ALater%2C%20when%20Frodo%2C%20Sam%20and%20Smeagol%20are%20climbing%20the%20stairs%20of%20Cirith%20Ungol%2C%0Athere%20is%20this%20exchange%2C%20which%20I%20this%20passage%20and%20the%20passage%20I%20just%20quoted%0Afrom%20%22Journey%20to%20the%20Crossroads%22%20are%20what%20you%20are%20confusing%20with%20Mordor.%0A%0A%22%27I%20wonder%20when%20we%27ll%20find%20water%20again%3F%22%20said%20Sam.%20%20%22But%20I%20suppose%20even%20over%0Athere%20they%20drink%3F%20%20Orcs%20drink%2C%20don%27t%20they%3F%27%22%0A%0A%22%27Yes%2C%20they%20drink%2C%27%20said%20Frodo%2C%20%27But%20do%20not%20let%20us%20speak%20of%20that.%20%20Such%0Adrink%20is%20not%20for%20us.%27%22%0A%0A%22%27Then%20all%20the%20more%20need%20to%20fill%20our%20bottles%2C%27%20said%20Sam.%20%20%27But%20there%20isn%27t%0Aany%20water%20up%20her:%20not%20a%20sound%20or%20a%20trickle%20have%20I%20heard.%20%20And%20anyway%20Faramir%0Asaid%20we%20were%20not%20to%20drink%20any%20water%20in%20Morgul.%27%22%0A%0A%22%27No%20water%20flowing%20out%20of%20Imlad%20Morgul%2C%20were%20his%20words.%27%20said%20Frodo.%20%20%27We%0Aare%20not%20in%20that%20valley%20now%2C%20and%20if%20we%20came%20on%20a%20spring%20it%20would%20be%20flowing%0Ainto%20it%20and%20not%20out%20of%20it.%27%22%0A%0ATTT%2C%20%22The%20Stairs%20of%20Cirith%20Ungol%22%0A%0AI%20recall%20no%20passages%20warning%20against%20water%20in%20Mordor.%20%20Besides%2C%20the%20Sea%20of%0ANurnen%20lays%20within%20Mordor%2C%20and%20we%20are%20told%20that%20there%20were%20fields%20there%0Awhere%20Sauron%27s%20slaves%20and%20servants%20grew%20food.%0A%0A--%0AAaron%20Clausen%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A
