Quoth%20%22A%20Tsar%20Is%20Born%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3Cf2cXa.5458$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0ACongratulations.%20%20You%27ve%20contacted%20the%20author%20of%20that%20FAQ%2C%20and%20he%0Athanks%20you%20for%20the%20compliment.%20:%29%20%20%28At%20least%2C%20I%20_think_%20you%27re%0Areferring%20to%20one%20of%20my%20FAQs...%20see%20below.%29%0A%0A%0AWhich%20FAQ%20exactly%20quotes%20you%20by%20address%3F%20%20%28If%20it%27s%20not%20the%20Meta-FAQ%2C%0ANewsgroup%20FAQ%2C%20Tolkien%20FAQ%2C%20or%20Tolkien%20LessFAQ%2C%20I%27ll%20need%20to%20point%20you%0Ato%20someone%20else.%29%20%20Can%20you%20give%20an%20exact%20URL%20and%20perhaps%20a%20question%0Anumber%3F%20%20I%20just%20searched%20through%20the%20full%20text%20source%20for%20email%0Aaddresses%20%28well%2C%20for%20%22@%22%20signs%29%2C%20and%20I%20didn%27t%20see%20any%20address%20that%0Alooked%20like%20your%20current%20one.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20the%20only%20place%20where%20I%27ve%0Afound%20addresses%20that%20I%20don%27t%20know%20personally%20is%20the%20%22Acknowledgements%22%0Asection%20of%20the%20Loos%20FAQ%20and%20LessFAQ.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22Gregg%20Cattanach%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CkxkMa.2197$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0AHmm.%20%20In%20%22The%20Ring%20Goes%20South%22%2C%20as%20the%20blizzard%20begins%2C%20we%20read%0A%0A%20%20%20%22I%20wonder%20if%20this%20is%20a%20contrivance%20of%20the%20Enemy%2C%22%20said%20Boromir.%0A%20%20%20%22They%20say%20in%20my%20land%20that%20he%20can%20govern%20the%20storms%20in%20the%20Mountains%0A%20%20%20of%20Shadow%20that%20stand%20upon%20the%20borders%20of%20Mordor.%20He%20has%20strange%0A%20%20%20powers%20and%20many%20allies.%22%0A%0A%20%20%20%22His%20arm%20has%20grown%20long%20indeed%2C%22%20said%20Gimli%2C%20%22if%20he%20can%20draw%20snow%0A%20%20%20down%20from%20the%20North%20to%20trouble%20us%20here%20three%20hundred%20leagues%20away.%22%0A%0A%20%20%20%22His%20arm%20has%20grown%20long%2C%22%20said%20Gandalf.%0A%0AWe%20never%20really%20learn%20what%20the%20cause%20of%20that%20blizzard%20was%2C%20but%20its%20odd%0Abehavior%20%28easing%20when%20the%20Fellowship%20stopped%20advancing%2C%20for%20example%29%0Aat%20least%20suggests%20that%20it%20wasn%27t%20entirely%20natural.%20%20Moreover%2C%0AGandalf%27s%20words%20here%20almost%20sound%20like%20he%20is%20contradicting%20Gimli%27s%0Adoubts%20and%20confirming%20Boromir%27s%20suspicion.%20%20At%20the%20very%20least%2C%20the%20men%0Aof%20Gondor%20believed%20that%20Sauron%20could%20control%20the%20weather%20near%20Mordor%2C%0Athough%20one%20could%20always%20blame%20that%20on%20superstition.%0A%0ABut%20far%20more%20to%20the%20point%20is%20the%20statement%20right%20at%20the%20beginning%20of%0A%22The%20Battle%20of%20the%20Pelennor%20Fields%22%2C%20referring%20to%20the%20Witch%20King:%0A%0A%20%20%20%22The%20darkness%20was%20breaking%20too%20soon%2C%20before%20the%20date%20that%20his%0A%20%20%20Master%20had%20set%20for%20it:%20fortune%20had%20betrayed%20him%20for%20the%20moment%2C%20and%0A%20%20%20the%20world%20had%20turned%20against%20him%22%0A%0AIf%20Sauron%20could%20%22set%22%20a%20date%20for%20the%20darkness%20to%20break%2C%20that%20certainly%0Aimplies%20that%20he%20had%20some%20sort%20of%20weather%20control.%20%20That%20control%0Aobviously%20wasn%27t%20absolute%2C%20or%20else%20the%20darkness%20wouldn%27t%20have%20broken%0Aearly.%20Still%2C%20I%27d%20guess%20that%20near%20Mordor%20and%20when%20he%20put%20some%20effort%0Ainto%20it%20he%20_could_%20control%20the%20weather%20reasonably%20reliably%20%28and%20that%0Aonly%20an%20unexpected%20shift%20in%20large-scale%20weather%20patterns%20would%20throw%0Athat%20off.%20%20Heck%2C%20the%20unexpected%20breaking%20of%20the%20clouds%20in%20LotR%20could%0Aeven%20have%20been%20minor%20intervention%20by%20Manwe%20or%20Eru...%20or%20it%20might%20have%0Ajust%20been%20fate%2C%20as%20we%20call%20it%20in%20Middle-earth%20:%29%20%29.%0A%0AMore%20generally%2C%20I%20have%20trouble%20believing%20that%20Sauron%20would%20make%20the%0Atiming%20of%20his%20major%20military%20operations%20dependent%20on%20the%20random%0Achances%20of%20weather:%20it%20just%20seems%20pretty%20silly%20to%20delay%20a%20major%0Aoffensive%20until%20you%27re%2097%25%20confident%20that%20there%20will%20be%20an%20unbroken%0Aweek%20of%20east%20winds.%20:%29%0A%0AAs%20a%20more%20specific%20issue%2C%20there%20are%20several%20indications%20in%20LotR%20that%0ASauron%20sent%20forth%20the%20darkness%20and%20initiated%20his%20attack%20on%20Minas%0ATirith%20as%20a%20direct%20response%20to%20Aragorn%27s%20use%20of%20the%20Palantir.%0A%28Prompting%20Sauron%27s%20strike%20was%20a%20significant%20part%20of%20Aragorn%27s%0Adecision%20to%20use%20the%20Stone%2C%20as%20I%20recall.%29%20%20The%20fact%20that%20Sauron%20was%0Aable%20to%20strike%20within%20a%20few%20days%20of%20that%20event%20makes%20me%20think%20that%20he%0Adidn%27t%20have%20to%20wait%20for%20the%20perfect%20weather%20pattern%20to%20establish%0Aitself.%0A%0AAll%20in%20all%2C%20while%20I%20don%27t%20know%20that%20we%20have%20absolute%20proof%20of%20Sauron%27s%0Aweather-manipulation%20abilities%2C%20I%20think%20there%27s%20a%20lot%20of%20evidence%0Asupporting%20the%20idea.%20%20At%20the%20very%20least%2C%20I%20think%20that%20the%20black%0Agloom%20he%20sent%20over%20Gondor%20was%20entirely%20preplanned.%0A%0A%09%09%09%20%20%20%20%20%20Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22Joe%20Seamour%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3C5gKTa.118165$GL4.31476@rwcrnsc53%3E:%0A%0AElrond%27s%20wife%20was%20Celebrian%2C%20daughter%20of%20Celeborn%20and%20Galadriel.%20%20I%27m%0A99%25%20certain%20that%20she%20isn%27t%20mentioned%20in%20_The%20Hobbit_%20nor%20in%20any%20scene%0Awith%20Bombadil.%20%20She%20is%20mentioned%20a%20couple%20of%20times%20in%20the%20main%20text%20of%0ALotR%2C%20however.%20%20The%20first%20is%20in%20%22Many%20Meetings%22%2C%20when%20we%20read%20that%0AElladan%20and%20Elrohir%20were%20not%20at%20the%20feast%20because%20%22they%20rode%20often%20far%0Aafield%20with%20the%20Rangers%20of%20the%20North%2C%20forgetting%20never%20their%20mother%27s%0Atorment%20in%20the%20dens%20of%20the%20orcs%22.%20%20The%20second%20is%20in%20%22Farewell%20to%0ALorien%22%20when%20Aragorn%20thanks%20Galadriel%2C%20saying%20%22O%20Lady%20of%20Lorien%20of%0Awhom%20were%20sprung%20Celebrian%20and%20Arwen%20Evenstar.%22%0A%0AThe%20most%20complete%20story%20of%20Celebrian%27s%20ordeal%20is%20in%20Appendix%20A.iii%2C%0Ashortly%20after%20the%20death%20of%20Arvedui.%20%20The%20relevant%20passage%20is:%0A%0A%20%20%20%22In%20the%20days%20of%20Arahad%20I%20the%20Orcs%2C%20who%20had%2C%20as%20later%20appeared%2C%20long%0A%20%20%20been%20secretly%20occupying%20strongholds%20in%20the%20Misty%20Mountains%2C%20so%20as%0A%20%20%20to%20bar%20all%20the%20passes%20into%20Eriador%2C%20suddenly%20revealed%20themselves.%0A%20%20%20In%202509%20Celebrian%20wife%20of%20Elrond%20was%20journeying%20to%20Lorien%20when%20she%0A%20%20%20was%20waylaid%20in%20the%20Redhorn%20pass%2C%20and%20her%20escort%20being%20scattered%20by%0A%20%20%20the%20sudden%20assault%20of%20the%20Orcs%2C%20she%20was%20seized%20and%20carried%20off.%0A%20%20%20She%20was%20pursued%20and%20rescued%20by%20Elladan%20and%20Elrohir%2C%20but%20not%20before%0A%20%20%20she%20had%20suffered%20torment%20and%20had%20received%20a%20poisoned%20wound.%20%20She%0A%20%20%20was%20brought%20back%20to%20Imladris%2C%20and%20though%20healed%20in%20body%20by%20Elrond%2C%0A%20%20%20lost%20all%20delight%20in%20Middle-earth%2C%20and%20the%20next%20year%20went%20to%20the%0A%20%20%20Havens%20and%20passed%20over%20Sea.%22%0A%0AIt%27s%20a%20long%20quote%2C%20but%20that%27s%20the%20whole%20story.%20%20I%20don%27t%20think%20that%0Amany%20more%20details%20are%20provided%20elsewhere.%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22Matt%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CXeDPa.36272$N7.4253@sccrnsc03%3E:%0A%0AThe%20only%20discussion%20of%20the%20Maiar%20as%20a%20group%20can%20be%20found%20in%20the%0A%22Valaquenta%22%2C%20which%20is%20the%20second%20text%20in%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20as%0Apublished.%20%20It%20starts%20out%20with%20a%20discussion%20of%20the%20Valar%2C%20but%20there%27s%0Aa%20section%20near%20the%20end%20with%20the%20subtitle%20%22Of%20the%20Maiar%22%20or%20something%0Aclose%20to%20it%20%28only%20the%20section%20on%20%22Enemies%22%20comes%20later%2C%20as%20I%20recall%29.%0AOh%2C%20and%20just%20as%20a%20warning%2C%20I%20don%27t%20think%20the%20name%20%22Gandalf%22%20is%20used%0Athere%20at%20all:%20he%20is%20called%20%22Olorin%22%2C%20which%20you%20may%20recall%20from%0AFaramir%27s%20rhyme%20about%20Gandalf%27s%20many%20names.%0A%0A%5BAs%20a%20trivial%20side%20note%2C%20the%20term%20%22chapter%22%20might%20be%20misleading:%20I%0Awould%20call%20the%20internal%20divisions%20of%20the%20%22Quenta%20Silmarillion%22%20itself%0A%27chapters%27%20%28I%20think%20they%20are%20numbered%20starting%20with%20%221%22%29%2C%20while%0Asections%20like%20the%20%22Valaquenta%22%2C%20the%20%22Akalabeth%22%2C%20and%20the%20%22Quenta%0ASilmarillion%22%20itself%20are%20essentially%20independent%20writings.%5D%0A%0AI%20should%20point%20out%2C%20however%2C%20that%20you%20really%20need%20to%20read%20the%0A%22Ainulindale%22%20to%20understand%20what%20the%20Valar%20and%20Maiar%20fundamentally%0Awere%20%28whether%20the%20Maiar%20are%20discussed%20by%20name%20there%20or%20not%29.%20%20And%20the%0A%22Quenta%20Silmarillion%22%20proper%20also%20mentions%20quite%20a%20few%20Maiar%20%28though%0Anot%20Gandalf%2C%20as%20far%20as%20I%20can%20recall%29.%20%20Gandalf%20is%20also%20mentioned%20in%0A%22Of%20the%20Rings%20of%20Power%20and%20the%20Third%20Age%22%2C%20of%20course%2C%20though%20his%0AMaia-nature%20isn%27t%20the%20focus%20there.%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22Simon%20J.%20Rowe%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AGah.%20%20Is%20there%20some%20dark%20secret%20about%20%22Matt%22%20that%20I%20don%27t%20know%2C%20one%0Athat%20is%20inspiring%20multiple%20people%20to%20be%20impolite%20to%20him%3F%20%20First%20of%0Aall%2C%20people%20read%20at%20different%20rates%20just%20naturally.%20%20I%20have%20at%20least%0Aone%20friend%20who%20reads%20at%20what%20sounds%20to%20me%20like%20a%20snail%27s%20pace%2C%20but%0Ahe%27s%20certainly%20an%20intelligent%20person%3B%20I%20think%20he%20may%20spend%20more%20time%0Athinking%20about%20what%20he%27s%20reading%20as%20he%20goes%20than%20I%20do.%20%20%28I%20tend%20to%0Aread%20a%20book%20quickly%20and%20then%20spend%20the%20next%20week%20or%20more%20pondering%20the%0Aimplications%20of%20the%20whole.%29%0A%0AMore%20important%2C%20though%2C%20a%20lot%20of%20people%20are%20_very_%20busy%20with%20their%0Awork%20and%20don%27t%20really%20have%20a%20lot%20of%20time%20to%20spend%20on%20any%20one%20book.%20%20%28I%0Ashudder%20to%20think%20about%20how%20long%20it%20would%20have%20taken%20me%20to%20get%20through%0Aan%20unfamiliar%20book%20while%20I%20was%20taking%20my%20first%20class%20on%20quantum%20field%0Atheory%20and%20a%20class%20on%20string%20theory%20at%20the%20same%20time%21%29%20%20If%20Matt%20is%0Areading%20Tolkien%20in%20part%20as%20research%20for%20his%20studies%2C%20then%20I%27d%20imagine%0Athat%20he%27s%20got%20a%20lot%20of%20other%20things%20on%20his%20plate%2C%20too.%0A%0AI%20guess%20my%20message%20in%20a%20nutshell%20is%2C%20please%2C%20everyone%2C%20_think_%20about%0Ahow%20other%20people%20might%20take%20what%20you%20say%20before%20you%20say%20it.%20%20Those%20are%0Areal%20people%20you%27re%20talking%20to%20on%20the%20other%20side%20of%20the%20screen.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22k%2A%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3Cbe9o0p$2oapp$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0AI%27ve%20actually%20written%20a%20little%20CGI%20script%20to%20help%20people%20with%20that%0Avery%20question.%20%20You%20tell%20it%20the%20sorts%20of%20things%20you%20like%20to%20read%2C%20and%0Ait%20suggests%20a%20reasonable%20order%20in%20which%20to%20read%20the%20books.%20%20It%20will%0Aeven%20suggest%20which%20parts%20of%20each%20book%20you%27re%20likely%20to%20enjoy%20most.%20%20%28I%0Akeep%20meaning%20to%20go%20back%20and%20tweak%20it%20at%20some%20point%2C%20but%20most%20people%0Awho%20have%20commented%20on%20it%20seem%20to%20like%20it.%29%20%20You%20can%20find%20the%20list%20from%0A%0Ahttp:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Fbooks.html%0A%0ALet%20me%20know%20what%20you%20think%21%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%22k%2A%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3Cbeaf7l$2tn7i$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0A%0AYou%20don%27t%20need%20to%20go%20as%20far%20as%20all%20that%21%20:%29%20In%20fact%2C%20to%20let%20you%20in%20on%0Aa%20little%20secret%20about%20the%20inner%20workings%20of%20the%20script%2C%20no%20book%20listed%0Abelow%20the%20Biography%20will%20have%20any%20parts%20that%20match%20your%20stated%0Apreferences%20at%20all.%20%20In%20any%20case%2C%20once%20you%27ve%20gotten%20to%20a%20point%20in%20the%0Alist%20where%20two%20or%20three%20books%20haven%27t%20proven%20to%20be%20very%20enjoyable%20to%0Ayou%2C%20you%20should%20probably%20stop%20reading%20there.%20:%29%0A%0A%0AI%27m%20guessing%20that%20you%20copied%20this%20out%20of%20the%20%22Titles%20Only%22%20mode%20of%20the%0Ascript.%20%20I%20hope%20that%20you%20took%20a%20look%20at%20the%20default%20mode%20%28that%20lists%0Arecommended%20sections%2C%20too%29%20as%20well:%20the%20list%20of%20section%0Arecommendations%20is%20especially%20useful%20for%20books%20like%20_Unfinished%0ATales_%2C%20where%20the%20first%20part%20%28or%20even%20two%29%20of%20the%20book%20isn%27t%20really%0Aworth%20reading%20until%20you%27ve%20read%20_The%20Silmarillion_.%20%20The%20Third%20Age%0Astories%20are%20the%20easiest%20place%20to%20start%20if%20you%20haven%27t%20read%20Silm.%20yet.%0A%0AIn%20any%20case%2C%20enjoy%20the%20books%21%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CDX3Ma.1628$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0AEr%2C%20check%20me%20on%20this%2C%20but%20aren%27t%20any%20audio%20books%20of%20LotR%20out%20there%0Afully%20protected%20by%20copyright%3F%20%20I%20mean%2C%20even%20if%20you%27ve%20got%20some%20quarrel%0Awith%20the%20recording%20industry%2C%20I%20don%27t%20think%20that%20audio%20books%20of%20LotR%0Aare%20produced%20by%20the%20major%20record%20labels%21%20%20%28Certainly%20not%20under%20the%0Asame%20contract%20model%20that%20is%20used%20for%20music%2C%20in%20any%20case%2C%20and%20I%20think%0Athat%27s%20what%20most%20peoples%27%20complaints%20about%20the%20recording%20industry%0Aare%20based%20on.%29%0A%0AThey%27re%20recordings%20of%20the%20work%20of%20a%20great%20author%20%28still%20the%20rightful%0Aproperty%20of%20his%20estate%20under%20law%29%20and%20produced%20by%20people%20who%20certainly%0Adeserve%20to%20be%20rewarded%20for%20their%20good%20work%20%28most%20of%20them%20are%20probably%0Aeven%20still%20alive%2C%20right%3F%29.%20%20So%20what%27s%20the%20legal%20or%20ethical%20basis%20for%0Adownloading%20them%20rather%20than%20buying%20them%3F%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20David%20Salo%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3C180720031510551719%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0AHeh.%20%20Unfortunately%2C%20I%20_don%27t_%20have%20a%20lot%20of%20extra%20time%20on%20my%20hands%0Athese%20days%20%28trying%20to%20wrestle%20a%20research%20project%20to%20a%20close%20and%0Aall%29.%20:%29%0A%0A%0AI%20have%20absolutely%20no%20idea%2C%20and%20I%27ve%20wondered%20which%20was%20%22right%22%20for%0Aquite%20some%20time.%20%20%28Mostly%20when%20trying%20to%20write%20%22properly%22%20in%20posts%0Ahere%2C%20in%20fact.%29%20%20I%20have%20a%20vague%20recollection%20that%20_The%20Hobbit_%20tended%0Anot%20to%20capitalize%20race%20names%20but%20that%20LotR%20and%20Silm.%20tended%20to%3B%20I%27m%0Anot%20quite%20sure%20why%2C%20but%20it%20might%20serve%20to%20remind%20the%20reader%20that%2C%20for%0Aexample%2C%20these%20aren%27t%20traditional%20%22house%20elves%22%20but%20rather%20Eldar.%20%20I%0Athink%20that%20for%20the%20most%20part%2C%20I%27ve%20adopted%20the%20%22capitalize%20just%20about%0Aeverything%22%20strategy%20%28though%20I%20do%20wonder%20what%20to%20do%20with%20%22Humans%22%2C%0Asince%20my%20feminist%20upbringing%20rebels%20against%20%22Men%22%29.%0A%0AI%27d%20love%20to%20see%20the%20pattern%2C%20too.%20%20Maybe%20at%20some%20point%20I%27ll%20do%20some%0Asort%20of%20statistical%20sampling.%20%20But%20don%27t%20hold%20your%20breath.%20:%29%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20Gonzalo%20Diethelm%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3C3f03dbe7$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AWell%2C%20if%20one%20_did_%20want%20to%20make%20the%20argument%20that%20such%20a%20%22transfer%20of%0Avisa%22%20was%20necessary%2C%20there%27s%20always%20the%20possibility%20that%20some%20other%0AElf%20in%20Rivendell%20gave%20up%20his%20or%20her%20place%20so%20that%20Bilbo%20could%20go.%20%20But%0Ain%20the%20end%2C%20I%20think%20it%27s%20pretty%20clear%20that%20it%20_was_%20just%20a%20suggestion%0Aby%20Arwen.%20%20The%20letter%20by%20Tolkien%20that%20Conrad%20quoted%20later%20in%20his%20reply%0Aexplains%20the%20details%20quite%20well.%0A%0A%0AWhat%20do%20you%20mean%20by%20%22FACT%22%3F%20%20I%20assume%20you%27re%20implicitly%20asking%20for%0A%22canonical%22%20evidence%20for%20Sam%27s%20departure%2C%20but%20you%20haven%27t%20said%20what%0Asources%20you%20consider%20to%20be%20%22canonical%22.%20%20%28In%20particular%2C%20you%20seem%20to%0Abe%20hesitant%20to%20accept%20Tolkien%27s%20direct%20and%20unambiguous%20statement%20in%0Athe%20letter%20quoted%20above.%29%20%20Most%20of%20the%20available%20evidence%20is%20collected%0Ain%20the%20FAQ%20question%20on%20this%20topic%2C%20at%0A%0Ahttp:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Ffaq%2FHistory.html%23SamWest%0A%0AIn%20particular%2C%20LotR%20strongly%20implies%20that%20Sam%20did%20eventually%20sail%0AWest.%20%20Frodo%20predicts%20it%2C%20and%20one%20of%20the%20last%20entries%20in%20the%20Tale%20of%0AYears%20includes%20the%20fact%20that%20Sam%20was%20last%20seen%20by%20hobbits%20heading%20west%0Afrom%20the%20Shire%20toward%20the%20Grey%20Havens%2C%20and%20that%20the%20hobbits%27%20tradition%0Awas%20that%20he%20passed%20over%20the%20Sea.%0A%0AFor%20a%20long%20time%2C%20that%20didn%27t%20convince%20me:%20I%20rather%20liked%20the%20sad%0Anotion%20of%20Sam%20spending%20his%20last%20days%20at%20the%20Havens%2C%20gazing%20out%20across%0Athe%20Sea%20that%20he%20could%20never%20cross%20to%20the%20friends%20whom%20he%20would%20never%0Asee%20again.%20%20But%20that%27s%20the%20tragedy%20lover%20in%20me%2C%20I%20guess%20%28I%20find%20that%20I%0Aoften%20enjoy%20movies%20more%20when%20they%20don%27t%20have%20a%20generic%20Hollywood%0Aending%2C%20for%20example%29.%20%20Once%20I%20saw%20Tolkien%27s%20letter%20directly%20stating%0Athat%20Sam%20_had_%20crossed%20the%20Sea%2C%20I%20decided%20that%20the%20suggestions%20to%20that%0Aeffect%20in%20LotR%20_were_%20meant%20seriously%2C%20and%20that%20their%20ambiguity%20was%0Ajust%20part%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20usual%20style%20rather%20than%20a%20hint%20that%20they%0Aweren%27t%20true.%20%20For%20all%20the%20tragic%20grandeur%20of%20his%20tales%2C%20Tolkien%20was%0Avery%20fond%20of%20happy%20endings%20and%20hesitant%20to%20break%20them.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20Graham%20Lockwood%0A%3CGondhirAtC%2AH%2AO%2AK%2AL%2AI%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CBB2E45AA.94F7%25GondhirAtC%2AH%2AO%2AK%2AL%2AI%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0A%0AAs%20I%20think%20I%20mentioned%20in%20my%20previous%20reply%2C%20the%20more%20detailed%20mode%20of%0Athe%20script%20does%20recommend%20skipping%20the%20First%20Age%20stories%20in%20UT%20if%20you%0Ahaven%27t%20read%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20yet.%20%20And%20as%20for%20spoilers%2C%20I%20think%20the%0Amajority%20of%20the%20%22spoilable%22%20stories%20in%20Silm.%20are%20already%20spoiled%20by%0A_The%20Hobbit_%20and%20LotR%20%28where%20did%20Glamdring%20come%20from%3F%20%20What%20did%20Beren%0Aand%20Luthien%20do%3F%29%0A%0AAs%20you%20might%20guess%2C%20configuring%20the%20script%20to%20often%20suggest%20UT%20before%0ASilm.%20was%20a%20difficult%20choice%20for%20me%20to%20make.%20%20The%20reason%20that%20I%20made%0Athat%20choice%20is%20essentially%20as%20follows.%20%20Almost%20anyone%20who%20enjoys%20LotR%0A%28and%20in%20particular%2C%20almost%20anyone%20who%20enjoys%20parts%20of%20the%20Appendices%29%0Awill%20find%20things%20in%20UT%20that%20they%20will%20also%20enjoy.%20%20The%20Third%20Age%0Astories%20in%20UT%20doesn%27t%20really%20depend%20on%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20at%20all%2C%20and%0Amany%20of%20the%20Second%20Age%20and%20%22all%20Age%22%20stories%20can%20be%20read%20easily%0Awithout%20Silm.%20as%20background.%0A%0AOn%20the%20other%20hand%2C%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20reads%20a%20lot%20like%20a%20history%20book%0Aor%20even%20like%20the%20Bible%2C%20especially%20near%20the%20beginning.%20%20I%20have%20had%20a%0Afair%20number%20of%20friends%20start%20Silm.%2C%20get%20frustrated%20with%20it%20and%20give%20up%0Abefore%20it%20gets%20more%20%22storylike%22%2C%20and%20never%20try%20any%20other%20Tolkien%20book.%0ATherefore%2C%20the%20script%20won%27t%20recommend%20Silm.%20before%20UT%20unless%20the%20user%0Asays%20that%20they%20really%20like%20reading%20histories.%0A%0AThat%27s%20my%20reasoning%2C%20anyway.%20:%29%20%20Others%20certainly%20disagree%20at%20times.%0ABut%20I%20think%20the%20flexibility%20of%20the%20booklist%20avoids%20any%20_real_%0Adisasters.%20:%29%0A%0A%0A%0AThe%20book%27s%20description%20in%20the%20booklist%20does%20indicate%20that.%20%20And%2C%20for%0Athe%20record%2C%20I%20don%27t%20think%20that%20the%20program%20would%20have%20recommended%20ATB%0Athis%20highly%20without%20being%20told%20that%20the%20user%20enjoyed%20Tolkien%27s%20poetry%0A%28of%20one%20sort%20or%20another%2C%20but%20probably%20%22light%20poetry%22%20in%20particular%29.%0A%0A%0A%0AOr%2C%20as%20I%20say%20in%20the%20booklist:%0A%0A%20%20%20%27Technically%2C%20this%20essay%20has%20absolutely%20nothing%20to%20do%20with%0A%20%20%20Middle-earth%20at%20all.%20However%2C%20in%20one%20section%20of%20it%20Tolkien%20makes%0A%20%20%20numerous%20reference%20to%20%22elves%22%20and%20the%20Art%20that%20they%20create:%20for%0A%20%20%20example%2C%20%22To%20the%20elvish%20craft%2C%20Enchantment%2C%20Fantasy%20aspires.%22%20In%0A%20%20%20the%20essay%2C%20he%20does%20not%20treat%20the%20elves%20as%20%22real%22%2C%20but%20nevertheless%0A%20%20%20it%20seems%20that%20his%20comments%20on%20elves%20here%20do%20apply%20to%20the%20elves%20of%0A%20%20%20Middle-earth.%27%0A%0AThat%27s%20how%20I%20justify%20putting%20it%20into%20a%20list%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20Middle-earth%0Awritings%2C%20anyway.%20:%29%0A%0A%0A%0AWell%2C%20sure.%20:%29%20%20It%20is%20a%20truly%20remarkable%20essay%20%28associated%20with%0A%22Quendi%20and%20Eldar%22%20in%20The%20War%20of%20the%20Jewels%29%2C%20discussing%20the%0A%22telepathy%22%20possessed%20by%20all%20%22incarnates%22%20in%20Middle-earth%2C%20ways%20in%0Awhich%20the%20Ainur%20could%20become%20%22bound%22%20to%20their%20physical%20forms%2C%20and%20the%0Amoral%20decisions%20of%20Manwe%20regarding%20Melkor.%0A%0ABut%20that%27s%20what%20I%20already%20said%20in%20the%20booklist.%20:%29%20%20It%27s%20an%20incredible%0Aread%2C%20and%20I%20honestly%20have%20no%20idea%20why%20Christopher%20Tolkien%20didn%27t%20find%0Asome%20place%20to%20include%20it%20in%20HoMe%20as%20published.%20%20It%20just%20contains%20so%0Amany%20amazingly%20cool%20tidbits%20about%20the%20way%20that%20Middle-earth%20works%20that%0Ait%27s%20absolutely%20worth%20the%20$2%20price.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20Graham%20Lockwood%0A%3CGondhirAtC%2AH%2AO%2AK%2AL%2AI%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3CBB4DB9A3.AA05%25GondhirAtC%2AH%2AO%2AK%2AL%2AI%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%5BInsert%20extremely%20short%2C%20mild%20chuckle%20here.%5D%0A%5BPause.%5D%0A%5BInsert%20brief%20yawn.%5D%0A%0A:%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%5BOkay%2C%20I%27m%20not%20willing%20to%20try%20to%20spoiler-proof%20my%20comments%20about%20the%0Abook%20or%20six-month-old%20movie%20in%20a%20detailed%20discussion%20here%2C%20so%20you%27ve%0Abeen%20warned.%20:%29%20%5D%0A%0A%0A%0AYou%20know%2C%20now%20that%20I%20think%20of%20it%2C%20I%20think%20you%27re%20completely%20right.%20%20In%0Athe%20book%2C%20Aragorn%20certainly%20saw%20that%20he%20_could_%20be%20attracted%20to%20the%0AEowyn%2C%20but%20he%20was%20of%20course%20thoroughly%20attached%20to%20Arwen%20and%0Apresumably%20didn%27t%20give%20serious%20consideration%20to%20dumping%20her%20in%20favor%0Aof%20someone%20else.%20%20Still%2C%20he%20felt%20pretty%20bad%20rejecting%20her%20advances.%0AIn%20the%20movie%2C%20Aragorn%20was%20downright%20flirting%20with%20Eowyn%20and%20no%20longer%0Ahad%20Arwen%20to%20be%20faithful%20to%2C%20but%20still%20seemed%20far%20too%20attached%20to%20her%0Aemotionally%20to%20seriously%20move%20on.%20%20So%20yeah%2C%20the%20romance%20was%20far%20less%0Aone-sided%20in%20the%20movie%2C%20though%20it%20didn%27t%20lead%20to%20any%20real%20difference%0Ain%20any%20characters%27%20behavior.%20%20That%27s%20bound%20to%20change%20in%20the%20final%0Ainstallment%2C%20though%2C%20where%20Aragorn%27s%20current%20non-book%20reasons%20for%20not%0Areaching%20out%20to%20Eowyn%20will%20undoubtedly%20be%20wrenched%20violently%20into%20his%0Abook%20reasons.%20:%29%20And%20that%2C%20of%20course%2C%20will%20provide%20a%20very%20clear%20and%0Adirect%20motivation%20for%20Eowyn%27s%20dispair...%20at%20the%20cost%20of%20making%20it%20seem%0Aa%20bit%20more%20Aragorn%27s%20fault%20%28in%20the%20book%2C%20he%20was%20blameless%2C%20never%0Ahaving%20encouraged%20her%20at%20all%29.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20Henry%20Hanna%20%3CUse-Author-Address-Header@%5B127.1%5D%3E%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%5BComments%20on%20romantic%20bits%20in%20the%20books%20snipped.%5D%0A%0A%0AYou%27re%20welcome.%20:%29%0A%0A%0AWhy%3F%20%20Some%20of%20Shakespeare%20is%20pretty%20blah.%20%20And%20a%20person%20who%20can%0Aactually%20read%20Leviticus%20or%20Numbers%20without%20dozing%20off%20can%20read%0Aanything.%20:%29%20On%20the%20other%20hand%2C%20there%20have%20been%20a%20great%20many%20excellent%0Abooks%20written%20in%20the%20past%20century%2C%20and%20_The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings_%20is%0Aalmost%20certainly%20one%20of%20them.%20%20%28I%20don%27t%20think%20it%27s%20any%20less%20respected%0Aas%20%22fine%20literature%22%20than%20Shakespeare%27s%20works%20were%20in%20his%20day%2C%20if%20I%0Arecall%20correctly%2C%20and%20it%27s%20at%20least%20as%20popular.%29%20%20In%20any%20case%2C%20I%27ve%0Afound%20that%20reading%20just%20one%20sort%20of%20literature%20at%20a%20time%20can%20start%20to%0Awear%20you%20down%3B%20for%20me%2C%20it%20really%20helps%20to%20alternate%20between%20serious%0Anovels%2C%20history%2C%20fantasy%2C%20science%20essays%2C%20and%20so%20forth.%20%20Your%20milege%0Amay%20vary%2C%20of%20course.%20:%29%0A%0A%0AHmm.%20%20Coming%20from%20someone%20who%20hasn%27t%20actually%20_read_%20%22the%20Ring%20books%22%2C%0AI%20don%27t%20know%20that%20I%27ll%20put%20much%20stock%20in%20your%20opinion%20for%20now.%20:%29%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%20Roger%20Clewley%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AI%27ve%20never%20known%20just%20how%20much%20credit%20to%20give%20to%20that%20%22chiefs%22%0Acomment.%20%20For%20reference%2C%20it%27s%20from%20early%20in%20the%20essay%20in%20UT:%0A%0A%20%20%20%22Of%20this%20Order%20the%20number%20is%20unknown%3B%20but%20of%20those%20that%20came%20to%20the%0A%20%20%20North%20of%20Middle-earth...%20the%20chiefs%20were%20five.%22%0A%0AAs%20a%20first%20observation%2C%20this%20statement%20doesn%27t%20give%20any%20indication%0Athat%20the%20Istari%20%28all%20the%20members%20%22of%20this%20order%22%2C%20whether%20%22chiefs%22%20or%0Anot%29%20were%20not%20all%20the%20same%20type%20of%20being.%0A%0AMore%20importantly%2C%20Tolkien%20never%20hints%20anywhere%20else%20that%20there%20were%0Amore%20than%20five%20Istari%20in%20total.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20LotR%20App.%20B%20states%20flat%20out%0Athat%20%22it%20is%20said%20there%20were%20five%22%20Istari%2C%20Saruman%20says%20essentially%20the%0Asame%20thing%20in%20%22The%20Voice%20of%20Saruman%22%2C%20and%20the%20more%20detailed%0Adiscussions%20of%20the%20five%20Istari%20given%20in%20UT%20and%20in%20PoMe%20always%20seem%20to%0Alist%20exactly%20five.%20%20That%20stands%20in%20stark%20contrast%20to%20this%20passage%2C%0Awhich%20seems%20to%20indicate%20not%20only%20that%20there%20were%20more%20than%20five%20Istari%0Ain%20%22the%20North%20of%20Middle-earth%22%20but%20that%20there%20were%20more%20%22chiefs%22%0Aelsewhere%20in%20the%20world.%0A%0AMy%20feeling%20is%20that%20the%20great%20weight%20of%20the%20evidence%20supports%20the%0Aexistence%20of%20exactly%20five%20Istari%2C%20all%20of%20them%20Maiar%20in%20nature.%0A%0A%0AAs%20an%20added%20note%20on%20this%20point%2C%20I%20believe%20that%20they%20were%20bound%20to%0Aphysical%20forms%20in%20much%20the%20same%20way%20that%20is%20described%20in%20the%20essay%0A%22Osanwe-kenta%22%2C%20though%20voluntarily%20rather%20than%20involuntarily%20seems%20to%0Abe%20the%20focus%20there.%20%20%28I%27m%20not%20quite%20sure%20how%20that%20voluntary%20binding%0Aworked...%20maybe%20they%20were%20just%20told%20to%20do%20a%20lot%20of%20%22begetting%22%20before%0Athey%20left.%20:%29%20%29%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Conrad%20Dunkerson%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AJust%20to%20clarify%20a%20little%2C%20I%27m%20pretty%20sure%20that%20Conrad%20is%20speaking%0Astory-externally%20here.%20%20That%20is%2C%20Tolkien%27s%20original%20concept%20of%20Dwarves%0Awas%20that%20they%20were%20some%20of%20Morgoth%27s%20creatures%2C%20but%20as%20he%20revised%20and%0Aexpanded%20the%20tales%20they%20became%20more%20neutral%20and%20finally%20generally%0Agood.%20%20%28As%20he%20pointed%20out%2C%20portraying%20them%20so%20positively%20in%20_The%0AHobbit_%20surely%20helped%20with%20that.%29%20%20I%20don%27t%20recall%20offhand%20when%20the%0A%22created%20by%20Aule%22%20story%20as%20presented%20in%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20first%0Aemerged%20%28and%20I%20don%27t%20have%20my%20books%20here%20to%20check%20directly%29.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Conrad%20Dunkerson%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0AI%27m%20currently%20leaning%20toward%20%22established%22%20as%20my%20new%20clarification%0Aword%2C%20together%20with%20a%20link%20to%20my%20full%20canonicity%20essay%20%28or%20possibly%0Ajust%20to%20the%20FAQ%20entry%2C%20which%20might%20also%20deserve%20to%20be%20updated%29.%20%20I%27ll%0Asee%20what%20I%20come%20up%20with.%0A%0A%0AThere%27s%20clearly%20not%20a%20way%20to%20_completely_%20clarify%20the%20meaning%2C%20of%0Acourse.%20%20My%20goal%20is%20more%20to%20make%20sure%20people%20don%27t%20think%20I%20mean%0A%22accepted%20by%20the%20Catholic%20church%22%20%28or%20think%20that%20_I_%20consider%20the%0Abooks%20as%20important%20as%20the%20church%20considers%20its%20canon%2C%20for%20that%0Amatter%21%20:%29%20%29%2C%20and%20to%20give%20a%20vague%20sense%20of%20the%20word%20to%20anyone%20who%0Adoesn%27t%20know%20the%20definition%20at%20all%20%28most%20children%2C%20for%20example%29.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Conrad%20Dunkerson%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0AWow%21%20%20You%27ve%20just%20demonstrated%20to%20me%20that%20my%20FAQ%20posting%20address%20is%0Adifferent%20than%20my%20normal%20posting%20address:%20I%27m%20on%20the%20%22by%20Volume%22%20list%0Atwice%20%28I%20apparently%20had%2017%20non-automated%20posts%20last%20week%29.%20%20That%27s%0Aconveinent:%20it%20means%20that%20my%20automated%20stuff%20_isn%27t_%20folded%20into%20my%0Ausual%20posting%20totals%2C%20which%20I%20think%20is%20as%20it%20should%20be.%20:%29%20%20Now%2C%20as%0Afor%20how%20_you_%20managed%20to%20write%20almost%20a%20FAQ%27s%20worth%20of%20content%20in%20the%0Apast%20week%2C%20I%20couldn%27t%20really%20say.%0A%0AIncidentally%2C%20this%20seems%20like%20as%20good%20a%20place%20as%20any%20to%20pass%20along%20a%0Acompliment%20I%27ve%20found%20for%20the%20page%20on%20my%20website%20that%20holds%20essays%20by%0Ayou%20and%20me%20%28http:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Fessays%2F%29.%20%20The%20site%0Awww.thelordoftherings.com%20links%20to%20that%20page%20with%20the%20comment:%0A%0A%20%20%20%20A%20collection%20of%20some%20of%20the%20finest%20essays%20concerning%20various%0A%20%20%20%20aspects%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20Middle-earth%20you%27re%20likely%20to%20find%20on%20the%0A%20%20%20%20WWW.%0A%0ASeeing%20as%20only%20two%20of%20my%20essays%20there%20could%20possibly%20qualify%20as%0Aparticularly%20%22fine%22%2C%20I%20figured%20sharing%20the%20compliment%20would%20be%20a%20good%0Athing.%20:%29%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Charlie%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0AAs%20you%27ve%20already%20learned%2C%20there%20are%20a%20wide%20range%20of%20views%20on%20what%0A%22canonical%22%20should%20mean%20for%20Tolkien%27s%20writings.%20%20%28I%27ve%20written%20a%20whole%0Aessay%20expressing%20my%20view%20on%20the%20matter.%29%20%20Some%20people%20don%27t%20like%20the%0Aidea%20of%20declaring%20some%20texts%20to%20be%20%22better%22%20than%20others%20at%20all%2C%0Apreferring%20just%20to%20explore%20the%20shape%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20ideas%20as%20they%20formed%0Aand%20reformed%20over%20time.%0A%0AOn%20the%20other%20hand%2C%20I%20would%20say%20that%20most%20people%20who%20discuss%0AMiddle-earth%20here%20have%20at%20least%20some%20notion%20of%20which%20texts%20are%0A%22canonical%22%20in%20the%20context%20of%20those%20discussions%2C%20even%20if%20it%27s%20not%0Aterribly%20firm%20or%20well-defined.%20%20%28Any%20discussion%20of%20Middle-earth%20itself%0Aas%20a%20%22secondary%20world%22%20--%20as%20opposed%20to%20Tolkien%27s%20process%20of%20writing%0Aabout%20it%20--%20_must_%20be%20based%20on%20some%20self-consistent%20definition%2C%20or%0Aelse%20rational%20discourse%20is%20impossible.%29%0A%0ASo%2C%20from%20that%20perspective%2C%20I%20will%20simply%20say%20that%20most%20people%20who%0Aaccept%20any%20notion%20of%20a%20Tolkien%20%22canon%22%20tend%20to%20reply%20most%20firmly%20on%0A_The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings_.%20%20Books%20like%20_The%20Hobbit_%2C%20_The%20Adventures%20of%0ATom%20Bombadil_%2C%20and%20_The%20Road%20Goes%20Ever%20On_%20which%20he%20published%20during%0Ahis%20lifetime%20tend%20to%20be%20assigned%20weight%20either%20equal%20to%20LotR%20or%20only%0Aslightly%20less.%20%20Beyond%20that%2C%20things%20get%20murky.%20%20But%20at%20least%20that%0Aanswers%20your%20question...%20I%20hope.%20:%29%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Eric%20Schrauth%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AYeah.%20%20The%20creator%20of%20that%20site%20seems%20to%20have%20stolen%20virtually%20the%0Aentire%20content%20of%20Barbara%20Strachey%27s%20book%20_The%20Journeys%20of%20Frodo_%20and%0Aput%20it%20online%20for%20free.%20%20I%20rather%20doubt%20that%20Ms.%20Strachey%20or%20her%0Apublishers%20gave%20him%20permission%2C%20or%20that%20he%20even%20bothered%20to%20ask%20them%0Aat%20all.%20%20My%20advice%20would%20be%20to%20write%20to%20the%20site%27s%20creator%20and%20kindly%0Asuggest%20that%20he%20practice%20%22courtesy%20%28at%20least%29%20to%20living%20authors%22%2C%20just%0Aas%20Tolkien%20asked%20his%20own%20readers%20after%20Ace%20published%20LotR%20without%20his%0Apermission.%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Lady%20Elwen%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0AI%20think%20Softrat%20was%20referring%20to%20the%20removal%20of%20the%20Valaquenta%20and%20the%0AAinulindale%2C%20rather%20than%20to%20the%20decision%20to%20include%20them%20in%20the%0Apublished%20book.%20%20However%2C%20I%20also%20seem%20to%20recall%20that%20Tolkien%20himself%0Ahad%20included%20both%20of%20those%20texts%20in%20a%20list%20of%20things%20to%20include%20along%0Awith%20the%20QS%20proper%20once%20they%20were%20finally%20published.%20%20%28I%27d%20want%20to%0Alook%20up%20the%20reference%2C%20however.%29%0A%0AAt%20any%20rate%2C%20my%20understanding%20is%20that%20your%20statement%20was%20essentially%20a%0Acorrect%20description%20of%20the%20latest%20state%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings.%20%20To%20me%2C%0Ait%27s%20only%20a%20minor%20quibble%20that%20Tolkien%20himself%20wanted%20those%20texts%20to%0Aaccompany%20the%20Quenta%20Silmarillion%20when%20it%20published.%0A%0A%0AAck.%20%20I%20don%27t%20think%20there%27s%20any%20need%20to%20apologize:%20as%20I%20said%2C%20I%20think%0Ayour%20summary%20was%20pretty%20much%20perfectly%20right.%20%20%28It%20always%20bugs%20me%20when%0Apeople%20are%20less%20than%20polite%20when%20they%20correct%20each%20other:%20that%20can%27t%0Ahelp%20but%20discourage%20newcomers%20from%20speaking%20up%20in%20the%20future.%29%0A%0A%0AYou%27re%20welcome%20to%20retreat%20back%20to%20lurking%2C%20but%20you%27re%20even%20more%0Awelcome%20to%20keep%20posting%20occasionally.%20:%29%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Furio97%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0ANope.%20%20%28Unless%20you%20count%20Aragorn%27s%20exploits%20at%20sea%20when%20he%20spent%20time%0Ain%20Gondor%20under%20the%20name%20%22Thorongil%22%2C%20as%20described%20in%20App.%20A.%29%0A%0A%0ANope.%20%20%28Unless%20Umbar%20is%20counted%20as%20part%20of%20Harad%2C%20in%20which%20case%0AAragorn%27s%20exploits%20above%20might%20count%20here%2C%20too.%20%20Oh%2C%20and%20the%0ANumenorian%20landing%20when%20they%20captured%20Sauron.%20%20You%20can%20see%20how%20much%0AI%27m%20stretching%20here.%20:%29%20%29%0A%0A%0ANope.%0A%0A%0ACertainly%20not%20in%20the%20Second%20or%20Third%20Age%20%28unless%20you%20count%20the%20brief%0Ascene%20of%20Gandalf%20visiting%20Thorin%20in%20%22The%20Quest%20of%20Erebor%22%2C%20published%0Ain%20_Unfinished%20Tales%29.%20%20Keep%20in%20mind%20that%20the%20Blue%20Mountains%20were%20the%0Aeastern%20border%20of%20Beleriand%2C%20so%20there%20may%20have%20been%20some%20events%20in%20the%0ASilmarillion%20that%20took%20place%20there.%20%20But%20again%2C%20it%27s%20a%20stretch.%0A%0AThe%20only%20story%20that%20I%20can%20think%20of%20that%20was%20really%20set%20in%20a%20place%0Aother%20than%20those%20in%20_The%20Hobbit_%2C%20LotR%2C%20or%20Silm.%20is%20%22Tal-Elmar%22%2C%20a%0Astory%20set%20along%20the%20west%20coast%20of%20Middle-earth%20in%20the%20Second%20Age%2C%20when%0Athe%20Numenorians%20were%20just%20beginning%20to%20return.%20%20Of%20course%2C%20Tolkien%0Aonly%20wrote%20a%20few%20pages%20of%20it%2C%20so%20it%27s%20not%20really%20satisfying%20at%20all.%0A%28You%20can%20find%20it%20in%20_The%20Peoples%20of%20Middle-earth_.%29%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28John%20Brock%29%20in%20article%0A%3Cbertlv$j60$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0A%0AYes%2C%20it%20was.%20%20And%20as%20you%20guessed%20below%2C%20it%20_was_%20chosen%20because%20it%0Acontained%20much%20of%20the%20%22most%20accessable%20material%22%20in%20Tolkien%27s%20notes.%0AI%20firmly%20second%20Stan%27s%20suggestion%20to%20read%20UT%20next.%20%20And%20as%20he%0Amentioned%2C%20my%20Custom%20Tolkien%20Book%20List%20might%20be%20a%20useful%20resource%0Aafter%20that%20%28it%20will%20suggest%20a%20reading%20order%20based%20on%20the%20user%27s%0Apreferences%29:%0A%0Ahttp:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Fbooks.html%0A%0A%0AUnfortunately%2C%20that%20only%20holds%20up%20through%20_Unfinished%20Tales_.%20%20After%0Athat%2C%20Christopher%20went%20through%20his%20father%27s%20drafts%20and%20writings%20in%0Aroughly%20chronological%20order%2C%20starting%20with%20%22The%20Book%20of%20Lost%20Tales%22%0A%28which%20consists%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20very%20earliest%20writings%20on%20Middle-earth%29.%0AThat%20means%20that%20HoMe%20starts%20with%20the%20very%20least%20%22familiar%22%20of%0ATolkien%27s%20writings%20%28along%20with%20_lots_%20of%20commentary%29%20and%20only%20slowly%0Amakes%20it%20way%20to%20what%20some%20of%20us%20would%20call%20%22canonical%22%20information.%0AMoreover%2C%20some%20readers%20would%20probably%20be%20totally%20uninterested%20in%20the%0Adrafts%20of%20LotR%20that%20are%20found%20in%20HoMe%20VI-VIII%20%28and%20part%20of%20IX%29%2C%20but%0Athey%20might%20be%20very%20interested%20in%20the%20stories%20and%20essays%20in%20HoMe%20X-XI.%0A%0A%0AParts%20of%20it%20are%20fantastic%2C%20suitable%20for%20anyone%20who%20enjoyed%20any%20part%20of%0Athe%20Appendices%20to%20LotR.%20%20Other%20parts%20can%20be%20pretty%20dry%2C%20and%20for%20many%0Apeople%20it%20would%20probably%20be%20best%20to%20just%20pretend%20the%20commentary%20wasn%27t%0Athere%20at%20all%20%28except%20occasionally%20to%20fill%20in%20gaps%20in%20the%0Anarrative...%20these%20are%20%22Unfinished%22%20tales%2C%20after%20all%29.%20%20Again%2C%20my%20Book%0AList%20will%20suggest%20which%20sections%20you%27re%20likely%20to%20enjoy%20most%20%28though%20I%0Amust%20admit%20that%20improving%20the%20section%20recommendations%20for%20UT%20is%20one%20of%0Amy%20highest%20Book%20List%20update%20priorities%29.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Kyle%20C.%20Maxwell%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0ANow%2C%20c%27mon.%20%20First%20of%20all%2C%20I%20have%20trouble%20imagining%20a%20class%20that%20would%0Aassign%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20as%20reading%20material%20%28or%20at%20least%2C%20a%20class%0Athat%20someone%20who%20didn%27t%20_want_%20to%20read%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20would%20ever%0Atake%29.%20%20And%20on%20top%20of%20that%2C%20if%20this%20were%20really%20a%20homework%20question%2C%0Awouldn%27t%20the%20original%20poster%20have%20copied%20the%20correct%20plural%20%22Maiar%22%3F%0A%28Why%20would%20they%20even%20know%20the%20singular%20form%20if%20they%20hadn%27t%20read%20the%0Abooks%20at%20all%3F%29%0A%0AAnd%20second%2C%20I%20don%27t%20think%20it%27s%20reasonable%20to%20demean%20others%20for%20wanting%0Ato%20jump%20straight%20to%20the%20information%20that%20interests%20them.%20%20Sure%2C%20you%0Aand%20I%20may%20enjoy%20_The%20Silmarillion_%2C%20but%20a%20lot%20of%20people%20honestly%20don%27t%0A%28the%20early%20parts%20in%20particular%20can%20be%20hard%20to%20get%20through%29.%20%20I%20don%27t%0Asee%20any%20difference%20between%20telling%20someone%20where%20the%20Maiar%20are%0Amentioned%20in%20_The%20Silmarillion_%20and%20telling%20them%20where%20Tolkien%27s%0Aearliest%20writings%20about%20Numenor%20are%20in%20HoMe.%20%20Either%20way%2C%20you%27re%0Aencouraging%20them%20to%20learn%20more%20about%20Tolkien%2C%20and%20maybe%20they%27ll%20be%0Ainterested%20enough%20by%20what%20they%20find%20to%20keep%20reading.%20%20I%20don%27t%20see%20any%0Adownside%20at%20all.%20:%29%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Paul%20Ciszek%29%20in%20article%0A%3Cbgm5vo$von$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0A%0A%0AI%20suspect%20that%20Matthew%20was%20thinking%20of%20the%20following%20quote%20from%20%22Of%0Athe%20Rings%20of%20Power%20and%20the%20Third%20Age%22%20in%20_The%20Silmarillion_:%0A%0A%20%20%20All%20living%20things%20were%20divided%20in%20that%20day%2C%20and%20some%20of%20every%20kind%2C%0A%20%20%20even%20of%20beasts%20and%20birds%2C%20were%20found%20in%20either%20host%2C%20save%20the%20Elves%0A%20%20%20only.%20%20They%20alone%20were%20undivided%20and%20followed%20Gil-galad.%20%20Of%20the%0A%20%20%20Dwarves%20few%20fought%20upon%20either%20side%3B%20but%20the%20Kindred%20of%20Durin%20of%0A%20%20%20Moria%20fought%20against%20Sauron.%0A%0A%5BCitation%20note:%20I%20copied%20this%20from%20an%20earlier%20Usenet%20posting%20since%20I%0Adon%27t%20have%20my%20books%20at%20hand%2C%20but%20I%27ve%20checked%20it%20in%20a%20couple%20of%0Amessages%20and%20I%27m%20quite%20confident%20that%20it%27s%20essentially%20correct.%5D%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20in%20article%0A%3Cbecmih$2425$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A%0A%0AThey%20aren%27t%20synonyms%2C%20true%2C%20but%20among%20their%20definitions%20are%20some%20that%0Aare%20reasonably%20similar.%20:%29%20%20I%20was%20very%20hesitant%20to%20just%20say%0A%22canonical%22%2C%20because%20I%20feared%20that%20many%20people%20wouldn%27t%20quite%20know%0Awhat%20I%20meant.%20%20%28Even%20among%20people%20on%20these%20groups%2C%20I%27ve%20seen%20those%20who%0Athought%20that%20we%20meant%20%22canonical%22%20in%20the%20traditional%20biblical%20sense%20of%0Athe%20word.%20%20Those%20folks%20were%20understandably%20disturbed%20that%20we%20seemed%20to%0Abe%20elevating%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20to%20divine%20status%21%29%20%20In%20fact%2C%20given%0Athat%20my%20Book%20List%20is%20intended%20for%20a%20_very_%20broad%20audience%20%28including%0Apeople%2C%20even%20kids%2C%20reading%20Tolkien%20for%20the%20first%20time%2C%20and%20with%20no%0Aconcept%20of%20the%20canonicity%20issue%29%2C%20I%20wanted%20to%20make%20sure%20that%20my%0Ameaning%20was%20clear.%20%20%28But%20I%20certainly%20didn%27t%20want%20to%20spend%20much%20time%20at%0Aall%20on%20definitions%21%20%20Not%20that%20everyone%20agrees%20on%20such%20things%20anyway.%0AAnd%20for%20the%20record%2C%20if%20you%20tell%20the%20list%20to%20give%20comments%20on%0Acanonicity%2C%20it%20will%20include%20an%20introductory%20section%20that%20describes%0Awhat%20I%20mean%20by%20the%20concept%20in%20considerable%20detail.%29%0A%0ASo%2C%20as%20you%20point%20out%2C%20%22trustworthy%22%20isn%27t%20really%20the%20right%20word.%20%20But%0Ait%27s%20also%20not%20the%20only%20word%20that%20I%20used:%20I%20specifically%20inserted%20it%20as%0Aa%20%22clarification%22%20of%20the%20word%20%22canonical%22.%20%20For%20those%20who%20know%20any%0Adefinition%20of%20%22canonical%22%2C%20that%20clarification%20should%20make%20it%20clear%0Athat%20I%27m%20using%20the%20word%20in%20a%20general%20sense%20%28rather%20than%20establishing%20a%0Anew%20church%29.%20%20For%20those%20who%20have%20no%20clue%20what%20%22canonical%22%20means%0A%28except%20that%20maybe%20it%27s%20related%20to%20large%20guns%29%2C%20%22trustworthy%22%20doesn%27t%0Afall%20_that_%20far%20off%20the%20mark...%20it%20will%20give%20them%20at%20least%20_some_%0Aconcept%20of%20what%20I%27m%20talking%20about.%0A%0ATo%20be%20honest%2C%20though%2C%20I%20don%27t%20see%20%22trustworthy%22%20as%20being%20_terribly_%0Awrong.%20%20In%20context%2C%20I%20think%20it%27s%20clear%20that%20Tolkien%20could%20in%20no%20sense%0Ahave%20been%20_lying_:%20it%27s%20his%20invented%20world%2C%20after%20all.%20%20What%20else%0Acould%20it%20mean%3F%20%20Well%2C%20%22trustworthy%22%20can%20mean%20%22reliable%22%2C%20and%20a%20very%0Avague%20definition%20of%20%22canonical%22%20in%20our%20case%20might%20be%20%22a%20reliable%20guide%0Ato%20Tolkien%27s%20developed%20vision%20of%20Middle-earth%22.%20%20%28See%20my%20essay%0A%22Tolkien%27s%20Parish%22%20for%20a%20far%20longer%20discussion.%29%20%20I%20guess%20I%20could%20have%0Asaid%20%22reliable%22%20instead%20of%20%22trustworthy%22%2C%20but%20%22unreliable%22%20is%20also%20a%0Anegative%20word%3B%20I%20think%20you%27d%20still%20object.%20%20Maybe%20I%20could%20say%0A%22finalized%22%2C%20but%20doesn%27t%20come%20close%20to%20suggesting%20the%20vague%20definition%0Aabove...%20I%20think%20it%27s%20even%20less%20clear%20than%20%22trustworthy%22.%0A%0AAt%20any%20rate%2C%20what%20other%20way%20of%20clarifying%20the%20meaning%20of%20%22canonical%22%0Aas%20we%20use%20it%20here%20would%20you%20suggest%3F%20%20%28I%20wouldn%27t%20use%20anything%20longer%0Athan%20two%20or%20three%20words%2C%20and%20one%20word%20would%20certainly%20be%20best.%29%20%20Maybe%0AI%20could%20just%20make%20%22canonical%22%20a%20hyperlink%20to%20my%20essay.%20:%29%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
READ%20IN%20FULL%20AND%20GIVE%20IT%20A%20THOUGHT%0A%0AMake%20from%20$20%2C000%20to%20$50%2C000%20in%204%20-%206%20weeks%21%0A%0ABy%20using%20a%20simple%20secure%20internet%20account%20called%20Paypal%0Athat%20takes%20only%20seconds%20to%20join%20and%20seconds%20to%20get%20you%0Astarted%20instead%20of%20the%20time%20and%20effort%20it%20takes%20to%20send%20it%0Aby%20post.%20JOIN%20Paypal%20at:%0A%0A%20https:%2F%2Fwww.paypal.com%2F%0A%0A%0AI%27ve%20actually%20taken%20the%2010%20minutes%20it%20requires%20to%20join%20this%0Awacky%20bunch%20of%20optimists%20and%20I%27m%20hoping%20that%20there%20are%0Aothers%20out%20there%20who%20will%20spare%20the%20change%20to%20try%20this.%0A%0AREAD%20ON.%20I%20found%20this%20on%20a%20bulletin%20board%20and%20decided%20to%0Atry%20it.%20%22A%20little%20while%20back%2C%20I%20was%20browsing%20through%20news%0Agroups%20and%20came%20across%20an%20article%20similar%20to%20this%20that%20said%0Ayou%20could%20make%20thousands%20of%20dollars%20within%20weeks%20with%20only%0Aan%20initial%20investment%20of%20$6.00%21%20So%20I%20thought%2C%20%22Yeah%20right%2C%0Athis%20must%20be%20a%20scam%22%2C%20but%20like%20most%20of%20us%2C%20I%20was%20curious%2C%0Aso%20I%20kept%20reading.%20Anyway%2C%20it%20said%20that%20you%20send%20only%20$1.00%0Ato%20each%20of%20the%206%20email%20addresses%20stated%20in%20this%20article.%0AYou%20then%20place%20your%20name%20and%20address%20at%20the%20bottom%20of%20the%0Alist%20at%20the%20%236th%20position%20and%20email%20it%20to%20as%20many%20people%20as%0Apossible%2C%20by%20advertising%20this%20page%20in%20as%20many%20ways%0Apossible%2C%20and%20posting%20this%20message%20%28with%20your%20email%20address%0Ain%20the%20list%29%20in%20at%20least%20200%20newsgroups.%20%28There%20are%0Athousands%29%20No%20catch%2C%20that%20was%20it.%20So%20after%20thinking%20it%0Aover%2C%20and%20talking%20to%20a%20few%20people%20first%2C%20I%20thought%20about%0Atrying%20it.%20I%20figured%20%22what%20have%20I%20got%20to%20lose%20except%20$6.00%2C%0Aright%3F%22%20SoS%20I%20invested%20the%20measly%20$6.00.%20Well%20GUESS%20WHAT%21%21%0AWithin%20days%2C%20I%20started%20getting%20money%20coming%20into%20my%20Pay%20Pal%0Aaccount%21%20JOIN%20at:%0A%0A%20https:%2F%2Fwww.paypal.com%2F%0A%0AI%20was%20shocked%21%20I%20figured%20it%20would%20end%20soon%2C%20but%20the%20money%0Ajust%20kept%20coming%20in.%20In%20my%20first%20week%2C%20I%20made%20about%20$25.00%0Awhich%20means%20that%2025%20people%20joined%20the%20group%20after%20they%20saw%0Amy%20posted%20messages.%20By%20the%20end%20of%20the%20second%20week%20I%20had%0Amade%20a%20total%20of%20over%20$1000.00%21%20In%20the%20third%20week%20I%20had%20over%0A$10%2C000.00%20and%20it%27s%20still%20growing.%20This%20is%20now%20my%20fourth%0Aweek%20and%20I%20have%20made%20a%20total%20of%20just%20over%20$42%2C000.00%20and%0Ait%27s%20still%20coming%20in%20rapidly.%20It%27s%20certainly%20worth%20$6.00%2C%0Aand%20the%205%20seconds%20it%20took%20to%20join%20Paypal.%20I%20have%20spent%20more%0Athan%20that%20on%20the%20lottery%21%0A%0ALet%20me%20tell%20you%20how%20this%20works%20and%20most%20importantly%2C%20why%20it%0Aworks.%0A%0AAlso%2C%20make%20sure%20you%20print%20a%20copy%20of%20this%20article%20NOW%2C%20so%0Ayou%20can%20get%20the%20information%20off%20of%20it%2C%20as%20you%20need%20it.%20I%0Apromise%20you%20that%20if%20you%20follow%20the%20directions%20EXACTLY%2C%20that%0Ayou%20will%20start%20making%20more%20money%20than%20you%20thought%20possible%0Aby%20doing%20something%20so%20easy%21%20Suggestion:%20Read%20this%20entire%0Amessage%20carefully%21%20%28Print%20it%20out%20or%20download%20it.%29%20Follow%0Athe%20simple%20directions%20and%20watch%20the%20money%20come%20in%21%20It%27s%0Athat%20easy.%20It%27s%20legal.%20And%2C%20your%20investment%20is%20only%20$6.00.%0AIMPORTANT:%20This%20is%20not%20a%20rip-off%3B%20it%20is%20not%20indecent%3B%20it%20is%0Anot%20illegal%3B%20and%20it%20is%20virtually%20no%20risk%20-%20it%20really%20works%21%0AIf%20all%20of%20the%20following%20instructions%20are%20adhered%20to%2C%20you%0Awill%20receive%20extraordinary%20dividends.%20AGAIN%2C%20PLEASE%20NOTE:%0AFollow%20these%20directions%20EXACTLY%2C%20and%20$50%2C000%20or%20more%20can%20be%0Ayours%20in%2020%20to%2060%20days.%20This%20program%20remains%20successful%0Abecause%20of%20the%20honesty%20and%20integrity%20of%20the%20participants.%0APlease%20continue%20its%20success%20by%20carefully%20adhering%20to%20the%0Ainstructions.%20You%20will%20now%20become%20part%20of%20the%20Mail%20Order%0Abusiness.%20In%20this%20business%20your%20product%20is%20not%20solid%20and%0Atangible%2C%20it%27s%20a%20service.%20You%20are%20in%20the%20business%20of%0Adeveloping%20Mailing%20Lists.%20Many%20large%20corporations%20are%20happy%0Ato%20pay%20big%20bucks%20for%20quality%20lists.%20However%2C%20the%20money%20made%0Afrom%20the%20mailing%20lists%20is%20secondary%20to%20the%20income%20which%20is%0Amade%20from%20people%20like%20you%20and%20me%20asking%20to%20be%20included%20in%0Athat%20list.%0A%0AHere%20are%20the%204%20easy%20steps%20to%20success:%0A%0ASTEP%201:%0A%0ATake%205%20seconds%202%20join%20Paypal.%0A%0Ahttps:%2F%2Fwww.paypal.com%2F%0A%0AThe%20Internet%27s%20most%20trusted%20Internet%20banking%20system%20for%0Ayour%20future%20income.%20When%20creating%20your%20Paypal%20account%20make%0Asure%20you%20use%20the%20same%20Email%20address%20as%20your%20user%20name%20in%0Athe%20list%20below%20so%20people%20can%20send%20money%20to%20your%20account.%0AOnce%20you%20have%20a%20Paypal%20account%20running%2C%20use%20Paypal%20to%20post%0A$1%20to%20EACH%20of%20the%206%20Email%20Addresses%20below%20because%20you%20pay%0Apeople%20with%20and%20email%20address%20in%20Paypal.%20To%20do%20this%20you%20may%0Aneed%20to%20use%20a%20credit%20card%20or%20an%20personal%20checking%20account%2C%20which%20is%20very%0Aeasy%2C%20and%20secure%20so%20nobody%20but%20Paypal%20may%20see%20it.%20If%20you%20use%20a%20credit%20card%0Athe%20person%20receiving%20the%20money%20will%20be%20charged%20$.52%20to%20receive%20the%20money.%0AIf%20you%20use%20a%20personal%20checking%20account%20the%20person%20will%20get%20the%20full%20$1.%20If%0Ayou%20don%27t%20have%20a%20credit%20card%20or%20a%20checking%20account%20show%20this%20great%20lucrative%0Aoffer%20to%20someone%20that%20has%0Aone%20and%20get%20them%20to%20help%20you%20pay%20the%20$6.%20What%20you%20are%20doing%0Ais%20creating%20a%20service.%20This%20is%20absolutely%20legal%21%20You%20are%0Arequesting%20a%20legitimate%20service%20and%20you%20are%20paying%20for%20it%21%0ALike%20most%20of%20us%20I%20was%20a%20little%20skeptical%20and%20a%20little%0Aworried%20about%20the%20legal%20aspects%20of%20it%20all.%20But%20I%20looked%0Aaround%20and%20did%20some%20homework%20and%20found%20it%20was%20perfectly%0Alegal.%0A%0AHere%20are%20the%206%20individual%20Email%20addresses%20that%20you%20have%20to%0Asend%20$1%20to%20through%20Paypal%20for%20this%20to%20work%20properly%20and%20for%0Ayou%20to%20receive%20money.%20%28If%20you%20don%27t%20send%20the%20money%20and%0Adecide%20to%20post%20the%20message%20with%20your%20name%20in%20it%20anyway%2C%0APaypal%20will%20instantly%20pick%20this%20up%20and%20terminate%20your%0Aaccount.%20If%20you%20did%20this%20you%20could%20get%20into%20serious%20trouble%0Abecause%20it%20is%20fraud.%20So%20follow%20the%20instructions%20and%20post%0Athe%20$6%20and%20you%20will%20make%20lots%20of%20money%20with%20no%20hassles%29.%0Areferral%20program%20fee%0A%0A1.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A2.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A3.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A4.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A5.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A6.%29%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0ASTEP%202%20Now%20take%20the%20%231%20Email%20Address%20off%20the%20list%20that%20you%0Asee%20above%2C%20move%20the%20other%20Email%20Addresses%20up%20%286%20becomes%205%2C%0A5%20becomes%204%2C%20etc.%29%20and%20add%20YOUR%20Email%20Address%20as%20number%206%0Aon%20the%20list.%0A%0ASTEP%203%20Change%20anything%20you%20need%20to%2C%20but%20try%20to%20keep%20this%0Aarticle%20as%20close%20to%20the%20original%20as%20possible.%20Now%2C%20post%0Ayour%20amended%20article%20to%20at%20least%20200%20newsgroups%20%28there%20are%0A24%2C000%20groups%20to%20submit%20to%29.%20And%20email%20your%20message%20to%20as%0Amany%20people%20you%20can.%20But%20remember%2C%20the%20more%20you%20post%20and%0Aemail%20the%20more%20money%20you%20make%21%20This%20is%20perfectly%20legal%21%20If%0Ayou%20have%20any%20doubts%2C%20r
