Raven%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AInterestingly%2C%20there%20are%20some%20female%20mammals%20who%20mate%20and%20then%20retain%20the%0Asperm%20in%20their%20uterus%20until%20they%27re%20ready%20to%20have%20their%20egg%28s%29%20fertilized.%0A%0ANot%20saying%20that%20Elves%20did%20that%2C%20but%20it%27s%20another%20possibility...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Raven%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AOr%20perhaps%20if%20he%20had%20been%20shorter%20with%20un-shod%20hairy%20feet...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0AThat%27s%20exactly%20the%20description%20of%20the%20water%20of%20the%20Morgul%20Vale:%0A%0A%20%20%20%22You%20will%20have%20no%20lack%20of%20water%20as%20you%20walk%20in%20Ithilien%2C%20but%20do%0A%20%20%20%20not%20drink%20of%20any%20stream%20that%20flows%20from%20Imlad%20Morgul%2C%20the%20Valley%0A%20%20%20%20of%20Living%20Death.%20%22%0AFaramir%20advice%20Frodo%20in%20%22Journey%20to%20the%20Cross-roads%2C%22%20and%20in%20%22The%20Stairs%0Aof%20Cirith%20Ungol%22%20Frodo%20and%20Sam%20discuss%20this%20advice:%0A%0A%20%20%20%22%20%20%60Then%20all%20the%20more%20need%20to%20fill%20our%20bottles%2C%27%20said%20Sam.%20%60But%0A%20%20%20%20there%20isn%27t%20any%20water%20up%20here:%20not%20a%20sound%20or%20a%20trickle%20have%20I%0A%20%20%20%20heard.%20And%20anyway%20Faramir%20said%20we%20were%20not%20to%20drink%20any%20water%0A%20%20%20%20in%20Morgul.%27%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27No%20water%20flowing%20out%20of%20Imlad%20Morgul%2C%20were%20his%20words%2C%27%20said%0A%20%20%20%20Frodo.%20%60We%20are%20not%20in%20that%20valley%20now%2C%20and%20if%20we%20came%20on%20a%20spring%0A%20%20%20%20it%20would%20be%20flowing%20into%20it%20and%20not%20out%20of%20it.%27%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27I%20wouldn%27t%20trust%20it%2C%27%20said%20Sam%2C%20%27not%20till%20I%20was%20dying%20of%20thirst.%0A%20%20%20%20There%27s%20a%20wicked%20feeling%20about%20this%20place.%27%20He%20sniffed.%20%27And%20a%0A%20%20%20%20smell%2C%20I%20fancy.%20Do%20you%20notice%20it%3F%20A%20queer%20kind%20of%20a%20smell%2C%20stuffy.%0A%20%20%20%20I%20don%27t%20like%20it.%27%22%0A%0ALater%20on%20they%20drink%20both%20of%20the%20water%20flowing%20in%20the%20valley%20between%20the%0AEphel%20D%FAath%0Aand%20the%20Morgai%20and%20from%20the%20highway%20cisterns.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A%0A%0A:%41nospam@nospam.net%20wrote:%0A%0A:%3E%20They%20clearly%20do%20have%20a%20will%20of%20their%20own%20as%20some%20chose%20to%20rebel.%0A%0A:%20Nowhere%20in%20scripture%20is%20this%20the%20case.%20This%20is%20part%20of%20the%20Christian%0A:%20angelology%20and%20has%20no%20scrptural%20basis%20whatsoever.%20For%20genuine%20poop%20on%0A:%20angels%20see%20the%20rabbinic%20midrashim.%0A%0A:%20The%20only%20time%20Satan%20is%20mentioned%20is%20in%20the%20book%20of%20Ayob%20%28Job%29%20and%20he%20is%0A:%20more%20of%20an%20advisor%20to%20G-D%20in%20that%20he%20suggests%20tests%20and%20procedures.%0A%0A:%20Bob%20Kolker%0A%0AYou%20said%20Judeo%20Christian%2C%20not%20Judaic.%20%20Christian%20beliefs%2C%20and%20Tolkien%27s%2C%0Ahold%20that%20angels%20had%20free%20will%20and%20were%20capable%20of%20rebelling.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ASure%20they%20did%2C%20they%20were%20called%20%22Hobbits%22.%20You%20didn%27t%20think%20that%20Bilbo%20was%0A%2Areally%2A%20writing%20his%20own%20stuff%20in%20Imladris%2C%20did%20you%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20wrote:%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%5E%5E%5E%5E%5E%5E%5E%5E%0A%3F%3FHave%20you%20got%20any%20ancestors%20in%20Russia%2C%20BTW%3F%20Last%20time%20I%20checked%20English%0Ahad%20no%20genitive%20case%20with%20an%20-a%20ending%2C%20but%20Russian%20still%20has%20it.%0A%0AArchie%0A%0A--%0A%22I%20have%20told%20my%20sons%20that%20they%20are%20not%20under%20any%0Acircumstances%20to%20take%20part%20in%20massacres%2C%20and%20that%0Athe%20news%20of%20massacres%20of%20enemies%20is%20not%20to%20fill%20them%0Awith%20satisfaction%20or%20glee.%22%0A%0AKurt%20Vonnegut%2C%20_Slaughterhouse-Five_%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20wrote:%0A%3Csnips%3E%0A%0AI%20disagree%2C%20at%20least%20about%20the%20American%20Civil%20War.%20%20By%20looking%20at%20the%20number%0Aof%20people%20involved%2C%20or%20number%20of%20casualties%2C%20it%20was%20a%20major%20war.%0A%0AI%20suspect%20we%27re%20getting%20off-topic%2C%20though%2C%20so%20I%20propose%20to%20leave%20it%20there.%0A%0AAndrew%0A--%0AAndrew%20Wells%0AReplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Robert%20J.%20Kolker%20wrote:%0ASpilling%20oil%20in%20seas%20%28Exxon%20Valdez%29%3B%20dumping%20radioactive%20waste%20into%0Arivers%20%28Techa%29%20or%20cyanide%20into%20lakes%20%28Kirgizia%29%20-%20sounds%20like%20Morgoth%20is%0Agiggling%20mad%2C%20doesn%27t%20it%3F%0A%0AArchie%0A%0A%0A--%0A%22I%20have%20told%20my%20sons%20that%20they%20are%20not%20under%20any%0Acircumstances%20to%20take%20part%20in%20massacres%2C%20and%20that%0Athe%20news%20of%20massacres%20of%20enemies%20is%20not%20to%20fill%20them%0Awith%20satisfaction%20or%20glee.%22%0A%0AKurt%20Vonnegut%2C%20_Slaughterhouse-Five_%0A%0A%0A
Sebastian%20Kapfer%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0A%0AI%27ll%20say%2C%20the%20original%20text%20there%20was%3B%0A%0A%22Orthanc%20is%20a%20tower%20in%20J.R.R.%20Tolkien%27s%20fantasy%20world%20of%20Middle-earth.%0AThe%20tower%20of%20black%20stone%20stands%20at%20the%20center%20of%20Isengard%27s%0Afortifications.%20During%20the%20initial%20portion%20of%20the%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings%0Atrilogy%2C%20it%20is%20the%20residence%20of%20Saruman%20until%20Isengard%20is%20attacked%20by%0AEnts%20and%20Gandalf%20forces%20Saruman%20and%20Gr%EDma%20%28Wormtongue%29%20out%20of%20the%0Atower.%0A%0AIn%20Tolkien%27s%20constructed%20languages%2C%20%22Orthanc%22%20had%20a%20dual%20meaning:%0AMount%20Fang%20in%20elvish%20and%20Cunning%20Mind%20in%20Rohan%27s%20language.%0A%0AIn%20Peter%20Jackson%27s%20movie%20The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings:%20The%20Two%20Towers%20the%0Atowers%20referred%20to%20are%20Barad-D%FBr%20and%20Orthanc%2C%20although%20in%20the%20book%20The%0ATwo%20Towers%20the%20towers%20are%20Barad-D%FBr%20and%20Minas%20Morgul.%22%0A%0A%0ALotR%20is%20technically%20not%20a%20trilogy%2C%20Gandalf%20did%20not%20force%20Saruman%20and%0AGrima%20out%20of%20Orthanc%20%28quite%20the%20opposite%29%2C%20and%20the%20%27two%20towers%27%20named%0Ain%20the%20book%20were%20Orthanc%20and%20Minas%20Morgul.%20%20If%20that%20is%20indicative%20of%0Amost%20of%20the%20entries%20there%20are%20likely%20ALOT%20of%20errors.%0A%0A%0AIt%20seems%20like%20anyone%20can%20go%20in%20and%20edit%20the%20text.%20%20That%20is%20both%20good%0Aand%20bad...%20it%20is%20easy%20to%20correct%20mistakes%2C%20but%20then%20it%20is%20just%20as%20easy%0Afor%20someone%20else%20to%20go%20and%20put%20them%20back%20in.%0A%0A%0A
Speaking%20Clock%20said:%0A%0AWell%2C%20at%20least%20it%20has%20the%20full%207%20stars%20unlike%20the%20original%20poster%20in%20this%0Athread%20suggested%20although%20they%20are%20in%20different%20places.%20I%20can%27t%20think%20of%20a%0Agood%20reason%20why%20PJ%20would%20have%20changed%20it%20from%20Tolkien%27s%20version%2C%20however.%0AIt%27s%20not%20like%20it%20%2Areally%2A%20affects%20the%20development%20of%20the%20story%20in%20any%20way.%0AIt%27s%20a%20detail%20that%20would%20have%20been%20just%20as%20much%20%22work%22%20and%20%22trouble%22%20to%20get%0Aright%20as%20to%20get%20wrong.%20Less%2C%20in%20fact%2C%20since%20someone%20had%20to%20take%20the%20time%20to%0A%22improve%22%20on%20it%20instead%20of%20just%20using%20Tolkien%27s%0A%0AHowever%2C%20I%20must%20say%20that%20both%20Pippin%20and%20Merry%20look%20quite%20good%20in%20their%20new%0Aduds%20%28star%20placement%20aside%29.%20No%20longer%20do%20they%20look%20like%20Shire%20country%0Abumpkins%20%28or%20young%20country%20gentlehobbits%3B%20I%27ve%20always%20thought%20that%0Amovie-Merry%20was%20by%20far%20the%20best%20dressed%20out%20of%20the%20main%20movie-Hobbits%2C%20what%0Awith%20his%20stylish%20vest%20and%20all%29%20which%2C%20I%20suppose%2C%20is%20the%20whole%20idea.%20And%20it%27s%0Aabout%20darn%20time%2C%20too%21%0A%0A%3CHan%20Strider%3E%0AThis%20ain%27t%20like%20stealin%27%20mushrooms%20back%20home%2C%20boy%21%0A%3C%2FHan%20Strider%3E%0A%0A%0AHmm%2C%20actually%20that%20looks%20like%20it%20might%20really%20be%20correct.%20I%20can%20only%20make%0Aout%20two%20stars%20%28well%2C%20dots%2C%20really%2C%20but%20I%20think%20they%27re%20stars%29%2C%20both%20just%20to%0Athe%20left%20%28the%20viewer%27s%20left%2C%20Aragorn%27s%20right%29%20of%20center%20and%20both%20above%20the%0Atree.%20Add%20another%20one%20just%20beneath%20those%20two%20and%20farther%20to%20the%20left%2C%20take%0Atheir%20mirror%20images%2C%20and%20stick%20another%20one%20up%20top%2C%20and%20you%27ve%20got%207%20stars%0Aall%20in%20the%20right%20places%20and%20room%20for%20a%20crown%20on%20top.%0A%0AMoreover%2C%20where%20did%20he%20get%20that%20armor%3F%20Did%20whoever-brought-him-Anduril%20bring%0Ahim%20that%20too%3F%20Did%20he%20pick%20it%20up%20in%20Minas%20Tirith%3F%20Did%20Gimli%20forge%20it%20for%20him%0Aout%20of%20a%20hubcap%3F%0A%0AAs%20far%20as%20some%20of%20the%20other%20pictures%20on%20that%20page%20go:%0A-Frodo%20seems%20to%20be%20using%20Galadriel%27s%20Phial%20in%20Shelob%27s%20lair%20here%2C%20but%0AGaladriel%20did%20not%20give%20that%20to%20him%20in%20the%20theatrical%20version%20of%20FotR.%20How%0Aare%20they%20going%20to%20explain%20it%3F%20I%20think%20it%20will%20seem%20a%20little%20out%20of%20place%20to%0Apeople%20who%20have%20only%20seen%20the%20theatrical%20versions.%0ASam:%20Well%2C%20Mr.%20Frodo%2C%20this%20is%20a%20right%20dark%20place%20and%20no%20mistake.%20I%20wish%20I%0Ahad%20a%20bit%20o%27%20light...%0AFrodo:%20Why%2C%20Sam%21%20That%20reminds%20me%21%20During%20an%20offscreen%20moment%2C%20Galadriel%20just%0Aso%20happened%20to%20give%20me%20this%20bottle%20that%20glows%20in%20the%20dark%20and%20I%27ve%20never%0Ashown%20it%20to%20anyone%20or%20even%20mentioned%20it%20to%20anyone%20since%21%20How%2C%20fortuitous%21%0A%0A-Is%20that%20Lurtz%20in%20that%20pic%20or%20just%20some%20random%20Uruk%20who%20just%20happens%20to%20look%0Aa%20lot%20like%20him%20%28all%20Uruk%27s%20look%20alike%3F%29%3F%0A%0A-I%20%2Alove%2A%20that%20pic%20of%20Gimli%20and%20Legolas.%20But%20isn%27t%20Legolas%20aiming%20a%20little%0Atoo%20far%20away%3F%20Looks%20to%20me%20like%20they%27ve%20got%20some%20more%20pressing%20issues%20closer%0Ato%20home.%20Oh%2C%20well%2C%20at%20least%20Gimli%20looks%20focused%20at%20the%20task%20at%20hand...%0A%0A-Mostly%20liked%20the%20rest%20of%20the%20pics%20too%2C%20but%20not%20enough%20to%20comment%20on%20all%20of%0Athem.%20Plot%20changes%20aside%2C%20I%20think%20the%20movies%20are%20simply%20gorgeous.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Stan%20Brown%20%20in%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20scripsit:%0A%0A%22Your%20time%20may%20come%22%A0%3F%20That%20doesn%27t%20look%20like%20a%20%2Astrong%2A%20hint%20to%0Ame.%20I%27d%20say%20Frodo%20was%20simply%20trying%20to%20comfort%20Sam.%0A%0A%0AI%20read%20the%20FAQ%2C%20which%20mentions%20the%20Appendix%20B%20%28%2Asigh%2A%20I%20always%20seem%20to%0Aoverlook%20the%20Appendices%29:%20%22Among%20them%20the%20tradition%20is%20handed%20down%0Afrom%20Elanor%20that%20Samwise%20passed%20the%20Towers%2C%20and%20went%20to%20the%20Grey%0AHavens.%20and%20passed%20over%20Sea%2C%20last%20of%20the%20Ring-bearers.%20So%20the%20matter%27s%0Asettled.%0A%0AI%20find%20it%20a%20bit%20disappointing%20that%20Sam%20eventually%20sailed%20to%20the%0AWest.%20He%20was%20the%20only%20true%20Hobbit%20of%20the%20Fellowship%2C%20and%20I%20thought%2C%0Awith%20Frodo%20in%20the%20West%2C%20and%20Merry%20and%20Pippin%20finally%20dying%20in%20Gondor%2C%0Athat%20Sam%20would%20have%20died%20in%20the%20Shire...%0A%0A--%0AMarie-Lan%20Nguyen%0A%AB%A0Et%20ideo%20ego%20adulescentulos%20existimo%20in%20scholis%20stultissimos%20fieri%2C%0Aquia%20nihil%20ex%20his%2C%20quae%20in%20usu%20habemus%2C%20aut%20audiunt%20aut%20vident.%A0%BB%20%28P%E9trone%29%0A%3Chttp:%2F%2Fwww.pip-pip.org%2F%3E%0A%0A%0A
Stan%20Brown%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0AYou%27re%20right.%20I%20habitually%20forget%20that%20distinction%20in%20English%20as%20it%20doesn%27t%0Areally%20exist%20in%20Danish.%0A%0A%0AThe%20early%20Danish%20kings%20number%20e.g.%20several%20Eriks%20and%20several%0AValdemars%2C%20but%20even%20though%20they%20do%20technically%20have%20numbers%2C%20they%0Aare%20normally%20distinguished%20by%20their%20bynames%20-%20e.g.%20Erik%20Menved%2C%0AErik%20Ejegod%20and%20Erik%20Klipping.%0A%0AI%20suspect%20that%20the%20same%20could%20apply%20to%20the%20Masters%20%28wasn%27t%20one%20of%20them%0Aat%20least%20remembered%20as%20%27the%20Old%27%20-%20the%20Bullroarer%20was%2C%20IIRC%2C%20a%20Took%29.%20It%0Awould%2C%20IMO%2C%20be%20more%20consistent%20with%20my%20impression%20of%20Hobbit%20culture%0Aif%20they%20used%20descriptive%20bynames%20instead%20of%20just%20the%20number.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20mail%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Stan%20Brown%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AWell%2C%20it%20%2Adid%2A%20begin%20at%20least%20as%20a%20sequel%20to%20the%20Hobbit.%20And%20the%0ASilmarillion%20was%20not%20published%20at%20the%20time.%20And%20LotR%20takes%20place%20%2Aafter%2A%20the%0AHobbit.%20You%20might%20say%20that%20LotR%20is%20a%20sequel%20to%20TH%20and%20that%20the%20Sil%20is%20a%0Aprequel.%20%3B%29%0A%0AIn%20any%20case%2C%20LotR%20is%20a%20sequel%20to%20%2Asomething%2A%20and%20a%20very%20good%20one%20at%20that%20%28as%0AI%27m%20sure%20most%20of%20the%20people%20here%20would%20agree%29%20which%20was%20my%20point.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Stephen%20wrote:%0A%0A%0AMy%20reference%20to%20%22published%22%20works%20is%20a%20reference%20to%20that%20which%20Tolkien%20released%0Aduring%20his%20lifetime.%20%20Silmarilion%20is%20obviously%20not%20included.%0A..%0ATolkien%20never%20intended%20to%20%22replace%22%20any%20published%20writings%2C%20merely%20add%20to%20them.%0A%20%22Replacing%22%20is%20inconsistent%20with%20his%20whole%20approach.%20%20Even%20the%20original%0Achapter%205%20of%20the%20Hobbit%20was%20not%20%22replaced%22%20so%20much%20as%20it%20was%20retained%2C%0Aexplained%2C%20and%20developed%20on.%20%20Tolkien%20understood%20that%20inconsistency%20tends%20to%0Aspoil%20suspension%20of%20disbelief.%20%20It%20is%20cheating%2C%20bad%20storytelling%2C%20and%20is%0Adisloyal%20to%20one%27s%20readers.%0A%0ATolkien%20may%20well%20have%20intended%20to%20radically%20revise%20parts%20of%20the%20Silmarillion%2C%0Abut%20that%20is%20a%20totally%20different%20matter.%20%20Since%20it%20was%20not%20yet%20published%2C%0ATolkien%20felt%20free%20to%20do%20what%20he%20wished.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20I%20do%20give%20higher%20marks%20to%20Silmarillion%20than%20other%20stuff%2C%20because%20it%0Acontains%20developed%20writings.%20%20I%20believe%2C%20therefore%2C%20that%20it%20takes%20precedents%0Aover%20writings%20that%20have%20not%20gone%20beyond%20the%20first-draft%20stage%2C%20even%20if%20such%0Awritings%20come%20later.%0A%0AIt%20is%20true%20that%20we%20do%20not%20know%20what%20form%20the%20Silmarillion%20would%20have%20taken%20had%0Ahe%20finished%20it%2C%20which%20is%20why%20it%20is%20far%20less%20%22canon%22%20than%20his%20published%20stuff.%0A%0AConsistency%20of%20writing%20is%20hard%20work.%20%20That%27s%20one%20of%20the%20reason%20one%20has%0Asecond-drafts%2C%20to%20iron%20out%20inconsistencies%2C%20including%20inconsistencies%20with%20what%0Aone%20has%20already%20released.%0A%0AThe%20writing%20we%20are%20talking%20about%20here%20is%20a%20barely-legible%20first%20draft%2C%20written%0Ain%20the%20last%20month%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20life.%20%20One%20may%20presume%20that%20he%20did%20not%20write%20it%0Awith%20the%20intention%20of%20immediately%20throwing%20it%20in%20the%20trash%2C%20but%20apart%20from%0Athat%2C%20there%20is%20no%20knowing%20what%20he%20would%20have%20done%20with%20it%20had%20he%20survived.%0AEither%20of%20two%20things%20would%20have%20happened%20-%20either%20he%20would%20have%20thought%20better%0Aof%20it%20entirely%2C%20or%20else%20he%20would%20have%20rewritten%20it%20countless%20times%20in%20order%20to%0Adevelop%20and%20improve%20it.%20%20One%20thing%20that%20could%20easily%20have%20happened%20%28in%20light%20of%0Ahis%20known%20devotion%20to%20consistency%29%20is%20that%20%28assuming%20there%20was%20actual%0Ainconsistency%29%20he%20would%20have%20realized%20that%20it%20contradicted%20earlier%20things%20he%0Ahad%20written%2C%20and%20revised%20it%20to%20bring%20them%20in%20harmony%20-%20resulting%20in%20a%20complex%0Aand%20nuanced%20tale.%0A%0AIt%20seems%20absurd%20to%20treat%20a%20barely%20legible%20first%20draft%20as%20the%20height%20of%0Acanonicity%20just%20because%20it%20was%20the%20last%20thing%20he%20wrote%2C%20and%20then%20complain%20that%0Ait%20isn%27t%20very%20good%20or%20contains%20inconsistencies%2C%20etc.%20etc.%0A%0AI%20note%20that%2C%20as%20late%20as%20January%2025%2C%201971%2C%20Tolkien%20was%20still%20saying%2C%20in%20letter%20%23%0A320%2C%20that%20Galadriel%20was%20a%20%22leader%20in%20the%20rebellion%20against%20the%20Valar%22.%0A%0AI%20don%27t%20really%20see%20a%20contradiction%20in%20letter353.%20%20%22Committed%20no%20evil%20deeds%22%20is%0Ano%20contradiction.%20%20The%20Valar%20do%20not%20represent%20God%2C%20and%20disobedience%20to%20them%20or%0Arebellion%20against%20them%20is%20not%20per%20se%20Evil.%20%20Tolkien%27s%20main%20point%20seems%20to%20be%0Athat%20she%20bore%20no%20role%20in%20the%20kinslaying%20or%20Feanor%27s%20other%20sins.%20%20He%20writes%20that%0A%22She%20was%20an%20enemy%20of%20Feanor%22.%20%20No%20problem%20here.%20%20Those%20who%20rebelled%20against%20the%0AValar%20need%20hardly%20be%20monolithic%2C%20or%20friendly%20to%20each%20other.%20%20He%20further%20states%0Athat%2C%20had%20it%20not%20been%20for%20Feanor%27s%20rebellion%2C%20she%20would%20have%20asked%20to%20leave%2C%0Aand%20her%20request%20would%20have%20been%20granted.%20%20No%20contradiction%20here%20at%20all.%0AThat%27s%20just%20a%20might-have-been%2C%20because%20what%20%2Aactually%2A%20happened%20was%20that%20Feanor%0A%2Adid%2A%20rebel%2C%20and%20the%20Valar%20therefore%20banned%20%2Aall%2A%20emigration.%20%20Galadriel%0Awilfully%20defied%20this%20ban%2C%20and%20hence%20became%20a%20rebel%20against%20the%20Valar.%20%20%22Left%0Aindependently%22%20presumably%20means%20%22independently%20of%20Feanor%20and%20his%20bunch%22%20-%20not%0Anecessarily%20that%20she%20left%20alone%20%28It%20seems%20extremely%20unlikely%20that%20she%20would%0Ahave%20travelled%20to%20ME%20solo%29.%20%20%22Other%20Noldor%22%20presumably%20means%20Noldor%20other%20than%0Aher%20own%20followers.%0A%0ARead%20properly%2C%20letter%20353%20clearly%20states%20that%20Galadriel%20disobeyed%20%28=%20%22rebelled%0Aagainst%22%29%20the%20Valar.%0A%0A%0A
Stephen%20wrote:%0A%0AIt%20may%20indeed%20be%20patently%20false%2C%20but%20it%20is%20also%20patently%20false%20for%20you%20to%20say%0Athat%20I%20said%20it.%0A%0A%0AI%20do%20not%20believe%20I%20have%20said%20anything%20that%20implies%20the%20contrary.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20I%0Asaid%20much%20the%20same%20thing%20earlier%20in%20the%20discussion.%0A%0A%0AI%20have%20nothing%20against%20the%20above%20statement%2C%20so%20long%20as%20it%20is%20not%20construed%20to%0Amean%20that%20any%20such%20material%20takes%20precedence%20over%20finished%20material%20that%0ATolkien%20chose%20to%20publish.%0A%0A%0ANo%20doubt.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20I%20made%20that%20very%20point%20earlier%20in%20the%20discussion.%20%20In%0Aresponse%2C%20others%20have%20posted%20citing%20material%20which%20they%20claim%20shows%20a%0Acontradiction%20between%20the%20published%20commentary%20in%20Road%20Goes%20Ever%20On%2C%20and%20a%0Abarely%20legible%20%22adumbration%22%20that%20Tolkien%20scribbled%20in%20the%20last%20month%20of%20his%0Alife.%20%20I%20remain%20skeptical%20that%20there%20actually%20is%20a%20contradiction%2C%20but%20in%20any%0Aevent%2C%20I%20believe%20Tolkien-published%20material%20takes%20precedence%20over%20that%0Aposthumously%20published.%0A%0A%0AAs%20someone%20just%20kindly%20pointed%20out%20to%20me%2C%20Tolkien%2C%20during%20his%20lifetime%2C%0Apublished%20some%20commentary%20regarding%20Galadriel%27s%20ban%20in%20Road%20Goes%20Ever%20On.%0A%0A%0AI%20know.%20%20That%20is%20often%20the%20case%20with%20unpublished%20materials%20before%20they%20are%0Apublished.%20%20They%20do%20not%20arrive%20fully%20formed%20onto%20the%20page%20from%20the%20author%27s%0Ahead.%0A%0A%0AThat%20is%20pure%20speculation%20on%20your%20part.%20%20It%20seems%20to%20me%20unlikely%20that%20any%20such%0Aedits%20would%20be%20required.%20%20Seems%20to%20me%20far%20more%20likely%20that%20the%20barely%20legible%0A%22adumbration%22%20would%20be%20the%20one%20receiving%20major%20edits%2C%20had%20Tolkien%20survived%20to%0Ado%20any%20more%20with%20it.%0A%0A%0AThe%20phrase%20%22other%20stuff%22%20means%20just%20that.%20%20It%20does%20not%20mean%20%22any%20and%20all%20other%0Astuff.%22%20%20I%20have%20absolutely%20no%20problem%20with%20the%20claim%20that%20certain%20other%0Awritings%20may%20be%20equally%20well%20developed%20as%20that%20which%20was%20published%20in%20the%0ASilmarillion.%20%20But%20I%20was%20not%20discussing%20such%20writings.%20%20The%20above%20paragraph%0Asays%20only%20what%20it%20says:%20%20that%20I%20regard%20Silmarillion%20%28the%20most%20obvious%20example%0Aof%20an%20unpublished%20but%20fairly%20developed%20writing%29%20as%20more%20canon%20than%20%20writings%0Athat%20never%20went%20beyond%20the%20first%20draft%20stage%2C%20even%20if%20those%20other%20writing%20came%0Alater.%0A%0ASpecifically%2C%20we%20were%20discussing%20a%20piece%20of%20writing%20that%20never%20even%20reached%20the%0A%22first%20draft%22%20stage.%20%20We%20were%20discussing%2C%20in%20particular%2C%20a%20barely%20legible%0A%22adumbration%22%20that%20Tolkien%20scrawled%20in%20the%20last%20month%20of%20his%20life.%20%20He%0Acertainly%20never%20meant%20to%20publish%20it%20in%20that%20form%2C%20and%20there%20is%20no%20way%20of%0Aknowing%20what%20form%20it%20would%20have%20taken%20had%20he%20had%20a%20chance%20to%20work%20on%20it%0Afurther.%0A%0A-%20John%20Whelan%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%5B...%5D%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0AVery%20good%2C%20Steuard.%0A%0AI%20think%20the%20length%20is%20justified%20-%20the%20question%20is%20not%20one%20to%20be%20treated%0Awith%20a%20short%20dismissal%20of%20CT%27s%20work%20as%20mere%20%27tampering%27%20or%20something%20of%0Athat%20kin.%0AInclusion%20of%20the%20history%20of%20the%20text%20seems%20unavoidable%20when%20you%20also%0Awish%20to%20explain%20the%20basis%20for%20CT%27s%20decisions.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:NN%25Na.82$41nospam@nospam.net...%0AThe%20cones%20were%20simply%20colliery%20spoil-heaps%20%28known%20as%20%27pit-bonks%27%20in%20this%0Apart%20of%20the%20world%29.%20%20I%20have%20always%20thought%20that%20this%20description%20-%20and%20that%0Aof%20the%20post-Sharkey%20Shire%20-%20were%20based%20on%20Tolkien%27s%20move%20from%20the%20village%20of%0ASarehole%20to%20Central%20Birmingham%20after%20the%20death%20of%20his%20mother%2C%20around%20100%0Ayears%20ago.%20%20At%20the%20time%2C%20Sarehole%20was%20an%20isolated%20agricultural%20village%2C%20and%0ALadywood%2C%20where%20the%20Oratory%20is%2C%20was%20the%20scene%20of%20heavy%20industry%20%28there%20was%20a%0Afactory%20building%20steam%20engines%20very%20close%20to%20it%29.%0ASpoil%20heaps%20were%20very%20common%20in%20Birmingham%20and%20the%20Black%20Country%20%28which%20was%0Anot%20called%20that%20for%20nothing%29%20although%20they%20have%20mostly%20been%20removed%0Anowadays%3B%20but%20there%20were%20still%20quite%20a%20few%20not%20so%20long%20ago.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:W7USa.16$41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0A%0AWell%20-%20and%20for%20all%20these%20years%20I%20thought%20that%20you%20were%20male.%0A%3Bo%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%20I%27ve%20actually%20written%20a%20little%20CGI%20script%20to%20help%20people%20with%20that%0A:%20very%20question.%20%20You%20tell%20it%20the%20sorts%20of%20things%20you%20like%20to%20read%2C%20and%0A:%20it%20suggests%20a%20reasonable%20order%20in%20which%20to%20read%20the%20books.%20%20It%20will%0A:%20even%20suggest%20which%20parts%20of%20each%20book%20you%27re%20likely%20to%20enjoy%20most.%20%20%28I%0A:%20keep%20meaning%20to%20go%20back%20and%20tweak%20it%20at%20some%20point%2C%20but%20most%20people%0A:%20who%20have%20commented%20on%20it%20seem%20to%20like%20it.%29%20%20You%20can%20find%20the%20list%20from%0A%0A:%20http:%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%2Fbooks.html%0A%0A:%20Let%20me%20know%20what%20you%20think%21%0A:%20%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0AI%20happened%20to%20look%20at%20your%20script%2C%20and%20something%20jumped%20out%20at%20me.%20%20Your%0Aphrase%20%22Some%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20about%20Middle-earth%20are%20considered%20to%20be%0Amore%20%22canonical%22%20%28trustworthy%29%20than%20others.%22%20strikes%20me%20as%20odd.%20%20%22Canonical%22%0Aand%20%22trustworthy%22%20are%20not%20synonyms%2C%20and%20it%20is%20strange%20to%20imply%20that%0Asome%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20are%20untrustworthy.%20%20Untrustworthy%20is%20such%0Aa%20negative%20word%20in%20my%20mind.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%20Quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20in%20article%0A:%20%3Cbecmih$2425$41nospam@nospam.net%3E:%0A:%3E%20Steuard%20Jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote:%0A:%3E%20:%20I%27ve%20actually%20written%20a%20little%20CGI%20script%20to%20help%20people%20with%20that%0A:%3E%20:%20very%20question.%20%20You%20tell%20it%20the%20sorts%20of%20things%20you%20like%20to%20read%2C%0A:%3E%20:%20and%20it%20suggests%20a%20reasonable%20order%20in%20which%20to%20read%20the%20books.%0A%0A:%3E%20Your%20phrase%20%22Some%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20about%20Middle-earth%20are%0A:%3E%20considered%20to%20be%20more%20%22canonical%22%20%28trustworthy%29%20than%20others.%22%0A:%3E%20strikes%20me%20as%20odd.%20%20%22Canonical%22%20and%20%22trustworthy%22%20are%20not%20synonyms%2C%0A:%3E%20and%20it%20is%20strange%20to%20imply%20that%20some%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20writings%20are%0A:%3E%20untrustworthy.%20%20Untrustworthy%20is%20such%20a%20negative%20word%20in%20my%20mind.%0A%0A:%20They%20aren%27t%20synonyms%2C%20true%2C%20but%20among%20their%20definitions%20are%20some%20that%0A:%20are%20reasonably%20similar.%20:%29%20%20I%20was%20very%20hesitant%20to%20just%20say%0A:%20%22canonical%22%2C%20because%20I%20feared%20that%20many%20people%20wouldn%27t%20quite%20know%0A:%20what%20I%20meant.%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A:%20To%20be%20honest%2C%20though%2C%20I%20don%27t%20see%20%22trustworthy%22%20as%20being%20_terribly_%0A:%20wrong.%20%20In%20context%2C%20I%20think%20it%27s%20clear%20that%20Tolkien%20could%20in%20no%20sense%0A:%20have%20been%20_lying_:%20it%27s%20his%20invented%20world%2C%20after%20all.%20%20What%20else%0A:%20could%20it%20mean%3F%20%20Well%2C%20%22trustworthy%22%20can%20mean%20%22reliable%22%2C%20and%20a%20very%0A:%20vague%20definition%20of%20%22canonical%22%20in%20our%20case%20might%20be%20%22a%20reliable%20guide%0A:%20to%20Tolkien%27s%20developed%20vision%20of%20Middle-earth%22.%20%20%28See%20my%20essay%0A:%20%22Tolkien%27s%20Parish%22%20for%20a%20far%20longer%20discussion.%29%20%20I%20guess%20I%20could%20have%0A:%20said%20%22reliable%22%20instead%20of%20%22trustworthy%22%2C%20but%20%22unreliable%22%20is%20also%20a%0A:%20negative%20word%3B%20I%20think%20you%27d%20still%20object.%20%20Maybe%20I%20could%20say%0A:%20%22finalized%22%2C%20but%20doesn%27t%20come%20close%20to%20suggesting%20the%20vague%20definition%0A:%20above...%20I%20think%20it%27s%20even%20less%20clear%20than%20%22trustworthy%22.%0A%0A:%20At%20any%20rate%2C%20what%20other%20way%20of%20clarifying%20the%20meaning%20of%20%22canonical%22%0A:%20as%20we%20use%20it%20here%20would%20you%20suggest%3F%20%20%28I%20wouldn%27t%20use%20anything%20longer%0A:%20than%20two%20or%20three%20words%2C%20and%20one%20word%20would%20certainly%20be%20best.%29%20%20Maybe%0A:%20I%20could%20just%20make%20%22canonical%22%20a%20hyperlink%20to%20my%20essay.%20:%29%0A%0A:%20%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0AI%20am%20not%20sure%20I%20really%20have%20a%20suggestion%20for%20you.%20%20Perhaps%20a%20footnote%0Ato%20a%20longer%20definition%20would%20be%20best.%20%20But%20then%20again%2C%20I%20doubt%20most%0Apeople%20even%20notice.%20%20Part%20of%20the%20problem%2C%20as%20you%20mention%2C%20is%20that%0A%22canonical%22%20is%20not%20really%20well%20defined%20for%20Tolkien%27s%20Middle-Earth%2C%0Aand%20any%20attempt%20at%20one%20or%20two%20word%20definition%20is%20going%20to%20be%20misleading.%0AI%20know%20you%20have%20made%20some%20effort%20elsewhere%20to%20define%20what%20you%20mean%0Aby%20canonical%2C%20but%20for%20example%20%22finalized%22%20is%20also%20not%20really%20a%20good%0Adefinition.%20%20What%20was%20the%20%22final%22%20version%20of%20the%20origin%20of%20the%20Sun%20and%0AMoon%3F%20%20Many%20references%20in%20the%20published%20%22Lord%20of%20the%20Rings%22%20imply%0Athe%20Sun%20and%20Moon%20were%20created%20long%20before%20the%20Elves%20and%20Men%20awoke%2C%0Aand%20that%20seems%20to%20be%20Tolkien%27s%20final%20intent%2C%20but%20do%20you%20consider%0A%22Myths%20Transformed%22%20more%20canonical%20than%20the%20published%20Silmarillion%3F%0A%0AAnother%20part%20of%20the%20%22problem%22%20is%20that%20you%20and%20I%20have%20very%20different%0Aideas%20about%20the%20importance%20of%20%22canonical%22.%20%20Personally%20I%20am%0Afar%20more%20interested%20in%20the%20evolution%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20ideas%20than%0Ain%20the%20%22final%22%20form%20they%20appeared.%20%20In%20some%20cases%20I%20find%0Athe%20earlier%20versions%20more%20interesting%2C%20but%20usually%20it%20is%0Ain%20no%20particular%20version%20I%20am%20most%20interested%2C%20but%20in%20the%20way%0Athe%20different%20versions%20are%20related.%20%20So%20to%20me%2C%20implying%20that%0Aany%20of%20the%20versions%20are%20somehow%20not%20trustworthy%20just%20seems%0Aodd.%20%20But%20to%20each%20their%20own.%0A%0AStephen%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AI%2C%20personally%2C%20prefer%20reading%20a%20one-volume%20book%20than%203%20separate%20books.%0AUnfortunately%2C%20both%20one-volume%20editions%20I%20have%20owned%20%28one%20hardback%2C%20one%0Asoftback%29%20have%20suffered%20spine%20meltdown%20due%20to%20heavy%20use%20and%20heavy%20strain%20on%0Athat%20giant%2C%20extended%20spine.%0A%0AThe%20hardcover%20cracked%20and%20split%20all%20the%20way%20down%20the%20middle.%20Eventually%20both%0Ahalves%20fell%20off%20and%20the%20two%20large%20front%20and%20back%20pieces%20stayed%20on%20only%0Abecause%20they%20were%20glued%20to%20the%20pieces%20of%20papaer%20next%20to%20them.%0A%0AThe%20softcover%20has%20only%20recently%20has%20begun%20to%20disintigrate%2C%20but%20chunks%20of%0Apages%20%2810%20or%20so%20at%20a%20time%29%20have%20started%20to%20fall%20out.%20The%20main%20book%20is%20now%0Amissing%20from%20approximately%20the%20Prologue%20to%20Bree.%20To%20be%20fair%2C%20though%2C%20I%20have%0Aseriously%20abused%20that%20book%2C%20cramming%20it%20into%20overstuffed%20bags%20which%20then%20get%0Athrown%20around%2C%20etc.%0A%0AOf%20course%2C%20the%20only%20non-one-volume%20LotR%20book%20I%20ever%20owned%20%28a%20softcover%20copy%0Aor%20FotR%29%20split%20down%20%2Aits%2A%20spine%20too%20and%20started%20to%20peal%2C%20so%20I%20guess%20I%20just%0Aover-use%20my%20LotR%20books...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ANo%2C%20duh%21%20Thanks%20for%20nuttin%27%21%20:P%0A%0A%0AOK%2C%20you%20people%20have%20convinced%20me.%20I%27ve%20placed%20my%20order%20and%20expect%20to%20get%20it%0Asome%20time%20this%20y%E9n%20but%20I%27m%20not%20getting%20my%20hopes%20up...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20wrote:%0A%0A%0ADon%27t%20have%20access%2Ftime%20to%20check%20it%20out%2C%20but%20my%20impression%20was%20there%20was%0Aother%20some%20references%20to%20this.%20%20As%20to%20the%20specific%20identification%20of%20their%0Anature%2C%20only%20the%20five%20%27chiefs%27%20are%20known%20%28from%20other%20material%29%20as%20being%0AMaiar%2C%20the%20others%20%28if%20we%20accept%20their%20existence%29%20could%20have%20been%20or%20not%0AMaiar.%20%20We%20simply%20have%20nothing%20known%20that%20speaks%20to%20this.%20%20We%20simply%0Acannot%20assume%20they%20were%20of%20the%20same%20kind%2C%20while%20admitting%20it%20is%20a%0Aspeculative%20possibility.%0A%0A%0AAgain%2C%20there%20is%20only%20room%20for%20speculation%20here.%20%20There%20are%20references%20to%0Awizards%2Fwizardy%20not%20seemingly%20in%20connection%20with%20the%20five%20known%20Istari.%0AThere%20was%20a%20White%20Council%2C%20whose%20numbers%20are%20not%20made%20clear.%20%20If%20its%0Anumbers%20were%20greater%20than%20than%20Gandalf%2C%20Saruman%2C%20Radagast%2C%20Elrond%2C%0AGlorfindel%2C%20%3FCeleborn%2C%20%3FCirdan%20and%20Galadriel%2C%20then%20its%20inability%20to%20come%0Ato%20a%20decision%20about%20doing%20something%20about%20the%20Necromancer%20and%20other%0Amatters%20makes%20more%20sense.%20%20This%20is%20not%20proof%2C%20but%20makes%20narrative%20driven%0Asense.%20%20I%20don%27t%20know%20if%20there%20were%20more%20of%20the%20Istari%20around%20in%20ME%3B%20but%20at%0Aleast%20when%20Tolkien%20wrote%20the%20above%20selection%2C%20%20he%20seems%20to%20have%20reserving%0Athe%20possibility%20that%20there%20were%20more.%20%20The%20case%20for%20exactly%20five%20or%20more%0Athan%20five%20simply%20remains%20unproven%20%28and%20probably%20unprovable%29.%20%20At%20least%20in%0Amy%20case%2C%20any%20argument%20about%20%22canoncity%22%20about%20any%20particular%20text%20on%20this%0Aon%20any%20other%20subject%20brings%20nothing%20worth%20noting%20in%20any%20discussion.%0ASimply%20put%2C%20the%20existing%20corpus%20of%20texts%20is%20ambiguous%20on%20numbers%20of%0AIstari.%0A%0A%0AAnd%20you%20are%20totally%20%27permitted%27%20to%20do%20so%2C%20or%20change%20your%20mind.....%0A%0A%0AI%20have%20wondered%20on%20this%20point.%20%20While%20the%20joining%20with%20the%20physical%20form%0Awas%20voluntary%2C%20my%20impression%20was%20that%20the%20five%20Istari%20did%20not%20have%20the%0Afreedom%20to%20cast%20off%20these%20forms.%20%20As%20to%20your%20other%20suggestion%2C%20I%20now%20have%0Aa%20whole%20new%20idea%20what%20Gandalf%20was%20doing%20in%20the%20%22Lost%20Years%22%20when%20there%20is%0Ano%20record%20of%20him.%20%20Why%20the%20Old%20Goat%2C%20I%20never%20knew%20you%20%20.......%20%20:-%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20wrote:%0A%0A%0AYes%2C%20that%27s%20my%20conviction%20as%20well.%0A%0A%0AGood%20resource.%20%20Yes%2C%20by%20FACT%20I%20%28poorly%29%20implied%20the%20%22canonical%22%0Asources%20%28which%2C%20by%20definition%2C%20aren%27t%20really%20canonical%2C%20since%0Athere%20is%20no%20common%20agreement%20on%20what%20the%20canon%20is%29.%20I%20guess%20my%0Awhole%20post%20was%20not%20very%20clear.%20My%20only%20point%20was%20to%20try%20and%0Aassert%20that%2C%20since%20Bilbo%20and%2C%20later%2C%20Sam%2C%20crossed%20west%2C%20the%0Awhole%20rigmarole%20about%20Arwen%20%22ceding%22%20or%20giving%20up%20her%20place%20to%0AFrodo%20didn%27t%20make%20much%20sense.%0A%0AJust%20for%20the%20record%2C%20I%20do%20accept%20Tolkien%27s%20letters%20as%20canon%3B%20I%0Adidn%27t%20notice%20Sam%20is%20explicitly%20mentioned%20in%20the%20letter%20quoted%21%0ATherefore%2C%20I%20agree%20that%20letter%20provides%20enough%20evidence%20to%20prove%0ASam%20crossed%20west.%0A%0A%0ARegards%2C%0A%0A--%0AGonzalo%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20probably%20differ%20from%20everyone%20else%2C%20in%20that%20I%20just%20assumed%20that%20he%20was%0Aretracing%20his%20steps%20backwards.%20%20He%20went%20that%20way%20previously%2C%20but%20in%20reverse%2C%0Awhilst%20fleeing%20Mordor%2C%20hiding%20from%20the%20orcs%20that%20persued%20him.%20%20When%20he%20said%2C%0A%22...this%20way...%22%2C%20he%20was%20referring%20simply%20to%20the%20path%2C%20not%20to%20the%20direction%0Aof%20travel.%0A%0A%28Is%20this%20an%20appropriate%20place%20to%20insert%20a%20%22Walk%20this%20way...%22%20joke%3F%29%0APatient:%20%22I%27ve%20got%20a%20billiard%20ball%20lodged%20in%20my%20rectum.%22%0ADoctor:%20%22Could%20you%20walk%20this%20way%2C%20please%3F%22%0APatient:%20%22If%20I%20could%20walk%20that%20way...%22%0A%0A--%0ARegards%2C%0A%0AMichael%20Cole%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Steuard%20Jensen%20wrote:%0A%3Csnips%3E%0A%0AI%20tried%20that%2C%20and%20my%20email%20got%20bounced%20straight%20back.%0A%0AAndrew%0A--%0AAndrew%20Wells%0AReplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Sue%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AYou%20wouldn%27t%20include%20_Unfinished%20Tales_%3F%0A%0AOr%20you%20just%20forgot%20about%20it%3F%20%3B%29%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
T.A.%20wrote:%0A%0A%0AThough%20Pippin%20may%20have%20meant%20to%20ask%20about%20Frodo%27s%20hope%20for%20returning%2C%20the%0A%22fool%27s%20hope%22%20that%20Gandalf%20is%20referring%20to%20here%2C%20is%20the%20hope%20that%20Frodo%20will%0Asucceed%20in%20getting%20the%20Ring%20to%20the%20fire.%20%20He%20is%20quoting%20Denethor%2C%20who%20does%20not%0Acare%20whether%20Frodo%20returns%20or%20not%2C%20but%20only%20about%20whether%20the%20quest%20succeeds%2C%0Aand%20considers%20Gandalf%27s%20plan%20to%20be%20the%20plan%20of%20a%20fool.%0A%0A%0ANo%20doubt%20someone%20will.%20%20However%2C%20the%20statement%20has%20adequate%20support%20in%20%22Shadow%0Aof%20the%20Past%22.%20%20Gandalf%20already%20knew%2C%20at%20the%20beginning%2C%20that%20Frodo%20could%20not%0Asucceed%20solely%20by%20virtue%20of%20his%20own%20strength%2C%20and%20told%20Frodo%20as%20much%20at%20the%0Avery%20start.%20%20It%20is%20established%2C%20at%20the%20very%20start%2C%20that%20Frodo%20lacks%20the%0Astrength%20of%20will%20to%20try%20to%20directly%20harm%20the%20Ring.%20%20And%20that%20is%20how%20it%20played%0Aout.%20%20Frodo%27s%20strength%20failed%2C%20but%20the%20Quest%20succeeded%20in%20spite%20of%20this%20by%20the%0Aintervention%20of%20Gollum%20and%20some%20incredible%20good%20luck%20%28of%20Fate%2C%20or%20Destiny%2C%20or%0AGod%2C%20or%20whatever%20you%20want%20to%20call%20it%29.%0A%0A%0A
Taemon%20said:%0A%0ADunno.%20Sorta%20just%20passing%20through.%20Thanks%20for%20noticing%20though.%20:%29%0A%0ASketch%20I%20had%20done%20by%20one%20of%20them%20pencil%20caricature%20guys%20at%20a%0Afair:%0Ahttp:%2F%2Fwww.angband.com%2Ftowers%2Fimages%2Fplayerart%2Fcavetroll.jpg%0A%0AAt%20work:%0Ahttp:%2F%2Fwww.scoop.co.nz%2Fstories%2Fimages%2F0211%2F8d7d6de79290007a0992.jpeg%0A%0AErm%2C%20wait%2C%20hmm:%0Ahttp:%2F%2Fwww.trollshop.net%2Ftrolls%2Ftrollcave%2Ftrollcave.htm%0A%0A====================================================================%0A%22The%20poor%2C%20confused%20cave%20troll.%20He%20doesn%27t%20know%20what%20he%27s%20doing.%0A%20He%20just%20never%20had%20the%20proper%20guidance.%22%20%20--%20Elijah%20Wood%0A====================================================================%0A%0A%0A%0A
Tar-Elenion%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AMy%20take%20on%20this%20has%20generally%20been%20that%20she%20was%20a%20strong%20advocate%20for%0Aleaving%20Valinor%20and%20helped%20to%20urge%2Fconvince%20many%20others%20to%20do%20so.%20%20She%0Athen%20%27led%20by%20example%27%2C%20leaving%20before%20the%20others%20and%20thus%2C%20by%20chance%2C%0Aavoided%20involvement%20in%20the%20kinslaying.%20%20I%27d%20argue%20that%20this%20fits%20all%0ATolkien%27s%20statements%20%28she%20could%20still%20very%20reasonably%20be%20said%20to%20have%0Aled%20the%20Noldor%20to%20exile%29%20without%20contradiction.%0A%0A%0ANot%20least%20the%20fact%20that%20he%20would%20then%20be%20Galadriel%27s%20cousin.%0A%0A%0ATo%20protect%20his%20wife%2C%20but%20then...%20I%20generally%20toss%20the%20whole%0A%27Teleporno%27%20concept%20on%20the%20incest%20grounds%20and%20the%20clear%20published%0Aindications%20that%20he%20was%20not%20Calaquendi.%0A%0A%0A
The%20American%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AIn%20fact%2C%20it%20was%20just%20the%20opposite%20of%20what%20you%27ve%20described.%20The%20mounds%0A%2Agrew%2A%20rather%20than%20shrank%20over%20the%20course%20of%20time.%20If%20the%20statement%20in%20LotR%0Athat%20they%20were%20built%20up%20by%20the%20labor%20of%20Sauron%27s%20minions%20isn%27t%20enough%2C%20in%20UT%0Athere%20is%20a%20tale%20of%20a%20Gondorian%20army%20battling%20wainriders%20before%20the%20Morranon.%0AIt%20even%20states%20that%20the%20hills%20that%20the%20Gondorians%20made%20their%20last%20stand%20was%0Alikely%20the%20very%20same%20hills%20that%20Aragorn%20et%20al%20made%20%2Atheir%2A%20last%20stand%20in%20the%0AWar%20of%20the%20Ring.%20However%2C%20it%20notes%20that%20the%20hills%20were%20significantly%0A%2Asmaller%2A%20at%20that%20time%20than%20they%20were%20by%20the%20end%20of%20the%20Third%20Age.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
The%20human%20Jensen%20asked:%0A%7CThe%20question%20involved%20the%20old%20possessions%20and%20property%20of%20the%20Elves%0A%7Cwho%20departed%20into%20the%20West.%20...%0A%7C%0A%7CSo%20what%20happened%20to%20all%20that%20stuff%3F%0A%7C%0A%7CAnd%20what%20about%20formerly%20Elvish%20land%3F%0A%0AI%20would%20say%20as%20the%20Elves%20left%2C%20their%20efforts%20at%20staying%20the%0Aravages%20of%20change%20and%20time%20would%20fall%20from%20the%20lands%20too.%20So%0Aabout%20the%20time%20that%20Men%20got%20brave%20enough%20to%20go%20into%2C%20say%0ARivendell%2C%20%20by%20then%20everything%20Elven%20would%20have%20succumbed%0Ato%20dust%20and%20wind%2C%20rain%20and%20bramble.%0A%0AOTOH%20aren%27t%20we%20sort%20of%20told%20that%20some%20of%20the%20Elven%20Lands%20stay%0Aas%20they%20were%20for%20quite%20sometime%20in%20%22%20A%20PART%20OF%20THE%20TALE%20OF%20ARAGORN%0AAND%20ARWEN%20%22%3F%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20--------------------%0A%0A%27...and%20she%20%5B%20Arwen%20%5D%20went%20out%20from%20the%20city%20of%20Minas%20Tirith%0Aand%20passed%20away%20to%20the%20land%20of%20Lorien%2C%20and%20dwelt%20there%20alone%0Aunder%20the%20fading%20trees%20until%20winter%20came.%20Galadriel%20had%20passed%0Aaway%20and%20Celeborn%20also%20was%20gone%2C%20and%20the%20land%20was%20silent.%0A%0A%5B%20So%20the%20elf%20host%20was%20gone%2C%20but%20the%20land%20was%20still%20empty%2C%0A%20%20granted%20not%20all%20that%20much%20time%20had%20passed...%20but%20read%20on%20%5D%0A%0A%27There%20at%20last%20when%20the%20mallorn-leaves%20were%20falling%2C%20but%20spring%0Ahad%20not%20yet%20come%2C%20she%20laid%20herself%20to%20rest%20upon%20Cerin%20Amroth%3B%0Aand%20there%20is%20her%20green%20grave%2C%20until%20the%20world%20is%20changed%2C%20and%0Aall%20the%20days%20of%20her%20life%20are%20utterly%20forgotten%20by%20men%20that%20come%0Aafter%2C%20and%20elanor%20and%20niphredil%20bloom%20no%20more%20east%20of%20the%20Sea.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20--------------------%0A%0AThis%20kind%20of%20circularly%20states%20that%20Arwen%27s%20grave%2C%20and%20the%0Aflowers%20of%20Lothlorien%20%28%20&%20maybe%20even%20mallorns%20near%20her%20final%20repose%29%0Astayed%20the%20same%20until%20the%20flowers%20of%20Lothlorien%20and%20maybe%20even%0Athe%20mallorns%20near%20her%20final%20repose%20weren%27t%20there%20--%20all%20of%20which%0Ais%20based%20on%20if%20Arwen%20was%20forgotten%20or%20not%3F%20Sounds%20like%20it%20stayed%0Athe%20same%20forever%20to%20me.%20.%20.due%20to%20the%20writings%20of%20some%20of%20them%0Ablasted%20thieving%20hairfoot%20hobbits.%0A%0AYet%20still%2C%20I%21%20CAVE%20TROLL%2C%20have%20through%20craft%20and%20brute%20force%0Agotten%20my%20huge%20hands%20on%20these%20rare%20artifacts%20that%20can%20but%20have%0Aonce%20been%20those%20of%20that%20witchling%20Ms.%20Undomiel:%0A%0A%2A%20http:%2F%2Fimages.google.com%2Fimages%3Fhl=en&lr=&ie=ISO-8859-1&q=+arwen+passport%0A%2A%20http:%2F%2Fshop.dashmount.co.uk%2Fphonecovers%2Farwen2.jpg%0A%0A====================================================================%0A%22The%20poor%2C%20confused%20cave%20troll.%20He%20doesn%27t%20know%20what%20he%27s%20doing.%0A%20He%20just%20never%20had%20the%20proper%20guidance.%22%20%20--%20Elijah%20Wood%0A====================================================================%0A%0A%0A
The%20prologue%20to%20The%20Hobbit%20%28or%20is%20it%20to%20LOTR%3F%29%20gives%20all%0Athese%20details%20about%20how%20Bilbo%20sort-of%20%22lied%22%20about%20how%20he%0Agot%20the%20Ring%2C%20changing%20the%20story%20so%20it%20looked%20like%20he%20didn%27t%0Ado%20anything%20wrong%20in%20getting%20%28stealing%29%20the%20Ring%20from%20Gollum.%0AThe%20prologue%20also%20mentions%20how%20the%20earlier%20editions%20of%20the%0Abooks%20had%20to%20be%20corrected%2C%20so%20that%20newer%20editions%20would%20tell%0Athe%20%22true%22%20story.%0A%0AMy%20question:%20are%20there%20really%20any%20editions%20of%20the%20Hobbit%20that%0Atell%20this%20part%20of%20the%20story%20%28Riddles%20in%20the%20Dark%29%20differently%0Afrom%20what%20you%20can%20read%20in%20any%20current%20version%20of%20The%20Hobbit%3F%0AWhich%20ones%3F%20If%20there%20are%2C%20are%20these%20editions%20a%20highly%20priced%0Acollector%27s%20item%3F%20Have%20they%20any%20higher%20%28monetary%29%20value%20than%0Aa%20recent%20run-of-the-mill%20edition%20of%20The%20Hobbit%3F%0A%0ARegards%2C%0A%0A%0A--%0AGonzalo%20Diethelm%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%0A%0A%0A
Then%20at%20last%20Pippin%20took%20Gandalf%27s%20hand.%0A%0A%27Tell%20me%2C%27%20he%20said%2C%20%27is%20there%20any%20hope%3F%20For%20Frodo%2C%20I%20mean%3B%20or%20at%20least%0Amostly%20for%20Frodo.%27%0A%0AGandalf%20put%20his%20hand%20on%20Pippin%27s%20head.%20%27There%20never%20was%20much%20hope%2C%27%20he%0Aanswered.%20%27Just%20a%20fool%27s%20hope%2C%20as%20I%20have%20been%20told.%27%0A%0A%22Furio97%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:41nospam@nospam.net...%0Ajust%20a%0Awas%0AAs%0AThanks%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
This%20is%20a%20pyramid%20scheme.%0A%0A%22j%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:OMaVa.7364$41nospam@nospam.net...%0Alucrative%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
Thomas%20Sperre%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20enriched%20us%20with:%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0AI%20think%20that%20the%20clan%20heads%20among%20the%20Hobbits%20come%20close%20to%20the%20idea%0Aof%20an%20aristocracy%20-%20or%20perhaps%20rather%20the%20gentry.%20Kind%20of%20a%0Aproto-aristocracy%2C%20I%20think.%0A%0AThis%20kind%20of%20clan%20headship%20is%20what%20resulted%20in%20the%20first%20%27generation%27%0Aof%20aristocracy%20-%20local%20chiefs%20and%20petty%20kings%20who%20was%20allowed%20some%0Aextra%20influence%20and%20rights%20for%20swearing%20allegiance%20to%20a%20king%20over%20a%0Alarger%20area.%20This%20is%20what%20happened%20in%20Denmark%20shortly%20before%20year%201000%2C%0Awhen%20the%20areas%20of%20the%20Danes%20were%20slowly%20gathered%20under%20one%20king.%0A%0AThe%20clan%20headship%20among%20the%20Hobbits%20was%20hereditary%20%28with%20some%20complex%0Arules%20in%20case%20of%20a%20childless%20head%20-%20as%20Frodo%20was%29%2C%20and%20if%20some%20of%20the%0Aclan%20heads%20held%20further%20titles%20%28the%20Thain%20and%20the%20Master%29%20that%20only%0Astresses%20the%20importance%20of%20their%20position.%0A%0A--%0ATroels%20Forchhammer%0AValid%20e-mail%20address%20is%20t.forch%28a%29mail.dk%0A%0A%0A%0A
Troels%20Forchhammer%20wrote:%0ABut%20we%20have%20no%20idea%20how%20old%20he%20is.%20I%20favour%20the%20theory%20%28which%20seems%20more%0Aimplicit%20in%20the%20text%29%20that%20he%20was%20knocking%20about%20in%20the%20Second%20Age%2C%20in%0Awhich%20case%2C%20he%20isn%27t%20%2Ajust%2A%20a%20man%2C%20but%20rather%20is%20someone%20outliving%20his%0Alifespan.%20In%20which%20case%20he%20has%20passed%20beyond%20being%20a%20mortal%2C%20which%20for%0Ame%20is%20the%20important%20threshold:%20my%20basic%20premise%20as%20to%20why%20humans%20can%27t%0Ado%20magic%20is%20based%20around%20my%20own%20personal%20theory%20that%20to%20perform%20magic%0Ayou%20need%20to%20be%20an%20immortal%20%28or%20at%20least%2C%20to%20have%20a%20much%20longer%20lifespan%2C%0Aas%20the%20dwarves%20do%29.%20I%20think%20it%27s%20because%20directly%20using%20magic%20is%0Adangerous%20for%20a%20human%2C%20and%20would%20kill%20them%20because%20there%20bodies%20are%20not%0Arobust%20enough%20to%20handle%20the%20stress.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20they%20%2Acan%2A%20use%20an%20intermediate%20device%2C%20which%20access%20the%20magic%2C%0Aand%20allow%20humans%20to%20then%20focus%20it%20safely%20%28such%20as%20a%20palantir%2C%20perhaps%29.%0AUnless%20of%20course%20these%20objects%20are%20simply%20%2Avery%2A%20advanced%20technology%20%28or%0Ait%20could%20be%20a%20mix%20of%20the%20two%29.%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0AOf%20course%20there%20are:%20there%20always%20will%20be%2C%20unless%20we%20find%20a%20lost%20cache%0Aof%20letters%20or%20other%20writings%20Tolkien%20wrote%20-%20one%27s%20entitled%20%22What%20I%0Ameant%20when%20I%20wrote...%22%20%3B%29%0A%0A%3Csnip%3E%0A%0A%0AUmmm...%20why%20are%20those%20%22properties%20that%20were%20definitely%20magical%22%3F%20Isn%27t%0Athat%20exactly%20what%20a%20horn%20is%20supposed%20to%20do%3F%21%20I%20mean%2C%20Eowyn%20was%20hardly%0Agoing%20to%20say%20%22He%20that%20blows%20it%20at%20need%20shall%20be%20ignored%2C%20actually%2C%20as%0Ano-one%20like%20him%20on%20account%20that%20he%20SMELLS%21%20Oh%2C%20and%20next%20time%20I%20give%20you%0A%20%20a%20lift%2C%20watch%20where%20you%20put%20your%20hands%2C%20you%20dirty%20git%21%22.%20It%27s%20just%20a%0Abit%20of%20hyperbole%2C%20as%20I%20read%20it%20-%20a%20nice%20bit%20of%20marketing.%0A%0ADunno.%20I%20was%20surprised%20actually%20that%20the%20horn%20doesn%27t%20seem%20to%20be%20in%20the%0Aindex%20under%20%22Things%22.%0A%0A%3Csnip%20discussion%20of%20quote%20on%20magic%20from%20Letters%3E%0AWell%2C%20that%27s%20one%20thing%20we%27ll%20never%20agree%20on%21%0A%0A:%29%0A%0AJamie%0A%0A--%0A%22The%20more%20I%20see%20of%20the%20world%2C%20the%20more%20am%20I%20dissatisfied%20with%20it%3B%20and%0Aevery%20day%20confirms%20my%20belief%20of%20the%20inconsistency%20of%20all%20human%0Acharacters%2C%20and%20of%20the%20little%20dependence%20that%20can%20be%20placed%20on%20the%0Aappearance%20of%20either%20merit%20or%20sense.%22%0A%0AJane%20Austen%2C%20Pride%20and%20Prejudice%0A%0A%0A%0A
Well%2C%20in%20my%20quick%20off-the%20-cuff%20comment%2C%20I%20don%27t%20think%20I%20stated%20that%20I%0Athought%20%22Peter%20Jackson%20is%20a%20jerk%21%22%20-%20although%20I%20understand%20that%20this%20has%0Abeen%20the%20reaction%20of%20some.%20But%20I%20do%20think%20that%20he%20didn%27t%20truly%20understand%0Athe%20books.%20Watching%20the%20interviews%20with%20him%2C%20both%20sets%2C%20for%20each%20movie%2C%20he%0Aand%20the%20main%20actors%20in%20the%20film%20seem%20completely%20unaware%20of%20Tolkein%27s%20very%0ACatholic%20worldview%2C%20and%20absolutely%20unaware%20of%20Tolkein%27s%20deliberate%20inclusion%0Aof%20Catholic%20themes%20and%20symbolism.%20They%20seem%20to%20be%20treating%20the%20ideas%20in%20the%0Abook%20as%20half%20action-adventure%20%2F%20half%20new-age-style%20mythology.%20John%20Rhys%0ADavies%20interview%20was%20most%20indicative%20of%20this.%20So%2C%20yes%2C%20I%20do%20believe%20that%0AJackson%20did%20not%20understand%20Tolkein%2C%20and%20missed%20many%20of%20the%20core%20messages%20of%0Athe%20books.%20He%20does%20well%20on%20the%20surface%2C%20but%20hasn%27t%20even%20begun%20to%20plumb%20the%0Adepths.%20He%20loses%20a%20lot%2C%20and%20thus%2C%20so%20do%20we%20all.%20Still%2C%20it%20is%20a%20very%20good%0Awork%20of%20film.%0A%0AI%20do%20take%20exception%2C%20a%20bit%2C%20to%20your%20description%20of%20Faramir%20and%20his%20interlude%0Awith%20Frodo%2C%20Sam%2C%20and%20Golum%20as%20a%20%22tea%20break%22%20-%20as%20written%20it%20worked%20well%20-%0Aeven%20for%20a%20clueless%20audiance%20who%20is%20geared%20more%20for%20visual%20special%20effects%2C%0Athan%20for%20finding%20deep%20meaning%20in%20a%20story...%20There%27s%20a%20battle%2C%20a%20capture%20with%0Athe%20hobbits%20scared%20out%20of%20their%20minds%2C%20Golum%20is%20nearly%20killed%2C%20Faramir%20finds%0Aout%20about%20the%20Ring%2C%20and%20teeters%20on%20the%20cusp%20-%20didn%27t%20need%20an%20extra%20Nazgul%0Abattle.%20But%20yes%2C%20since%20it%20just%20ended%20right%20there%2C%20w%2Fo%20any%20of%20the%20further%0A%22excitements%2C%20I%20can%20see%20where%20PJ%20needed%20to%20entertain%20his%20audience.%20But%20he%0Adidn%27t%20need%20to%20make%20Faramir%20or%20Treebeard%20into%20idiots%2C%20just%20to%20beef%20up%20his%0Amain%20characters%21%20My%20son%2C%20age%2012%20at%20the%20time%2C%20was%20highly%20offended%20by%20this%20-%0Aand%20he%27s%20just%20a%20kid%21%20LOL%20It%20could%20have%20worked%2C%20Jackson%20just%20took%20the%20easy%0Away%20out%2C%20apparently.%20Well%2C%20at%20least%20they%27re%20putting%20the%20huorns%20back%20at%20Helms%0ADeep%20-%20my%20son%20was%20mad%20at%20that%20omission%20too.%20%28I%20gotta%20say%2C%20watching%20the%20movie%0Awith%20this%20kid%20was%20amazing%2C%20I%20couldn%27t%20believe%20the%20details%20he%20remembered%20from%0Athe%20books%21%29%0A%0AAnyway....%0A%0AHave%20a%20good%20one%2C%0ALis%0A%0A%0A%22jere7my%20tho%3Frpe%22%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%0Anews:41nospam@nospam.net...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
When%20Gollum%20leads%20Frodo%20and%20Sam%20down%20from%20the%20Emyn%20Muil%20to%20the%20Dead%0AMarshes%2C%20he%20tells%20them%0A%0A%20%20%20%22Here%21%20%20We%20can%20get%20down%20here.%20%20Smeagol%20went%20this%20way%20once.%20%20I%20went%0A%20%20%20this%20way%2C%20hiding%20from%20Orcs.%22%0A%0ANow%2C%20we%20know%20of%20at%20least%20one%20time%20when%20Gollum%20was%20in%20the%20Dead%20Marshes:%0AAragorn%20caught%20him%20there%20after%20his%20%22escape%22%20from%20Mordor.%20%20I%20had%20always%0Aunthinkingly%20assumed%20that%20this%20was%20the%20time%20when%20he%20%22went%20this%20way%0Aonce%22%2C%20but%20I%20recently%20realized%20that%20was%20quite%20unlikely.%20%20After%20leaving%0AMordor%2C%20it%20seems%20very%20unlikely%20that%20Gollum%20would%20end%20up%20entering%20the%0ADead%20Marshes%20from%20the%20northwest%20%28Frodo%20and%20Sam%20were%20pretty%20much%20on%20the%0Aopposite%20side%20of%20the%20Marshes%20from%20Mordor%29.%0A%0AThat%20can%20only%20mean%20that%20he%20came%20that%20way%20when%20he%20first%20traveled%20south%0Atoward%20Mordor%2C%20which%20may%20give%20some%20insight%20into%20a%20few%20minor%20questions%0Aabout%20his%20travels.%20%20First%20of%20all%2C%20if%20he%20ended%20up%20in%20the%20Emyn%20Muil%20it%0Aseems%20very%20likely%20that%20he%20got%20there%20by%20following%20the%20Anduin%20%28Gandalf%0Asays%20in%20%22The%20Shadow%20of%20the%20Past%22%20that%20Gollum%20turned%20south%20there%0Ainstead%20of%20crossing%20it%20and%20following%20Bilbo%20back%20west%29.%20%20In%20fact%2C%20I%27m%0Atempted%20to%20conclude%20that%20he%20followed%20the%20Anduin%20all%20the%20way%20south%20to%0ARauros.%0A%0AI%27ve%20always%20wondered%20what%2C%20exactly%2C%20inspired%20Gollum%20to%20turn%20aside%20when%0Ahe%20did.%20%20Gandalf%20said%20that%0A%0A%20%20%20%22Mordor%20draws%20all%20wicked%20things%2C%20and%20the%20Dark%20Power%20was%20bending%20all%0A%20%20%20its%20will%20to%20gather%20them%20there.%20%20The%20Ring%20of%20the%20Enemy%20would%20leave%0A%20%20%20its%20mark%2C%20too%2C%20leave%20him%20open%20to%20the%20summons.%20%20And%20all%20folk%20were%0A%20%20%20whispering%20then%20of%20the%20new%20Shadow%20in%20the%20South%2C%20and%20its%20hatred%20of%0A%20%20%20the%20West.%20%20There%20were%20his%20fine%20new%20friends%2C%20who%20would%20help%20him%20in%0A%20%20%20his%20revenge.%22%0A%0AThis%20actually%20seems%20to%20make%20three%20claims:%0A%0A1.%20That%20%22wicked%22%20things%20could%20be%20%22drawn%22%20to%20Mordor%20by%20Sauron%27s%20will.%0A%20%20%20But%20what%20does%20%22wicked%22%20mean%3F%20%20And%20how%20could%20a%20generic%20%22will%22%20draw%0A%20%20%20living%20things%20somewhere%3F%20%20%28This%20could%20be%20related%20to%20the%20way%20in%0A%20%20%20which%20Saruman%27s%20will%20tired%20his%20enemies%20in%20Rohan%2C%20and%20possible%20also%0A%20%20%20to%20the%20%22countersummons%22%20of%20Morgoth%20as%20he%20tried%20to%20seduce%20the%0A%20%20%20spirits%20of%20dead%20Elves%20to%20come%20to%20him%20instead%20of%20to%20Mandos.%29%0A%0A2.%20That%20the%20One%20Ring%20left%20Gollum%20%22open%20to%20the%20summons%22.%20%20The%20word%0A%20%20%20%22too%22%20seems%20to%20imply%20that%20this%20was%20at%20least%20to%20some%20extent%0A%20%20%20different%20from%20the%20attraction%20of%20%22wicked%20things%22%20to%20Mordor%3B%20I%20can%0A%20%20%20only%20assume%20that%20this%20means%20that%20this%20means%20Gollum%20was%20being%20drawn%0A%20%20%20there%20for%20both%20reasons%20independently.%20%20That%20leads%20me%20to%20suspect%0A%20%20%20that%20%22wicked%22%20actually%20is%20being%20used%20literally%20here%2C%20rather%20than%0A%20%20%20meaning%20something%20like%20%22of%20evil%20unnatural%20origin%22%20%28which%20would%0A%20%20%20apply%20to%20creatures%20like%20Orcs%20and%20Trolls%20but%20not%20to%20nasty%20Men%2C%20for%0A%20%20%20example%29.%20%20It%27s%20intriguing%20to%20think%20that%20Sauron%20could%20somehow%20draw%0A%20%20%20people%20and%20things%20to%20him%20based%20on%20their%20internal%20temperment%20alone.%0A%0A3.%20That%20Gollum%20somehow%20believed%20that%20the%20Shadow%20in%20the%20South%20that%20he%0A%20%20%20heard%20rumors%20of%20would%20be%20willing%20and%20able%20to%20help%20him%20regain%20the%0A%20%20%20Ring.%20%20I%20have%20no%20idea%20what%20would%20have%20led%20him%20to%20that%20conclusion%20at%0A%20%20%20all%2C%20to%20be%20honest%2C%20so%20I%27d%20love%20to%20hear%20other%20peoples%27%20thoughts.%0A%0AAt%20any%20rate%2C%20the%20fact%20that%20Gollum%20followed%20the%20Anduin%20to%20the%20south%0Aactually%20makes%20me%20think%20of%20an%20entirely%20different%20motive%20that%20might%0Ahave%20led%20him%20to%20turn%20aside%20when%20he%20did.%20%20It%20seems%20at%20least%20possible%0Athat%20he%20wanted%20to%20see%20if%20his%20people%20were%20still%20living%20where%20he%20had%0Agrown%20up%2C%20on%20the%20banks%20of%20the%20Anduin%20not%20too%20far%20from%20the%20Gladden%0AFields.%20%20That%20might%20not%20have%20been%20enough%20to%20make%20him%20turn%20aside%20on%20its%0Aown%2C%20but%20it%20might%20have%20been%20enough%20if%20it%20were%20coupled%20with%20a%20general%2C%0Aunconscious%20feeling%20that%20south-southeast%20%28i.e.%20toward%20Mordor%29%20was%20an%0A%22easier%22%20or%20%22more%20pleasant%22%20direction%20to%20travel%20than%20west.%20%20Whether%0Agoing%20there%20was%20really%20his%20goal%20or%20not%2C%20I%20wonder%20what%20his%20reaction%20was%0Awhen%20he%20reached%20the%20site%20of%20his%20old%20home%20and%20found%20it%20deserted.%0A%0AMoving%20on%20a%20little%2C%20I%27m%20also%20very%20curious%20to%20know%20why%20Gollum%20ended%20up%0Aneeding%20to%20%22hide%20from%20Orcs%22%20in%20the%20Emyn%20Muil%20at%20all.%20%20If%20he%20followed%0Atheh%20Anduin%20all%20the%20way%20to%20Rauros%2C%20why%20would%20he%20turn%20east%20from%20there%0Ainto%20the%20rocky%2C%20pathless%20hills%20rather%20than%20just%20climbing%20down%20past%20the%0Awaterfall%20and%20continuing%20down%20the%20river%20until%20he%20was%20closer%20to%20Mordor%3F%0A%28I%20_assume_%20he%20could%20have%20easily%20found%20the%20North%20Stair%20if%20he%27d%20been%0Alooking%20for%20a%20way%20down.%29%20%20And%20if%20he%20were%20being%20chased%20by%20Orcs%20%28or%20just%0Atrying%20to%20hide%20from%20them%29%2C%20why%20would%20he%20plunge%20into%20the%20hills%20instead%0Aof%20just%20crossing%20the%20River%2C%20which%20it%20seems%20he%20was%20easily%20capable%20of%0Adoing%20%28and%20which%20they%20certainly%20would%20not%20do%29%3F%20%20I%20think%20of%20the%0A%22attraction%22%20of%20Mordor%20as%20a%20subtle%2C%20subconscious%20thing%2C%20not%20as%0Asomething%20so%20strong%20that%20it%20would%20overcome%20Gollum%27s%20reason%21%0A%0AAnyway%2C%20I%27m%20interested%20to%20know%20what%20other%20people%20think%20about%20my%0Aconclusions%20here%2C%20or%20about%20this%20topic%20in%20general.%0A%0A%09%09%09%09%09%09Steuard%20Jensen%0A%0A%0A
Wilbur07:%09%20don%21%0A%20donsaner:%09%20rock%21%21%21%21%21%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20hey%2C%20what%27s%20up%20big%20penis%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20just%20waiting%20for%20quiting%20time%20fuzzy%20balls%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20do%20you%20have%20a%20twenny%20spot%20you%20could%20len%27%20me%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20I%20have%20a%201%20million%20turkish%20lira%20note%20here%20I%20could%20lend%20you%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20cool%21%20%20send%20to%0A683%20Abbot%20Ave%0ADaly%20City%2C%20CA%2094014%0A%0Ain%20California%0A%20donsaner:%09%20George%20Bush%20is%20really%20stupid%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20http:%2F%2Fpreview.explodingjizz.com%2Fhp%2Fe%2F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20thats%20a%20lovely%20site%21%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20i%27m%20reading%20my%20email%20that%27s%20what%20i%20got%20today%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20www.allure.com%0A%20donsaner:%09%20i%20want%20to%20retire%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20what%27s%20yer%20email%20again%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20why%20do%20you%20want%20to%20retire%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%41nospam@nospam.net%0A%20donsaner:%09%20i%20am%20tired%20of%20working%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20me%20too%0A%20donsaner:%09%20do%20they%20count%20you%20in%20the%20unemployment%20rate%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20i%20dunno.%20%20what%20category%20am%20i%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20how%20much%20is%20a%20mil%20in%20lira%2C%20turkish%2C%20in%20federal%20reserve%20notes%2C%0Aunited%20statesish%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20not%20sure%20-%20i%20am%20wondering%20how%20they%20determine%20how%20many%20people%0Aare%20unemployed.%20No%20one%20ever%20calls%20me%20to%20ask.%0A%20donsaner:%09%201%20million%20turkish%20lira%20=%2075%20cents%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20well%2C%20they%20take%20the%20total%20number%20of%20people%20who%20are%20eligible%0Afor%20employment%2C%20then%20call%20the%20IRS%20on%20figures%20as%20to%20how%20many%20are%20sending%20a%20cut%0Afrom%20their%20paychecks%2C%20and%20take%20that%20as%20the%20employment%20ratio.%20%201%20minus%20that%20is%0Athe%20employment%20rate%2C%20get%20it%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20okay%2C%20send%20me%2026.6%20million%20lira%20in%20united%20states%20federal%0Areserve%20notes%2C%20ie%20that%20is%20a%20twenny%20spot.%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20Bip%20Genius%21%0A%20donsaner:%09%20did%20we%20go%20to%20school%20with%20someone%20named%20Rohit%20Gupta%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20no%2C%20that%20was%20my%20roommate%20one%20summer%3B%20why%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20we%20just%20hired%20someone%20by%20that%20name%20-%20i%20wonder%20if%20it%20is%20the%0Asame%20guy%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20the%20name%20sounded%20familiar%20somehow%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20you%27re%20kidding%21%20%20he%20used%20to%20work%20at%20www.riskinc.com%20when%20i%20was%0Aan%20engineering%20student%21%0A%20donsaner:%09%20probably%20not%20the%20same%20guy%20-%20he%20is%20a%20doctor%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20oh%2C%20you%27re%20right.%20%20it%27s%20like%20john%20smith%20probably%2C%20over%20there%0A%20donsaner:%09%20there%20is%20a%20big%20leadership%20change%20here%20-%20hope%20I%20don%27t%20lose%20my%0Ajob%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20well%2C%20if%20they%27re%20hiring%2C%20put%20my%20resume%20in%21%0A%20donsaner:%09%20the%20tech%20field%20went%20from%20red%20hot%20to%20ice%20cold.%20now%20i%20hear%20they%0Aare%20shipping%20the%20tech%20jobs%20over%20seas%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20cool%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20have%20you%20ever%20eaten%20pussy%20so%20good%20you%27d%20die%20for%20it%3F%0A%20donsaner:%09%20nope%20cant%20say%20i%20have.%20usually%20smells%20sort%20of%20funky.%20sort%20of%0Amessy%20too.%20and%20then%20there%20are%20the%20pubic%20hairs...%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20not%20the%20women%20I%20know%21%20%20If%20it%27s%20kept%20clean%20it%27s%20wonderful%2C%20to%0Aeat%21%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20Seen%20any%20documentaries%20lately%3F%0A%20Wilbur07:%09%20Subject:%20Any%20Elven%20Miscarriages%20or%20Stillborns%0AFrom:%20%22Robert%20J.%20Kolker%22%41nospam@nospam.net%0ADate:%207%2F28%2F03%2011:17%20AM%20Pacific%20Daylight%20Time%0AMessage-id:%20%3CoNdVa.756$41nospam@nospam.net%3E%0A%0ADid%20miscarriage%20or%20stillbirth%20occur%20in%20elvenkind%3F%0A%0ABob%20Kolker%0A%20donsane