in%20article%20%3Cdfawa.64%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%0Asteuard%20jensen%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%3A%0Ain%20the%20book%2C%20it%20wasn%27t%20even%20really%20a%20romance%20on%20%2Aeither%2A%20side.%20it%20was%0Amore%20like%20aragorn%20passed%20through%20rohan%20being%20all%20noble%20and%20courtly%20and%0Aheroic%2C%20and%20eowyn%20realized%20how%20much%20her%20life%20there%20sucked%2C%20and%20how%0Alittle%20future%20she%20had%2C%20and%20that%20there%20was%20a%20big%2C%20interesting%20world%20out%0Athere%20that%20she%20wanted%20to%20see%20and%20be%20a%20part%20of.%20i%20don%27t%20believe%20that%0Aromantic%20attachment%20to%20aragorn%20was%20her%20primary%20reason--%20or%20even%20a%0Areason--%20for%20dressing%20as%20a%20boy%20and%20playing%20soldier.%0A--%0Apciszek%20at%20theworld%20dot%20com%20%7C%20%22if%20more%20of%20us%20valued%20food%20and%20cheer%20and%0A%7C%20song%20above%20hoarded%20gold%2C%20it%20would%20be%20a%0A%7C%20merrier%20world.%22%20-thorin%20oakenshield%0A
in%20article%20%3Cey2qa.2575%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%0Arec.arts.books.tolkien%2C%20a%20tsar%20is%20born%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%3A%0Athe%20echoes%20come%20from%20the%20original%20sound%20energy.%20if%20the%20direct%20sound%0Acan%27t%20be%20heard%20at%20distance%20x%2C%20certainly%20the%20echoes%20can%27t%20either.%0Amore%20evidence%20that%20it%27s%20magic.%20they%20are%20removed%20from%20the%20affairs%20of%0Athe%20%22western%20branch%20of%20the%20fellowship%22%2C%20so%20they%20do%20not%20get%20any%20form%0Aof%20news%20about%20it.%0A--%0Astan%20brown%2C%20oak%20road%20systems%2C%20cortland%20county%2C%20new%20york%2C%20usa%0Ahttp%3A%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%0Atolkien%20faqs%3A%20http%3A%2F%2Ftolkien.slimy.com%20%28steuard%20jensen%27s%20site%29%0Atolkien%20letters%20faq%3A%0Ahttp%3A%2F%2Fusers.telerama.com%2F~taliesen%2Ftolkien%2Flettersfaq.html%0Afaq%20of%20the%20rings%3A%20http%3A%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Fgenl%2Fringfaq.htm%0Aencyclopedia%20of%20arda%3A%20http%3A%2F%2Fwww.glyphweb.com%2Farda%2Fdefault.htm%0Amore%20faqs%3A%20http%3A%2F%2Foakroadsystems.com%2Ftech%2Ffaqget.htm%0A
in%20article%20%3Cijvna.2913%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%3D20%0Arec.arts.books.tolkien%2C%20a%20tsar%20is%20born%3D20%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%3A%0All%0Ao%0Afirst%2C%20sentimental%20reasons%3A%20elwing%27s%20grandfather%20and%20grandmother%20had%3D20%0Awon%20it%20from%20morgoth%20after%20terrible%20privations.%20had%20it%20been%20a%20mere%20%3D20%0Apiece%20of%20gravel%20i%20think%20it%20would%20have%20been%20precious%20to%20them%20for%20that%3D20%0Areason.%0Asecond%2C%20the%20silmaril%20had%20some%20sort%20of%20power%20to%20heal%20the%20hurts%20of%3D20%0Amiddle-earth.%20when%20l%3Dfathien%20wore%20it%2C%20%22for%20a%20little%20while%20the%20land%20of%3D20%0Athe%20dead%20that%20live%20became%20like%20a%20vision%20of%20the%20land%20of%20the%20valar%2C%3D20%0Aand%20no%20place%20has%20been%20since%20so%20fair%2C%20so%20fruitful%2C%20or%20so%20filled%20with%3D20%0Alight.%22%0Athird%2C%20the%20thing%20was%20pretty%20in%20itself%2C%20and%20it%20beautified%20its%20wearer%3A%3D20%0A%22then%20dior%20arose%2C%20and%20about%20his%20neck%20he%20clasped%20the%20nauglam%3Dedr%3B%20and%3D20%0Anow%20he%20appeared%20as%20the%20fairest%20of%20all%20the%20children%20of%20the%20world%2C%20of%3D20%0Athreefold%20race%3A%20of%20the%20edain%2C%20and%20of%20the%20eldar%2C%20and%20of%20the%20maiar%20of%3D20%0Athe%20blessed%20realm.%22%0Afourth%2C%20dior%20would%20not%20have%20turned%20it%20over%20because%20the%20demand%20came%3D20%0Afrom%20celegorm%20and%20curufin%2C%20who%20had%20essentially%20tried%20to%20rape%20his%3D20%0Amother.%20and%20elwing%20would%20not%20turn%20it%20over%20to%20the%20remaining%20brothers%2C%3D20%0Awho%20had%20murdered%20her%20father.%0Atolkien%20sums%20it%20all%20up%20in%20the%20%22war%20of%20wrath%22%20chapter%3A%20%22then%20elwing%3D20%0Aand%20the%20people%20of%20sirion%20would%20not%20yield%20the%20jewel%20which%20beren%20had%3D20%0Awon%20and%20l%3Dfathien%20had%20worn%2C%20and%20for%20which%20dior%20the%20fair%20was%20slain%3B%20and%3D20%0Aleast%20of%20all%20while%20e%3De4rendil%20their%20lord%20was%20on%20the%20sea%2C%20for%20it%20seemed%3D20%0Ato%20them%20that%20in%20the%20silmaril%20lay%20the%20hea
in%20article%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%2C%0Astan%20brown%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%3A%0Awas%20unfinished%20tales%20the%20next%20book%20from%20christopher%20tolkien%20after%0Athe%20silmarillion%3F%20if%20so%20i%20wonder%20if%20reading%20all%20the%20books%20in%0Apublished%20order%20might%20not%20be%20best%20recommendation%20%28the%20most%20accessable%0Amaterial%20being%20published%20first%29.%0Apersonally%20i%27ve%20browsed%20unfinished%20tales%20in%20bookstores%20without%0Areally%20being%20drawn%20in%2C%20although%20i%20may%20give%20it%20a%20try%20at%20some%20point%2C%0Aand%20the%20history%20volumes%20look%20far%20too%20dry%20for%20me.%20that%27s%20why%20i%20like%0Alurking%20here%20-%20lots%20of%20interesting%20tidbits%20of%20information%20without%0Ahaving%20to%20slog%20through%20all%20the%20books%21%0A--%0Ajohn%20brock%41nospam@nospam.net%0A
in%20the%20year%20of%20the%20goat%2C%20the%20great%20and%20powerful%20louis%20epstein%0Adeclared...%0Ai%27m%20sure%20new%20line%20is%20quite%20distraught%20at%20fotr%20going%20down%20a%20notch%0Aon%20the%20all-time%20list.%20i%20guess%20they%27ll%20just%20have%20to%20console%0Athemselves%20with%20the%20fact%20that%20each%20film%20has%20turned%20in%20a%20better%0Athan%20300%25%2Bprofit.%0A--%0Asean%20o%27hara%0A%22harry%20goes%20through%20absolute%20hell%20every%20time%20he%20returns%20to%20school.%0Aso%20i%20think%20that%20a%20bit%20of%20snogging%20would%20alleviate%20matters.%22%0A-j.k.%20rowling%0A
istr%20reading%20that%20the%20guns%20on%20the%20first%20day%20of%20the%20battle%20of%20the%20somme%20%28one%0Aof%20the%20wwi%20battles%2C%20anyway%29%20could%20be%20heard%20clearly%20on%20hampstead%20heath%2C%0Agetting%20on%20for%20200%20miles%20away.%20%28i%20don%27t%20know%20if%20this%20is%20true%20or%20just%20an%0Aurban%20myth%2C%20though%29.%0Aandrew%0A--%0Aandrew%20wells%0Areplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A
jamie%20armstrong%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news%3A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0Asure%2C%20but%20it%20doesn%27t%20allow%20any%20possibility%20of%20%27human%20magic%27%20to%20be%0Adismissed%20out%20of%20hand.%20the%20horn%20was%20said%20to%20have%20magical%20properties.%0Athe%20horn%20was%20shown%20to%20have%20properties%20which%20cannot%20be%20explained%20by%0Anormal%20physics.%0Ai%20take%20that%20as%20%27independant%20evidence%27...%20the%20letter%20draft%20shows%20both%0Asides%20of%20a%20disputed%20idea%2C%20but%20i%27d%20argue%20that%20there%20are%20several%0Aexternal%20pieces%20of%20evidence%20that%20argue%20only%20for%20one%20side%20%28that%20men%0Acould%20work%20%27magic%27%29%20and%20little%20outside%20that%20letter%20to%20support%20the%0Aother%20view.%20still%2C%20nothing%20in%20the%20text%20absolutely%20proves%20the%20point...%0Athere%20is%20always%20a%20way%20to%20come%20up%20with%20an%20alternate%20explanation.%0Ahowever%2C%20the%20letter%20itself%20shows%20that%20%3Etolkien%3C%20believed%20they%20had%20used%0Aspells%20and%20this%20conflicted%20with%20his%20later%20idea%20that%20they%20shouldn%27t%20be%0Aable%20to.%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28John%20Brock%29%20writes:%0A%0AGorbag:%20%20%27E%27s%20dead%2C%20that%27s%20what%27s%20wrong%20with%20%27im%21%0AShagrat:%20No%2C%20no%2C%20%27e%27s%20uh%2C...he%27s%20resting.%0AGorbag:%20%20Look%2C%20matey%2C%20I%20know%20a%20dead%20%27obbit%20when%20I%20see%20one%2C%20and%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20I%27m%20looking%20at%20one%20right%20now.%0A%0A--%0Amailto:41nospam@nospam.net%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20phone:+49-7800-555-1212%20%28TELNET%20778-7698%29%0A%20%20http:%2F%2Fwww.bawue.de%2F~jjk%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20fax:+49-7800-555-1212%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20As%20the%20air%20to%20a%20bird%2C%20or%20the%20sea%20to%20a%20fish%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20so%20is%20contempt%20to%20the%20contemptible.%20%5BBlake%5D%0A%0A%0A
jeff%20blanks%20wrote%3A%0Aat%20the%20risk%20of%20sounding%20dense%2C%20is%20there%20an%20lotr%20link%3F%0Aandrew%0A--%0Aandrew%20wells%0Areplace%20nospam%20with%20my%20first%20name%20to%20reach%20me%0A
jere7my%20tho%3Frpe%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AYou%20mean%20Arwen%2C%20I%20hope.%0A%0AUnless%20Eowyn%20is%20scheduled%20to%20do%20some%20%2Areally%2A%20weird%20stuff%20in%20the%20next%20movie%21%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
k%2A%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ASounds%20good%20to%20me%20except%20that%20I%20would%20read%20the%20Silmarillion%20before%20you%20read%0AUnfinished%20Tales.%20The%20Sil%20was%20compiled%20by%20Tolkien%27s%20son%20Christopher%20out%20of%0Ahis%20notes%20and%20into%20a%20relatively%20coherent%20storyline%20%28even%20though%20Tolkien%27s%0Anotes%20themselves%20contradicted%20each%20other%20in%20many%20MANY%20places%29.%20As%20such%2C%20the%0ASil%20is%20a%20pretty%20good%20read%20just%20by%20itself.%20Reading%20IT%20first%20would%20A%29%20spoil%20a%0Alot%20of%20things%20in%20the%20Sil%20and%20B%29%20be%20very%20confusing%20at%20times%20because%20it%0Aassumes%20you%20already%20know%20what%20happened%20in%20the%20Sil.%0A%0A%0AIn%20case%20you%20don%27t%20already%20knot%2C%20this%20is%20a%20book%20of%20poetry%2C%20most%20of%20it%20rather%0Awhimsical%20like%20the%20Hobbits%27%20poetry%20in%20LotR%20but%20some%20of%20it%20is%20different.%0A%0A%0AAs%20implied%20by%20the%20title%2C%20this%20is%20a%20compilation%20of%20some%20of%20Tolkien%27s%20letters.%0AI%20haven%27t%20read%20it%20myself%20but%20people%20here%20occasionally%20quote%20usefull%20tidbits%0Aof%20information%20from%20it...%0A%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0ANot%20really%20%22set%20in%20Middle-earth%22%2C%20but%20is%20an%20essay%20%22on%20fairy%20stories%22%0A%28imagine%20that%21%29.%0A%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0AThe%20%22History%20of%20Middle%20Earth%22%20%28which%20consists%20of%2012%20volumes%2C%20all%20of%20which%20I%0Asnipped%29%20is%20Christopher%20Tolkien%27s%20further%20efforts%20to%20share%20his%20father%27s%0Aunpublished%20work%20with%20the%20fans.%20It%20contains%20many%20many%20different%20variations%0Aof%20various%20texts%2C%20old%20rough%20drafts%20of%20LotR%2C%20and%20all%20sorts%20of%20odds%20and%20ends.%0AHeavily%20commented%20on%20by%20Christopher%2C%20but%20the%20difference%20between%20the%20writings%0Aof%20the%20two%20Tolkien%27s%20is%20made%20very%20clearly%20throughout.%0A%0A%0AHmm%2C%20I%20haven%27t%20heard%20of%20this%20myself.%20I%20read%20the%20description%20on%20the%20website.%0ADoes%20anyone%20have%20any%20comments%20on%20it%3F%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
