41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Paul%20Ciszek%29%20wrote:%0A%0A%3Csnippo%3E%0A%0A%0ARevving%20up%20the%20Bible%20Library%20CD-ROM%2C%20the%20Gray%20Home%20Bible%20Commentary%0Areports%20that%0A%0A%22Some%20think%20the%20Sethites%20are%20meant%20by%20%27the%20sons%20of%20God%2C%27%20but%20others%0Aregard%20it%20as%20a%20reference%20to%20fallen%20angels%20...%22%0A%0AIt%20also%20cites%20works%20purporting%20to%20give%20%2Fscientific%2F%20evidence%20for%20the%0Aview%20that%20they%20were%20%22fallen%20angels%22%2C%20which%20seems%20unlikely.%20Since%20the%0ANephilim%20were%20%22giants%22%2C%20perhaps%20archaeological%20evidence%20of%20really%20tall%0Apeople%20is%20meant.%20Of%20course%2C%20in%20ancient%20Palestine%2C%20six%20feet%20might%20be%0Aconsidered%20%22really%20tall%22%2C%20for%20all%20I%20know.%0A%0AThe%20%2FInterpreter%27s%20Bible%2F%20commentary%20appears%20to%20be%20above%20such%20issues%2C%0Aapparently%20being%20written%20on%20the%20theory%20that%20a%20commentary%20need%20not%0Aconcern%20itself%20with%20the%20meaning%20of%20the%20passage%20concerned%2C%20but%20the%0Aexposition%20asks%0A%0A%22Were%20the%20sons%20of%20God%20rebellious%20and%20fallen%20agels%2C%20as%20Milton%20conceived%0Athem%20in%20%2FParadise%20Lost%2F%3F%22%0A%0Aan%20indication%20of%20the%20age%20of%20this%20belief.%0A%0AThe%20%2FBritannica%202002%2F%20reminds%20us%20that%20this%20is%20an%20area%20where%20Judaism%0Aand%20Christianity%20were%20heavily%20influenced%20by%20Zoroastrianism.%20There%20are%2C%0Aof%20course%2C%20no%20Zoroastrian%20holy%20books%20%28as%20opposed%20to%20books%20influenced%0Aby%20Zoroastrianism%29%20in%20the%20Bible%2C%20thus%20explaining%20the%20difficulty%20in%0Afinding%20a%20Biblical%20basis%20for%20the%20Zoroastrian%20viewpoint.%0A%0AThe%20issue%20of%20%22angels%22%20was%20%28when%20I%20subscribed%2C%20some%20years%20ago%29%0Adiscussed%20a%20lot%20on%20other%20usenet%20groups%20%28alt.bible%20being%20the%20most%0Aobvious%29.%20An%20enormous%20amount%20of%20Biblical%20material%20was%20stretched%2C%0Atwisted%20and%20deformed%20to%20meet%20whatever%20version%20of%20angelology%20%2F%0Ademonology%20is%20being%20defended.%20The%20%22sons%20of%20God%20are%20angels%22%20theory%20is%0Aone%20example.%20The%20%22Lucifer%22%20passage%20in%20one%20of%20the%20prophets%20is%20another%0Aoften%20applied%20to%20Satan%20yet%20also%20said%20to%20be%2C%20in%20context%2C%20referring%20to%20a%0Ahuman%20monarch.%20Another%20example%20is%20the%20Cherub%20set%20to%20guard%20the%20Garden%0Aof%20Eden:%20some%20count%20it%20as%20an%20angel%20%28a%20specific%20%22order%22%20of%20angel%29%20--%0Aand%20yet%20%22cherub%22%20and%20%22gryphon%22%20are%20one%20and%20the%20same%20thing%2C%20what%20Graves%0Acalled%20a%20%22calendar%20beast%22%2C%20symbolizing%20the%20seasons%20of%20the%20sacred%20year.%0AThe%20passage%20in%20Paul%20which%20scholars%20think%20actually%20%2Fis%2F%20a%20list%20of%0Aangelic%20orders%20%28thrones%2C%20dominions%2C%20etc%29%20does%20not%20usually%20appear%20in%0Athese%20discussions%20because%20these%20amateur%20angelologists%20%28as%20it%20were%29%0Atend%20to%20interpret%20it%20as%20referring%20to%20ordinary%20human%20power%20structures.%0A%0AHowever%2C%20I%20have%20to%20agree%20that%20reducing%20angels%2C%20who%20if%20nothing%20else%20are%0AGod%27s%20messengers%2C%20to%20the%20status%20of%20robot%20is%20...%20bizarre.%20And%20unlikely%0Ato%20be%20correct.%20Even%20the%20film%20%2FDogma%2F%20%28which%20may%20be%20considered%20the%20very%0Adefinition%20of%20blasphemy%29%20only%20gives%20one%20choice%20that%20angels%20are%20unable%0Ato%20make%20--%20the%20choice%20of%20ignoring%20God.%0A--%0AYou%20are%20not%20being%20ignored%21%20With%20rare%20exceptions:%0AI%20download%20on%20Saturdays.%20I%20upload%20on%20Sundays.%20Patience%20is%20a%20virtue%0A%0A%0A
quoth%41nospam@nospam.net%20%28charlie%29%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%3A%0A%5Bsnip%5D%0Aas%20you%27ve%20already%20learned%2C%20there%20are%20a%20wide%20range%20of%20views%20on%20what%0A%22canonical%22%20should%20mean%20for%20tolkien%27s%20writings.%20%28i%27ve%20written%20a%20whole%0Aessay%20expressing%20my%20view%20on%20the%20matter.%29%20some%20people%20don%27t%20like%20the%0Aidea%20of%20declaring%20some%20texts%20to%20be%20%22better%22%20than%20others%20at%20all%2C%0Apreferring%20just%20to%20explore%20the%20shape%20of%20tolkien%27s%20ideas%20as%20they%20formed%0Aand%20reformed%20over%20time.%0Aon%20the%20other%20hand%2C%20i%20would%20say%20that%20most%20people%20who%20discuss%0Amiddle-earth%20here%20have%20at%20least%20some%20notion%20of%20which%20texts%20are%0A%22canonical%22%20in%20the%20context%20of%20those%20discussions%2C%20even%20if%20it%27s%20not%0Aterribly%20firm%20or%20well-defined.%20%28any%20discussion%20of%20middle-earth%20itself%0Aas%20a%20%22secondary%20world%22%20-%20as%20opposed%20to%20tolkien%27s%20process%20of%20writing%0Aabout%20it%20-%20_must_%20be%20based%20on%20some%20self-consistent%20definition%2C%20or%0Aelse%20rational%20discourse%20is%20impossible.%29%0Aso%2C%20from%20that%20perspective%2C%20i%20will%20simply%20say%20that%20most%20people%20who%0Aaccept%20any%20notion%20of%20a%20tolkien%20%22canon%22%20tend%20to%20reply%20most%20firmly%20on%0A_the%20lord%20of%20the%20rings_.%20books%20like%20_the%20hobbit_%2C%20_the%20adventures%20of%0Atom%20bombadil_%2C%20and%20_the%20road%20goes%20ever%20on_%20which%20he%20published%20during%0Ahis%20lifetime%20tend%20to%20be%20assigned%20weight%20either%20equal%20to%20lotr%20or%20only%0Aslightly%20less.%20beyond%20that%2C%20things%20get%20murky.%20but%20at%20least%20that%0Aanswers%20your%20question...%20i%20hope.%20%3A%29%0Asteuard%20jensen%0A
quoth%20graham%20lockwood%0A%3Cgondhiratc%2Ah%2Ao%2Ak%2Al%2Ai%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20in%20article%0A%3Cbb4db9a3.aa05%25gondhiratc%2Ah%2Ao%2Ak%2Al%2Ai%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%3A%0A%5Binsert%20extremely%20short%2C%20mild%20chuckle%20here.%5D%0A%5Bpause.%5D%0A%5Binsert%20brief%20yawn.%5D%0A%3A%29%0A%5Bokay%2C%20i%27m%20not%20willing%20to%20try%20to%20spoiler-proof%20my%20comments%20about%20the%0Abook%20or%20six-month-old%20movie%20in%20a%20detailed%20discussion%20here%2C%20so%20you%27ve%0Abeen%20warned.%20%3A%29%20%5D%0Ayou%20know%2C%20now%20that%20i%20think%20of%20it%2C%20i%20think%20you%27re%20completely%20right.%20in%0Athe%20book%2C%20aragorn%20certainly%20saw%20that%20he%20_could_%20be%20attracted%20to%20the%0Aeowyn%2C%20but%20he%20was%20of%20course%20thoroughly%20attached%20to%20arwen%20and%0Apresumably%20didn%27t%20give%20serious%20consideration%20to%20dumping%20her%20in%20favor%0Aof%20someone%20else.%20still%2C%20he%20felt%20pretty%20bad%20rejecting%20her%20advances.%0Ain%20the%20movie%2C%20aragorn%20was%20downright%20flirting%20with%20eowyn%20and%20no%20longer%0Ahad%20arwen%20to%20be%20faithful%20to%2C%20but%20still%20seemed%20far%20too%20attached%20to%20her%0Aemotionally%20to%20seriously%20move%20on.%20so%20yeah%2C%20the%20romance%20was%20far%20less%0Aone-sided%20in%20the%20movie%2C%20though%20it%20didn%27t%20lead%20to%20any%20real%20difference%0Ain%20any%20characters%27%20behavior.%20that%27s%20bound%20to%20change%20in%20the%20final%0Ainstallment%2C%20though%2C%20where%20aragorn%27s%20current%20non-book%20reasons%20for%20not%0Areaching%20out%20to%20eowyn%20will%20undoubtedly%20be%20wrenched%20violently%20into%20his%0Abook%20reasons.%20%3A%29%20and%20that%2C%20of%20course%2C%20will%20provide%20a%20very%20clear%20and%0Adirect%20motivation%20for%20eowyn%27s%20dispair...%20at%20the%20cost%20of%20making%20it%20seem%0Aa%20bit%20more%20aragorn%27s%20fault%20%28in%20the%20book%2C%20he%20was%20blameless%2C%20never%0Ahaving%20encouraged%20her%20at%20all%29.%0Asteuard%20jensen%0A
quoth%20henry%20hanna%20%3Cuse-author-address-header%40%5B127.1%5D%3E%20in%20article%0A%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%3A%0A%5Bcomments%20on%20romantic%20bits%20in%20the%20books%20snipped.%5D%0Ayou%27re%20welcome.%20%3A%29%0Awhy%3F%20some%20of%20shakespeare%20is%20pretty%20blah.%20and%20a%20person%20who%20can%0Aactually%20read%20leviticus%20or%20numbers%20without%20dozing%20off%20can%20read%0Aanything.%20%3A%29%20on%20the%20other%20hand%2C%20there%20have%20been%20a%20great%20many%20excellent%0Abooks%20written%20in%20the%20past%20century%2C%20and%20_the%20lord%20of%20the%20rings_%20is%0Aalmost%20certainly%20one%20of%20them.%20%28i%20don%27t%20think%20it%27s%20any%20less%20respected%0Aas%20%22fine%20literature%22%20than%20shakespeare%27s%20works%20were%20in%20his%20day%2C%20if%20i%0Arecall%20correctly%2C%20and%20it%27s%20at%20least%20as%20popular.%29%20in%20any%20case%2C%20i%27ve%0Afound%20that%20reading%20just%20one%20sort%20of%20literature%20at%20a%20time%20can%20start%20to%0Awear%20you%20down%3B%20for%20me%2C%20it%20really%20helps%20to%20alternate%20between%20serious%0Anovels%2C%20history%2C%20fantasy%2C%20science%20essays%2C%20and%20so%20forth.%20your%20milege%0Amay%20vary%2C%20of%20course.%20%3A%29%0Ahmm.%20coming%20from%20someone%20who%20hasn%27t%20actually%20_read_%20%22the%20ring%20books%22%2C%0Ai%20don%27t%20know%20that%20i%27ll%20put%20much%20stock%20in%20your%20opinion%20for%20now.%20%3A%29%0Asteuard%20jensen%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3CdLWOa.3$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AOh%2C%20I%20assumed%20there%20was%20a%20connection%20%2F%20deception%20going%20on%20but%20did%20not%0Aparticularly%20care.%20%20Advertising%20is%20often%20deceptive%20and%20it%20isn%27t%20the%0Afirst%20time%20THAT%20sort%20of%20stunt%20has%20been%20pulled%20either.%20%20I%27m%20not%0Ainclined%20to%20look%20up%20the%20works%20of...%20ermmm...%20whatever%20his%20name%20was...%0Aso%20it%20doesn%27t%20much%20matter%20to%20me%20one%20way%20or%20the%20other.%20%20Live%20and%20let%0Alive%20and%20all%20that.%0A%0A%0AOh.%20%20Well%20that%27s%20different%20then.%0A%0A%22Burn%20her%21%22%20%20:%29%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3CuaBOa.103$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0ASomething%20like%20%27established%27%2C%20%27finalized%27%2C%20%27consistent%27...%20maybe%20throw%0Ain%20a%20%27most%27%20to%20indicate%20that%20even%20these%20are%20subjective%20measures.%0AStill%2C%20different%20people%20use%20each%20of%20those%20terms%20%28AND%20%27trustworthy%27%29%20in%0Adefining%20%27canon%27...%20the%20difference%20in%20what%20we%20consider%20important%20is%0Apart%20of%20the%20difference%20in%20what%20we%20consider%20%27canon%27.%20%20Some%20prefer%20a%0Atext%20be%20%27finalized%27%20and%20others%20that%20it%20be%20%27trustworthy%27%20%28presumably%20in%0Acomparison%20to%20other%20texts%29.%20%20Thus%20there%20is%20no%20way%20to%20%27clarify%20what%20we%0Amean%20by%20canon%27%20in%20just%20a%20few%20words.%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%29%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%3Cx31Ma.19$41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0APossibly%2C%20but%20I%27ve%20always%20taken%20the%20text%20to%20be%20speaking%20of%20the%0Aspecific%20Elves%20who%20were%20dragging%20Thorin.%20%20THOSE%20elves%20were%20doing%20so%0Abecause%20%3Ethey%3C%20did%20not%20like%20dwarves.%20%20THOSE%20elves%20did%20not%20like%20dwarves%0Abecause%20%3Ethey%3C%20had%20fought%20wars%20with%20them.%20%20Not%20%27their%20people%27%20or%0A%27their%20ancestors%27%20or%20%27the%20ancestors%20of%20the%20people%20who%20now%20ruled%20their%0Akingdom%27...%20those%20particular%20elves.%0A%0A%0AHmmm...%20well%2C%20Thranduil%20was%20described%20as%20the%20greatest%20elven%20king%0Aliving%20at%20that%20time.%20%20His%20palace%20was%20apparently%20well%20appointed%20and%0Asupplied%2C%20so%20I%27d%20generally%20assumed%20that%20he%20had%20a%20fair%20bit%20of%20coin%0Aabout.%0A%0A%0AWell%2C%20there%20we%20get%20back%20into%20%27story%20external%27.%20%20The%20idea%20of%20%27seven%0Ahouses%27%20was%20a%20post%20%27The%20Hobbit%27%20development%20and%20thus%20could%20not%20have%0Abeen%20included%20in%20that%20book.%0A%0AIn%20Silm%20the%20Dwarves%20of%20Belegost%20and%20Nogrod%20know%20of%20trouble%20in%20the%20East%0Abefore%20the%20Elves%20do...%20the%20bit%20about%20%27your%20lesser%20kindred%20are%20fleeing%0Ato%20the%20hills%27.%20%20That%20indicates%20they%20had%20information%20about%20elves%20in%20the%0Aeast%2C%20and%20they%20were%20also%20said%20to%20have%20fought%20%27wars%27%20with%20Elves%20prior%0Ato%20Doriath.%20%20As%20such%20they%20might%20have%20been%20the%20Dwarves%20in%20question.%0A%0A%0AAck...%20yes.%20%20Sorry%2C%20I%20thought%20the%20discussion%20was%20over%20whether%20to%0Aaccept%20the%20given%20explanation%20or%20seek%20a%20more%20complete%20one%3B%0A%0A%22Even%20so%20it%20%5BThe%20Hobbit%5D%20could%20really%20stand%20quite%20apart%20%5Bfrom%20the%0Amythology%5D%2C%20except%20for%20references%20%28unnecessary%2C%20though%20they%20give%20an%0Aimpression%20of%20historical%20depth%29%20to%20the%20Fall%20of%20Gondolin%20...%3B%20the%0Abranches%20of%20the%20Elfkin%20...%2C%20and%20the%20quarrel%20of%20King%20Thingol%2C%20Luthien%27s%0Afather%2C%20with%20the%20Dwarves....%22%0ALetters%20%23257%0A%0AThere%20is%20another%20reference%20in%20letters%2C%20but%20I%20can%27t%20dig%20it%20out%20of%0AGoogle%20and%20don%27t%20have%20the%20book%20at%20hand.%20%20In%20any%20case%2C%20the%20reference%20to%0AThingol%27s%20feud%20with%20the%20Dwarves%20that%20Tolkien%20writes%20of%20here%20can%20only%0Abe%20the%20passage%20in%20question.%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20%28Steuard%20Jensen%29%20wrote%20in%20news:NE_Na.79%0A$41nospam@nospam.net:%0A%0A%0AVery%20interesting%21%20Now%20I%20at%20least%20have%20some%20recommendation.%20I%20will%20let%0Ayou%20know%20if%20the%20script%20recommended%20me%20the%20right%20thing%20after%20I%20have%20read%0Aall%20those%20books%20in%20that%20order%20:-%29%0A%0AIf%20you%20are%20interested%2C%20here%20is%20the%20order%20that%20I%20got%20for%20myself%20from%20the%0Ascript:%0A-------%0ARecommended%20Reading%20Order%20for%20Books%20about%20Middle-earth%0ABooks%20in%20the%20%22History%20of%20Middle-earth%22%20series%20are%20labeled%20by%20series%0Aorder:%20%5BHoMe%20N%5D%20is%20the%20Nth%20book%20in%20the%20series.%0A%0A%20%20%201.%20The%20Hobbit%0A%20%20%202.%20The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings%20%28%22LotR%22%29%20%28often%20published%20in%20three%20volumes:%0AThe%20Fellowship%20of%20the%20Ring%2C%20The%20Two%20Towers%2C%20and%20The%20Return%20of%20the%20King%29%0A%20%20%203.%20The%20Appendices%20and%20Prologue%20of%20The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings%0A%20%20%204.%20Unfinished%20Tales%0A%20%20%205.%20The%20Silmarillion%0A%20%20%206.%20The%20Adventures%20of%20Tom%20Bombadil%20%28Often%20most%20easily%20found%20as%20part%20of%0AThe%20Tolkien%20Reader%20%28USA%29%20or%20Tales%20from%20the%20Perilous%20Realm%0A%28Commonwealth%29%2C%20which%20both%20also%20contain%20quite%20a%20few%20of%20Tolkien%27s%0Awritings%20not%20related%20to%20Middle-earth.%29%0A%20%20%207.%20The%20Letters%20of%20J.R.R.%20Tolkien%20%28ed.%20Humphrey%20Carpenter%29%0A%20%20%208.%20The%20Book%20of%20Lost%20Tales%2C%20Parts%20I-II%20%28HoMe%20I-II%29%0A%20%20%209.%20Morgoth%27s%20Ring%20and%20The%20War%20of%20the%20Jewels%20%28HoMe%20X-XI%29%20%28%22The%20Later%0ASilmarillion%22%29%0A%20%2010.%20The%20Peoples%20of%20Middle-earth%20%28HoMe%20XII%29%0A%20%2011.%20Sauron%20Defeated%20%28HoMe%20IX%29%20%28second%20half:%20%22The%20Notion%20Club%20Papers%22%0Aand%20%22The%20Drowning%20of%20Anad%FBn%EA%22%29%0A%20%2012.%20The%20Lost%20Road%20%28HoMe%20V%29%0A%20%2013.%20Pictures%20by%20J.R.R.%20Tolkien%20and%20J.R.R.%20Tolkien:%20Artist%20and%0AIllustrator%20%28the%20latter%20edited%20by%20Wayne%20G.%20Hammond%20and%20Christina%20Scull%29%0A%20%2014.%20Tolkien:%20The%20Authorized%20Biography%20%28by%20Humphrey%20Carpenter%29%0A%20%2015.%20%22On%20Fairy%20Stories%22%2C%20published%20in%20Tree%20and%20Leaf%20%28Often%20most%20easily%0Afound%20as%20part%20of%20The%20Tolkien%20Reader%20%28USA%29%2C%20which%20also%20contains%20%22The%0AAdventures%20of%20Tom%20Bombadil%22%2C%20or%20The%20Monsters%20and%20the%20Critics%20and%20Other%0AEssays%20%28Commonwealth%29%2C%20both%20of%20which%20also%20contain%20a%20number%20of%20Tolkien%27s%0Awritings%20not%20related%20to%20Middle-earth.%29%0A%20%2016.%20The%20Shaping%20of%20Middle-earth%20%28HoMe%20IV%29%0A%20%2017.%20The%20History%20of%20The%20Lord%20of%20the%20Rings%20%28HoMe%20VI-IX%29%20%28usually%0Apublished%20in%20four%20volumes:%20The%20Return%20of%20the%20Shadow%2C%20The%20Treason%20of%0AIsengard%2C%20The%20War%20of%20the%20Ring%2C%20and%20either%20the%20first%20half%20of%20Sauron%0ADefeated%20or%20the%20separate%20volume%20The%20End%20of%20the%20Third%20Age%29%0A%20%2018.%20The%20Lays%20of%20Beleriand%20%28HoMe%20III%29%0A%20%2019.%20%22Osanwe-kenta:%20%60Enquiry%20into%20the%20Communication%20of%20Thought%27%22%0A%28Published%20in%20the%20Tolkien%20linguistics%20journal%20Vinyar%20Tengwar%20%2339%20%28July%0A1998%29%2C%20which%20is%20available%20for%20$2%20at%20the%20Elvish%20Linguistic%20Fellowship%0Awebsite%29%0A----------%0A%0AThanks%21%0Ak%2A%0A%0A%0A
since%20they%20knew%20holding%20onto%20it%20was%20destroying%20elven%20unity%20and%20dooming%20the%0Abatle%20against%20morgoth%2C%20never%20mind%20their%20own%20peace%20and%20security%2C%20why%20the%20hell%0Adidn%27t%20dior%20or%20elwing%20or%20whoever%20else%20had%20the%20silmaril%20just%20give%20it%20back%20to%0Athe%20sons%20of%20feanor%3F%0A%28it%20would%20have%20burnt%20them%20up%2C%20and%20good%20ridance.%29%0Atsar%20parmathule%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20said:%0A%7Bsnip%7D%0A%0A....%22I%20know%20who%20it%20is%20you%20hunt.%20His%20comings%20and%20goings%20have%20been%20as%20an%20echo%0Aof%20fear%20echoing%20down%20the%20canyon%20walls.%0AHALLO-HALLO-hallo-hallo-allo-llo-lo-o-o-o%21%22%0A%0AGerard%20merely%20stared%20at%20the%20big%20oaf%2C%20dumbfounded.%20With%20hope%20in%20his%20eye%2C%20he%0Aturned%20to%20Mesmerelda%2C%20reached%20into%20his%20pocket%2C%20and%20quickly%20pulled%20out%20a%0Abottle%20of%20Visine%20which%20he%20promptly%20cleaned%20all%20hope%20from%20his%20eyes.%20Hopeless%2C%0Anow%2C%20he%20looked%20back%20to%20Mesmerelda%20and%20asked%2C%20%22Do%20you%20know%20who%20he%20is%3F%22%0A%0A%22Oh%2C%20he%27s%20one%20of%20dem%20Taixus%20Ranger%20folk%20I%20wuz%20talkin%27%20%27bout.%20Don%27t%20know%20his%0Aname%2C%20though.%22%0A%0A%22My%20real%20name%20is%20not%20important%2C%22%20interrupted%20the%20stranger%20again.%20%22But%20I%20walk%0Awith%20great%20strides%20and%20so%20around%20these%20parts%2C%20I%20am%20known%20as%20Walker%2C%20Taixus%0ARanger.%22%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20said:%0A%0AErr...%20she%20did%3F%20OK%2C%20well%2C%20haven%27t%20seen%20the%20theatrical%20version%20but%20once%20in%0Atheaters%20so%20my%20memory%20could%20be%20wrong.%20I%20know%20the%20rest%20of%20the%20gift-giving%20was%0Anot%20in%20the%20theatrical%20version%20%28was%20it%3F%21%3F%21%29%20so%20that%20may%20have%20clouded%20my%0Athinking.%20Thanks%20for%20straightening%20that%20out%2C%20though.%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
41nospam@nospam.net%20wrote:%0A%0AI%20can%20agree%20with%20that.%20I%20was%20merely%20pointing%20out%20a%20flaw%20in%20the%20argument.%0A%0A%0A--%0AKristian%20Damm%20Jensen%20%20%20%20%7C%20If%20you%20can%27t%20take%20the%20trouble%20to%0Adamm%20%28at%29%20ofir%20%28dot%29%20dk%20%7C%20make%20your%20posting%20readable%2C%20I%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%20can%27t%20take%20the%20trouble%20to%20read%20it.%0A%0A%0A%0A
teepee%20said:%0A%0AGlamdring%20was%20the%20sword%20of%20Turgon%20and%20was%20forged%20in%20Gondolin%20%22for%20the%20Goblin%0Awars%22.%20Anduril%20was%20originaly%20Narsil%20and%20was%20forged%20by%20the%20Dwarf%20Telchar.%0AWhether%20this%20makes%20them%20somehow%20%22lesser%22%20than%20a%20sword%20of%20Feanor%20is%20anyone%27s%0Aguess%20but%20I%20doubt%20it.%0A%0AI%20don%27t%20think%20we%20ever%20learn%20what%20happened%20to%20any%20of%20Feanor%27s%20swords%20but%20I%0Adon%27t%20think%20any%20of%20them%20made%20it%20into%20the%20Third%20Age%20except%2C%20perhaps%2C%20as%0ABad-Guy-Loot%20like%20Glamdring%2C%20Orcrist%2C%20and%20Sting%20were.%20They%20just%20happened%20to%0Abe%20recovered%20by%20Thorin%20&%20Co.%0A%0AAll%20the%20First%20Age%20artifacts%20surviving%20into%20the%20Third%20Age%20that%20I%20know%20of%0A%28with%20the%20exception%20of%20the%20Troll%20Hoard%29%20were%20held%20by%20the%20heirs%20of%20the%0Aoriginal%20First%20Age%20owners%20and%20Feanor%20doesn%27t%20seem%20to%20have%20had%20any%20heirs%20left%0Aby%20that%20time.%20The%20Feanorians%20didn%27t%20do%20too%20well%20in%20the%20long%20run...%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%22The%20narrative%20ends%20here.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20There%20is%20no%20reason%20to%20think%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%7C%2F%2F%0A%28%2F%20%2F%2F%20%20%20%20that%20any%20more%20was%20ever%20written.%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7C%2F%2F%0A%7C%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20The%20manuscript%2C%20which%20becomes%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%0A%7C%2F%2F%20%20%20%20increasingly%20rapid%20towards%20the%20end%2C%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%0A%28%2F%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20peters%20out%20in%20a%20scrawl.%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%2F%2F%7C%7C%0A%7C%7C%20%20%20%20%20-Christopher%20Tolkien%2C%20_The%20Lost%20Road_%20%20%2F%2F%20%7C%7C%0A%0A%0A%0A%0A
the%20american%20wrote%3A%0Ahe%20wouldn%27t%20need%20to.%20wouldn%27t%20he%20still%20have%20innate%20common%20interests%0Awith%20the%20dwarves%3F%0Awhy%3F%20it%20was%20clear%20even%20up%20to%20the%20very%20end%20of%20the%20rings%2C%20that%20the%0Adwarves%20were%20still%20consumed%20by%20the%20seven.%20who%20knows%20what%20knowledge%0Athese%20secretive%20creatures%20did%20or%20didn%27t%20have%3F%0Asauron%20sure%20didn%27t%20think%20so%2C%20when%20he%20sent%20an%20emissary%20to%20seek%20their%20aid%0Ain%20recovering%20the%20one.%20could%20not%20saruman%2C%20had%20he%20the%20prescience%20to%0Aalign%20himself%20with%20the%20dwarves%2C%20have%20gained%20some%20knowledge%20he%20was%20devoid%0Aof%20the%20way%20things%20turned%20out%3F%0Ame%20too.%20%3C----%20does%20that%20make%20this%20a%20%22me%20too%22%20post%3F%0A
the%20softrat%20%41nospam@nospam.net%3E%20wrote%20in%20message%20news:%41nospam@nospam.net%3E...%0A%0A%0AAs%20others%20have%20noted%2C%20the%20Elves%20developed%20speech%20on%20their%20own.%0AValarin%20pre-dated%20any%20other%20language%20in%20Middle-Earth%2C%20but%20overall%20it%0Ahad%20minimal%20influence%20on%20the%20others%20because%20it%20was%20an%20extremely%0Adifficult%20and%20even%20%27unpleasant%27%20language%20for%20any%20but%20the%20Ainur%20to%0Aspeak.%20%20The%20exceptions%20would%20be%20Khuzdul%2C%20and%20possibly%20Black%20Speech%0Aand%2For%20Iglishmek.%20%20From%20the%20texts%20I%20believe%20that%20Iglishmek%20was%20most%0Alikely%20developed%20by%20the%20Dwarves%20largely%20independant%20of%20any%20Valarin%20%28or%0Aeven%20Elven%29%20influence%2C%20but%20it%20is%20possible%20that%20it%20was%20partly%20inspired%0Aby%20elven%20hand%20signs%20or%20even%20originally%20developed%20by%20Aule.%20%20Since%0AKhuzdul%20and%20Black%20Speech%20were%20%27invented%27%20languages%2C%20each%20developed%20by%0Aan%20Ainu%20%28Aule%20and%20Sauron%20respectively%29%2C%20it%20would%20make%20sense%20that%20they%0Amight%20include%20Valarin%20influences.%20%20From%20those%20two%20languages%20Valarin%0Amight%20also%20have%20then%20influenced%20human%20and%20Moriquendi%20tongues%20to%20a%0Alimited%20extent.%20%20The%20Calaquendi%20also%20picked%20up%20some%20terms%20influenced%0Aby%20Valarin%20and%20carried%20these%20back%20to%20Middle-Earth.%0A%0AThe%20real%20%27root%27%20language%20of%20Middle-Earth%20was%20the%20earliest%20form%20of%0Aelven%20speech%20%28%27Common%20Eldarin%27%29%20developed%20around%20the%20waters%20of%0ACuivienen.%20%20Every%20language%20except%20Valarin%20and%20the%20three%20listed%20above%0Awas%20heavily%20influenced%20by%20this%20tongue%20or%20one%20of%20its%20descendants.%0AHuman%20%28and%20Orcish%29%20languages%20evolved%20quickly%20enough%20and%20included%0Asufficient%20invention%20and%20alteration%20that%20these%20elven%20influences%20might%0Aeventually%20be%20obscured%2C%20but%20%27Common%20Eldarin%27%20definitely%20would%20stand%20at%0Athe%20top%20of%20almost%20every%20%27linguistic%20tree%27%20in%20Middle-Earth.%0A%0A%0A
well%2C%20in%20my%20quick%20off-the%20cuff%20comment%2C%20i%20don%27t%20think%20i%20stated%20that%20i%0Athought%20%22peter%20jackson%20is%20a%20jerk%21%22%20although%20i%20understand%20that%20this%20has%0Abeen%20the%20reaction%20of%20some.%20but%20i%20do%20think%20that%20he%20didn%27t%20truly%20understand%0Athe%20books.%20watching%20the%20interviews%20with%20him%2C%20both%20sets%2C%20for%20each%20movie%2C%20he%0Aand%20the%20main%20actors%20in%20the%20film%20seem%20completely%20unaware%20of%20tolkein%27s%20very%0Acatholic%20worldview%2C%20and%20absolutely%20unaware%20of%20tolkein%27s%20deliberate%20inclusion%0Aof%20catholic%20themes%20and%20symbolism.%20they%20seem%20to%20be%20treating%20the%20ideas%20in%20the%0Abook%20as%20half%20action-adventure%20%2F%20half%20new-age-style%20mythology.%20john%20rhys%0Adavies%20interview%20was%20most%20indicative%20of%20this.%20so%2C%20yes%2C%20i%20do%20believe%20that%0Ajackson%20did%20not%20understand%20tolkein%2C%20and%20missed%20many%20of%20the%20core%20messages%20of%0Athe%20books.%20he%20does%20well%20on%20the%20surface%2C%20but%20hasn%27t%20even%20begun%20to%20plumb%20the%0Adepths.%20he%20loses%20a%20lot%2C%20and%20thus%2C%20so%20do%20we%20all.%20still%2C%20it%20is%20a%20very%20good%0Awork%20of%20film.%0Ai%20do%20take%20exception%2C%20a%20bit%2C%20to%20your%20description%20of%20faramir%20and%20his%20interlude%0Awith%20frodo%2C%20sam%2C%20and%20golum%20as%20a%20%22tea%20break%22%20as%20written%20it%20worked%20well%0Aeven%20for%20a%20clueless%20audiance%20who%20is%20geared%20more%20for%20visual%20special%20effects%2C%0Athan%20for%20finding%20deep%20meaning%20in%20a%20story...%20there%27s%20a%20battle%2C%20a%20capture%20with%0Athe%20hobbits%20scared%20out%20of%20their%20minds%2C%20golum%20is%20nearly%20killed%2C%20faramir%20finds%0Aout%20about%20the%20ring%2C%20and%20teeters%20on%20the%20cusp%20didn%27t%20need%20an%20extra%20nazgul%0Abattle.%20but%20yes%2C%20since%20it%20just%20ended%20right%20there%2C%20w%2Fo%20any%20of%20the%20further%0A%22excitements%2C%20i%20can%20see%20where%20pj%20needed%20to%20entertain%20his%20audience.%20but%20he%0Adidn%27t%20need%20to%20make%20faramir%20or%20tr
